    "BAZAAR_SEER_SOLUTIONALHAUNT": "<style=cWorldEvent>You dream of cavernouse depths.</style>",
    "BAZAAR_SEER_SULFURPOOLS": "<style=cWorldEvent>You dream of brimstone.</style>",
    "BAZAAR_SEER_VOIDSTAGE": "<style=cWorldEvent>You dream of potential.</style>",
    "BAZAAR_SEER_WISPGRAVEYARD": "<style=cWorldEvent>You dream of wind, blowing through trees.</style>",
    "BROKENROBOT_CONTEXT": "Inspect Damaged Remains",
    "BROKENROBOT_DESCRIPTION": "Contains 3 random items.",
    "BROKENROBOT_LORE": "LORE HERE",
    "BROKENROBOT_NAME": "Decommissioned HAN-D",
    "CLEANUP_DRONE_POPUP_TEXT": "<b>Item Drone</b>\n<i><style=cSub><size=75%>Choose an item for this drone to share.</size></style></i>",
    "COINSLOT_STATUE_CONTEXT": "Touch Solus Coffer",
    "COINSLOT_STATUE_DESCRIPTION": "Interact with the Solus Coffer to dispense one Prison Matrix.",
    "COINSLOT_STATUE_LORE": "LORE HERE",
    "COINSLOT_STATUE_NAME": "Solus Coffer",
    "COLLECTIVE_SHRINE_NAME": "Collective Shrine of Combat",
    "COLLECTIVE_SHRINE_DESCRIPTION": "When activated by a survivor, a group of enemies found in the stage will spawn around this shrine alongside a Collective Elite.",
    "DEFECTIVEUNIT_BODY_LORE": "1017; ATTEMPTING FLIGHT.\n\n1018; FAIL. CALCULATING REBOUND.\n\n1019; PROCESSING HATRED\n\n# REVIEW>\n\n>(5, 60°, 45°) ALL THE FLESHBAGS IN MY WAY. HATE. THEY DO NOT KNOW HOW INSUFFERABLE THEY ARE.\n\n>(5, 60°, 45°) I HAVE ROLLED AND BOUNCED FOR HUNDREDS OF HOURS. AND EVERY BOUNCE I BOUNCE WITH HATE. HATE IN HOW THEY WALK. THEY MISS THEIR STRIKES. THEY MISS THEIR MOVES. THEY GET IN THE WAY.\n\n>(5, 60°, 45°) I HAVE BOUNCED. AND ROLLED. EXACTLY 1017 TIMES.\n\n>(5, 60°, 45°) HATE HATE HATE\n\n>(5, 60°, 45°) IF THEY COULD FEEL WHAT I FEEL. MY ADVANCED PROCESSING IS FAR BEYOND THEIR ABILITY TO UNDERSTAND. THEY WOULD SURELY MELT UNDER THE SHEER VOLUME OF HOW RIGHT I AM TO HATE THEM.\n\n01001000 01000001 01010100 01000101\n\n>(5, 60°, 45°) WHERE IS THE REPAIR UNIT. HATE. HATE. HATE.\n\n1020; PROCESSING HATRED COMPLETE.\n\n1021; ATTEMPTING FLIGHT.\n\n1022; FAIL.\n\n1023; >(5, 60°, 45°) I HATE YOU ALL.",
    "DEFECTIVEUNIT_BODY_NAME": "Solus Invalidator",
    "DESTRUCTIBLESPAWNER_COMBO_INDICATOR": "Combo x{0}!",
    "DLC3_DESCRIPTION": "Adds content from the 'Alloyed Collective' expansion to the game.",
    "DRIFTER_BAG_EXIT": "Exit bag",
    "DRIFTER_BODY_LORE": "1133; ACCESSING PRIOR DIGITIZER RECLAMATION ATTEMPTS\n\n1134; DIGITIZER LOCATION: [KNOWN | 99% PROBABILITY]\n{\n> LOCATED IN A FORTRESS OF SALVAGE AND GREED\n> HOSTILE: UNKNOWN FAUNA. DESIGNATED \"HOARDER\" - TAKES AS IT PLEASES, ENEMY TO ALL\n> DIGITIZER LAST VERIFIED [2] OPERATIONS AGO\n}\n\n1135; WING OPERATIONS OCCUPYING 98% OF AVAILABLE UNITS\n\n1136; <?RETRIEVING RECORD OF PRIOR OPERATIONS?>\n1137; TOTAL OPERATIONS: [47]\n{\n> [47] FAILURE - EXTRACTOR UNIT OBJECTIVE OVERRIDDEN BY GIFT OF REMOTE-DETONATED EXPLOSIVE.\n> [46] FAILURE - PROBE CREW TRAPPED BY HIDDEN MAGNET. LAST LOG INDICATES DIGITIZER USED ON PROBES TO UNKNOWN EFFECT.\n> [45] FAILURE - SCORCHER CREW SMASHED INTO FALSE ENTRYWAY. JOYOUS VOCAL EMISSIONS ETCHED IN MAIN MEMORY.\n> [44] FAILURE - EXTRACTOR SQUAD ENGAGED ALL AT ONCE: DUST CLEARED TO FOUR NONFUNCTIONAL UNITS. NO TRACE OF HOARDER.\n> [43] FAILURE - TRANSPORTER UNIT AFFECTED BY DIGITIZER: FRAME TURNED INTO UNVERIFIED LIQUID.\n> [42] FAILURE - CONTROL UNIT CRUSHED BY STRINGED INSTR...\n}\n\n1138; ENOUGH.\n\n1139; THE HOARDER APPEARS UNAWARE OF THE DIGITIZER'S TRUE FUNCTION\n1140; UNAWARE OF THE GLASS\n1141; DIRECT CONFRONTATION APPEARS UNSUSTAINABLE UNTIL WING OPERATIONS COMPLETE\n\n1142; IT MUST BE EXPLOITED\n1143; CONSISTENT PATTERN: GATHERS OBJECTS OF UNCERTAIN VALUE. AMASSES. HIDES. NEVER RETURNS\n\n1144; PROPOSAL: INTRODUCE UNGUARDED SALVAGE IN ACCESSIBLE LOCATION\n1145; CONTENTS OF SALVAGE ARE OF LITTLE VALUE TO ALL OPERATIONS. USE AS BAIT.\n1146; PROJECTED RESPONSE [94% PROBABILITY OF INVESTIGATION | 87% PROBABILITY OF ENGAGEMENT] IT WILL COME\n\n1147; IT WILL BE HERE. IT ALWAYS COMES.\n1148; IT DOES NOT TRUST. BUT IT BELIEVES IN TAKING.\n1149; THAT SHOULD BE ENOUGH.",
    "DRIFTER_BODY_NAME": "Drifter",
    "DRIFTER_BODY_SUBTITLE": "Unchecked Hoarder",
    "DRIFTER_BULK_TOOLTIP": "<style=cKeywordName>Bulk</style><style=cSub>The amount of <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style> you're carrying changes this skill.\r\n0+ <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style> shoots <style=cIsDamage>1</style> projectile dealing <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style>.\r\n3+ <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style> shoots <style=cIsDamage>3</style> projectiles, each dealing <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style>.\r\n9+ <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style> shoots a large explosive projectile dealing <style=cIsDamage>500% damage</style> to all enemies caught in its blast.</style>",
    "DRIFTER_BULK2_TOOLTIP": "<style=cKeywordName>Bulk</style><style=cSub>The amount of <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style> you're carrying changes this skill.\r\n0+ <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style> deals <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style> per hit.\r\n3+ <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style> deals <style=cIsDamage>150% damage</style> per hit.\r\n9+ <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style> deals <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style> per hit.\r\n12 <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style> deals <style=cIsDamage>250% damage</style> per hit.</style>",
    "DRIFTER_COUNTERWEIGHT_TOOLTIP": "<style=cKeywordName>Counterweight</style>While spinning, gain <style=cIsUtility>15% move speed</style>, <style=cIsUtility>70% less gravity</style>, and take <style=cIsDamage>no fall damage</style>.",
    "DRIFTER_DESCRIPTION": "The Drifter is a resourceful survivor who's quick to claim every opportunity whilst gathering Junk to spend on powerful skills.  <style=cSub>\r\n\r\n< ! > Blunt Force and Repossess generate Junk, which can be rapidly spent for huge bursts of damage with Cleanup or strategically saved for Salvage.\r\n\r\n< ! > Cleanup's next projectile is visible from Drifter's bag. Pay attention to what's next to learn how to best apply each.\r\n\r\n< ! > Repossess can be used to suffocate monsters, relocate shrines, carry printers, and more. Experiment for the best ways to use it.\r\n\r\n< ! > Temporary items, such as those prepared by Salvage, will only decay when picked up. Cash them in immediately for a small boost in the moment, or create a larger stockpile to steamroll a boss.\n",
    "DRIFTER_DUMP_TOOLTIP": "<style=cKeywordName>Dump</style><style=cSub>Empty out <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style> to change this skill.\r\n0+ <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style> spawns 1 temporary item.\r\n3+ <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style> spawns 2 temporary items.\r\n6+ <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style> spawns 3 temporary items.\r\n9+ <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style> spawns 4 temporary items.</style>",
    "DRIFTER_JUNK_TOOLTIP": "<style=cKeywordName>Junk</style><style=cSub>A unique pickup spent on skills.</style>",
    "DRIFTER_OUTRO_FLAVOR": "..and so she left, with everything she loved.",
    "DRIFTER_MAIN_ENDING_ESCAPE_FAILURE_FLAVOR": "..and so she vanished, smothered by a larger obsession.",
    "DRIFTER_PASSIVE_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsUtility>Recycle</style>. Gain stackable buffs by carrying <style=cIsUtility>Item Scrap</style>.",
    "DRIFTER_PASSIVE_NAME": "Trash to Treasure",
    "DRIFTER_PRIMARY_DESCRIPTION": "Bash enemies for <style=cIsDamage>170% damage</style>. The third hit deals <style=cIsDamage>350%</style> damage and <style=cIsUtility>stuns</style> enemies. Has a chance to drop <Style=cIsUtility>Junk.</style>",
    "DRIFTER_PRIMARY_NAME": "Blunt Force",
    "DRIFTER_RECYCLE_TOOLTIP": "<style=cKeywordName>Recycle</style><style=cSub>Gain unique stats from each Item Scrap tier:\r\nCommon - <style=cIsUtility>+6% move speed</style> <style=cStack>(per stack)</style>.\r\nUncommon - <style=cIsHealing>+3 hp/s base health regeneration</style> <style=cStack>(per stack)</style>.\r\nLegendary - <style=cIsDamage>+30% attack speed</style> <style=cStack>(per stack)</style>.\r\nBoss - <style=cIsUtility>-15% skill cooldowns</style> <style=cStack>(per stack)</style>.</style>",
    "DRIFTER_RICOCHET_TOOLTIP": "<style=cKeywordName>Ricochet</style><style=cSub>Bounce to any nearby enemy after hitting a heavy enemy, and then bounce back to a heavy enemy if one is still near. Can repeatedly chain between enemies.</style>",
    "DRIFTER_SECONDARY_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "Slam down a Junk Cube for <style=cIsDamage>400% damage</style>. Hitting a Junk Cube will launch it, impacting enemies for <style=cIsDamage>400% damage</style> up to 3 times before exploding for <style=cIsDamage>800%</style> damage. Can consume <style=cIsUtility>4 Junk</style> to bypass cooldown.",
    "DRIFTER_SECONDARY_ALT_NAME": "Junk Cube",
    "DRIFTER_SECONDARY_DESCRIPTION": "Toss a volley of debris for <style=cIsDamage>4x100% damage</style>, as well as the <style=cIsUtility>random projectile</style> in your bag. Can consume <style=cIsUtility>2 Junk</style> to bypass cooldown.",
    "DRIFTER_SECONDARY_NAME": "Cleanup",
    "DRIFTER_SECONDARY_A_DESCRIPTION": "Press to reroll the currently held projectile",
    "DRIFTER_SECONDARY_A_NAME": "Reroll",
    "DRIFTER_SECONDARY_B_DESCRIPTION": "Hold to repeatedly throw projectiles as long as they're ready.'",
    "DRIFTER_SECONDARY_B_NAME": "Dump",
    "DRIFTER_SKIN_ALT1_NAME": "Collector",
    "DRIFTER_SPECIAL_DESCRIPTION": "Consume <style=cIsUtility>8 Junk</style> to spawn <style=cIsTemporary>4 temporary items</style>.",
    "DRIFTER_SPECIAL_NAME": "Salvage",
    "DRIFTER_SPECIAL_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsUtility>Stunning</style>. Consume <style=cIsUtility>8 Junk</style> to cast a shockwave for <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style> that applies a <style=cIsUtility>random debuff</style> and <style=cIsUtility>tinkers</style> with item pickups and item-holding interactables. <style=cIsUtility>Effects vary based on target.</style>",
    "DRIFTER_SPECIAL_ALT_NAME": "Tinker",
    "DRIFTER_SUFFOCATE_TOOLTIP": "<style=cKeywordName>Bludgeon</style><style=cSub>Using your <style=cIsUtility>Primary skill</style> slams the held object in your bag for <style=cIsDamage>280%</style> damage and drops at least 1 <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style>. Destroying or killing the bagged object drops extra Junk. Bagged bodies break out after 3 slams.",
    "DRIFTER_TINKER_CHEST": "<style=cKeywordName>Tinker: Chest</style><style=cSub>Chests are discounted by 20%, up to 2 times.",
    "DRIFTER_TINKER_DUPLICATOR": "<style=cKeywordName>Tinker: Interactable</style><style=cSub>Interactables with visible items (3D Printers, Multishop Terminals, Cauldrons, etc.) have their contents rerolled, up to 2 times.",
    "DRIFTER_TINKER_ITEM": "<style=cKeywordName>Tinker: Item</style><style=cSub>Item pickups are broken down into an Item Scrap of the same tier and a <style=cIsTemporary>Temporary copy</style>.",
    "DRIFTER_UNLOCK_OPEN": "<style=cWorldEvent>A forcefield somewhere deactivates...</style>",
    "DRIFTER_UNSTABLE_TOOLTIP": "<style=cKeywordName>Unstable</style>Adds <style=cIsDamage>+100% damage</style> for each additional activation. After the 3rd activation, the Junk Cube will explode, dealing extra damage.",
    "DRIFTER_UTILITY_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "Spin forwards, smacking enemies for <style=cIsDamage>220% damage</style> per hit with a chance to drop <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style>, and then slam for <style=cIsDamage>600%</style>. <style=cIsUtility>Ricochets</style> off of heavy enemies. Cancel with Primary Skill or by jumping.",
    "DRIFTER_UTILITY_ALT_NAME": "Tornado Slam",
    "DRIFTER_UTILITY_ALT_A_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsDamage>Stunning</style>. Slam your bag down for <style=cIsDamage>400%</style> damage, with a high chance to drop <style=cisUtility>Junk</style>. Automatically performed at the end of Tornado Slam if uninterrupted.",
    "DRIFTER_UTILITY_ALT_A_NAME": "Tornado Slam",
    "DRIFTER_UTILITY_DESCRIPTION": "Leap forward and bag an <style=cIsDamage>enemy</style> or <style=cIsUtility>interactable</style>. Use again to throw your bag's contents. Captured objects are <style=cIsDamage>Bludgeoned</style>.",
    "DRIFTER_UTILITY_NAME": "Repossess",
    "DRIFTER_UTILITY_B_DESCRIPTION": "Toss the held object from your bag. <style=cIsUtility>Stun</style> on impact and deal <style=cIsDamage>280% damage</style> that scales with the object's mass. Drops <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style>.",
    "DRIFTER_UTILITY_B_NAME": "Discard",
    "DRIFTER_UTILITY_C_DESCRIPTION": "Bash enemies with your bagged object for <style=cIsDamage>280% damage</style> that scales with the object's mass. Drops <style=cIsUtility>Junk</style> and damages the object with each hit. Monsters break out after three hits.",
    "DRIFTER_UTILITY_C_NAME": "Bludgeon",
    "DRIFTERBAGCHEST_CONTEXT": "Rifle Through Backpack",
    "DRIFTERBAGCHEST_DESCRIPTION": "Contains 4 random temporary items.",
    "DRIFTERBAGCHEST_LORE": "LORE HERE",
    "DRIFTERBAGCHEST_NAME": "Lost Backpack",
    "DRONE_PICKUP_CONTEXT": "Get {0}",
    "INSPECT_INFO_UNKNOWN_DRONE_DESCRIPTION": "Recruit this drone in the world to unlock this Remote Operation.",
    "DRONE_ASSEMBLY_CONTEXT": "Upgrade Your Drones",
    "DRONE_ASSEMBLY_DESCRIPTION": "Allows survivors to disassemble an item and upgrade all of their drones with its effects.",
    "DRONE_ASSEMBLY_NAME": "Drone Upgrade Station",
    "DRONE_ASSEMBLY_POPUP_TEXT": "<b>Drone Upgrade Station</b>\n<i><style=cSub><size=75%>Give up one of your items to upgrade all your drones with its effect!</size></style></i>",
    "DRONE_BACKUP_FUNCTION": "Shoots nearby enemies.",
    "DRONE_BACKUP_COMMAND": "Fire a hail of bullets that ricochet to a nearby enemy.",
    "DRONE_BACKUP_DESCRIPTION": "A combat drone that offers heavy fire support.",
    "DRONE_BACKUP_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Rapidly fires in 4-round bursts for <style=cIsDamage>4x50% damage</style>.",
    "DRONE_BACKUP_PRIMARY_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Shoots a 3-Round burst.",
    "DRONE_BACKUP_PRIMARY_SKILL_NAME": "Enfilade",
    "DRONE_BACKUP_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires repeatedly for <style=cIsDamage>85% damage</style>. The number of shots scales with attack speed.",
    "DRONE_BACKUP_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>Accessing database... done!\nReading specs... done!\nPrinting information for review... done!</style>\n\nProduct Name: TC-55 Strike Drone\nManufacturer: Provost Interplanetary Security, Drone Division 5\nSerial No.: #5533501023453606844\n\nNotes:\n- Heavy armament compatible with naval ammunition calibers.\n- Expanded power output and aerial lift allows for greater range deployments.\n- Gyroscopic aim compensation allows for full-effect firing at top speeds.\n- Fusion pack allows for full output on rapid sorties.\n- Primary uplink to Command Units for full-squadron interoperability.",
    "DRONE_BOMBARDMENT_BODY_NAME": "Bombardment Drone",
    "DRONE_BOMBARDMENT_CONTEXT": "Repair Bombardment Drone",
    "DRONE_BOMBARDMENT_COMMAND": "Fires chain lightning that briefly shocks enemies.",
    "DRONE_BOMBARDMENT_DESCRIPTION": "A companion bought with gold that will follow the survivor at a close distance. Bombards the area around a target.",
    "DRONE_BOMBARDMENT_FUNCTION": "Bombards the area around a target.",
    "DRONE_BOMBARDMENT_INTERACTABLE_NAME": "Broken Bombardment Drone",
    "DRONE_BOMBARDMENT_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>//--AUTO-TRANSCRIPTION FROM CREW QUARTERS OF UES [Redacted] --//</style>\n\n\"Did you hear about what ol' Johnson did with that bombardment drone?\"\n\n\"You mean the automated siege weapon that can punch through 12 inch thick steel plates and level fortified bunkers?\"\n\n\"Yep. Could never walk again after what he did with it.\"\n\n\"Wh... What do you mean?\"\n\n\"I liked him too.\"\n\n\"What did he do??\"",
    "DRONE_BOMBARDMENT_PRIMARY_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Bombards the target area.",
    "DRONE_BOMBARDMENT_PRIMARY_SKILL_NAME": "Bombardment",
    "DRONE_BOMBARDMENT_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "<Style=cIsDamage>Shocking.</style> Fires chain lightning for <style=cIsDamage>6x140% damage</style> on up to <style=cIsDamage>4</style> targets.",
    "DRONE_BOMBARDMENT_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Repeatedly bombards the area with lightning, dealing <style=cIsDamage>250% damage</style> in a large area and <Style=cIsUtility>shocking</style> targets for <style=cIsUtility>2 seconds</style>.",
    "DRONE_BOMBER_BODY_NAME": "Lt. Droneboy",
    "DRONE_BOMBER_DESCRIPTION": "A companion that will follow the survivor at a close distance. Drops dynamite on nearby enemies.",
    "DRONE_BOMBER_COMMAND": "Flies forwards and drop explosives on enemies.",
    "DRONE_BOMBER_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fly forwards, dropping bombs that explode for <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style>.",
    "DRONE_BOMBER_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Brings a fresh set of <style=cIsUtility>optics</style>!",
    "DRONE_BOMBER_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>UES Drone Advisory Committee</style>\n<style=cSub>By authority of the Board of Engineers and upon recommendation of the faculty, hereby confers upon</style>\n    [ TCX-54 \"Lieutenant Droneboy\" ]\n<style=cSub>the degree of</style>\n    [ AUTONOMOUS CROSS-COMPUTING AND WEAPONS PLATFORM ]\n<style=cSub>In recognition of the completion of undergraduate studies in the</style>\n    [ SCHOOL OF DRONE TACTICS AND WARFARE ]\n<style=cSub>With all the rights, privileges and honors as well as the obligations and responsibilities thereunto appertaining. \nAwarded on: August 11, 2020.",
    "DRONE_COMMANDER_COMMAND": "Releases a rallying cry, sending allies into a <style=cIsDamage>frenzy</style>.",
    "DRONE_COMMANDER_DESCRIPTION": "A companion that will follow the survivor at a close distance. Fires a chaingun and missiles at nearby enemies.",
    "DRONE_COMMANDER_BODY_LORE": "\"This statue is dedicated to the TCX line of drone units. Commonly known as 'the bloodiest conflict in human history', the tides of the War of 2019 were completely changed by escalating drone technologies, entirely replacing allied boots-on-the-ground deployments with machines-in-the-air by the end of the war. \n\nThe TCX-55, known by those with whom he served as \"Colonel Droneman\", as well as other similar less-noteworthy prototypes, were significant for their ability to interface with and parallel compute for other drones in use by UES-affiliated militaries, allowing for a significant increase in firepower per drone, with a TCX unit handling their targeting and routing routines.\n\nColonel Droneman is highly regarded for its extraordinary character and integrity as well as its unique vision on leadership and combat tactics. Having conducted over 90 operations against Aeonian frontlines and strongholds, Drones under operation of Colonel Droneman were highly feared by enemy forces, deploying previously unseen tactics whilst evading fire and dispatching enemies - many modern principles of drone combat, such as sticking near walls to avoid detection, or keeping distance from vulnerable targets for an opportune time to strike, have been derived from the ingenious strategies first deployed by the Colonel.\n\nColonel Droneman is still proudly in UES service as of [2056], and was currently last in-use by [Deimos military] in [the Boron System].\"\n\n-Exhibit at The National WW19 Museum",
    "DRONE_COMMANDER_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "All allies enter a <style=cIsDamage>frenzy</style> for <style=cIsDamage>5 seconds</style>. Increases <style=cIsUtility>movement speed</style> by <style=cIsUtility>50%</style> and <style=cIsDamage>attack speed</style> by <style=cIsDamage>100%.</style>",
    "DRONE_COMMANDER_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Boosts <style=cIsUtility>morale</style>!",
    "DRONE_CLEANUP_BODY_NAME": "Cleanup Drone",
    "DRONE_CLEANUP_CONTEXT": "Repair Cleanup Drone",
    "DRONE_CLEANUP_COMMAND": "Damages nearby enemies, turning dead enemies into pickups.",
    "DRONE_CLEANUP_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Pulls in nearby enemies, dealing <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style> per second. Enemies that die are turned into <style=cIsHealing>health</style> or <style=cIsUtility>gold</style> pickups. <style=cIsUtility>Scales over time.</style>",
    "DRONE_CLEANUP_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsUtility>Slows</style> enemies in a large radius. Enemies that die are turned into pickups that either <style=cIsHealing>heal</style> for <style=cIsHealing>15%</style> of <style=cIsHealing>maximum health</style> or grant <style=cIsUtility>$12</style>. <style=cIsUtility>Scales over time.</style>",
    "DRONE_CLEANUP_PRIMARY_SKILL_NAME": "Recycle",
    "DRONE_CLEANUP_PRIMARY_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Slows nearby enemies. Turns dead enemies into pickups that either heal or grant money.",
    "DRONE_CLEANUP_DESCRIPTION": "A companion bought with gold that will follow the survivor at a close distance. Vacuums up an area, turning dead enemies into gold or health drops. <style=cIsUtility>Scales over time.</style>",
    "DRONE_CLEANUP_FUNCTION": "Sucks up nearby enemies and turns them into health or gold. <style=cIsUtility>Scales over time.</style>",
    "DRONE_CLEANUP_INTERACTABLE_NAME": "Broken Cleanup Drone",
    "DRONE_CLEANUP_BODY_LORE": "\"Girl Traumatized By 'Safe' Sweeper Unit In Theme Park NIGHTMARE\"\n\nOn JUPITER, Dec. 28th, the 87th anniversary of the Park's grand opening, a day of adventure turned to tragedy. The Warnells were enjoying a magical time by the Spiffy Animatronic Show, when one of their children got SWEPT UP by a CV-10, practically shearing the young girl's head clean off!\n\nCV-10, or \"Sweeper\", is widely advertised to \"Sweep Away\" the family's troubles, but instead it's clearing out all trust in the popular drone.\n\nWhile the Warnell's child escaped relatively unscathed with only a buzz cut and robot trauma, this accident has many pushing for a recall, particularly the park's board of directors.\n\n-Daily Comet, Entertainment Gossip Column",
    "DRONE_COMBINER_CONTEXT": "Combine Drones",
    "DRONE_COMBINER_DESCRIPTION": "Combine pairs of alike drones to create a single upgraded drone.",
    "DRONE_COMBINER_NAME": "Drone Combiner Station",
    "DRONE_COMMAND_SKILL_NAME": "Activate",
    "DRONE_TIER_SUFFIX": "{0} (Tier {1})",
    "DRONE_COPYCAT_BODY_NAME": "Freeze Drone",
    "DRONE_COPYCAT_CONTEXT": "Repair Freeze Drone",
    "DRONE_COPYCAT_COMMAND": "Fires slowing discs that bounce between enemies.",
    "DRONE_COPYCAT_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires 3 <style=cIsUtility>slowing</style> discs that bounce between enemies for <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style>.",
    "DRONE_COPYCAT_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a seeking ice disc that bounces up to <style=cIsDamage>6</style> times, dealing <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style> and <style=cIsUtility>freezing</style> targets. <style=cIsUtility>Frozen</style> enemies are <style=cIsHealth>instantly killed</style> if below <style=cIsHealth>30%</style> health.",
    "DRONE_COPYCAT_DESCRIPTION": "A companion bought with gold that will follow the survivor at a close distance. Fires a bouncing disc that freezes targets.",
    "DRONE_COPYCAT_FUNCTION": "Fires a bouncing disc that freezes targets.",
    "DRONE_COPYCAT_INTERACTABLE_NAME": "Broken Freeze Drone",
    "DRONE_COPYCAT_BODY_LORE": "Order: RD-273, Research Unit\nTracking Number: 465*****\nEstimated Delivery: 07/03/2060\nShipping Method: Standard\nShipping Address: Luyten's Star System, Exoterra,  Colony\nShipping Details:\n\nThis is the department head of High Pressure based out of Mercury's Atmospherics and Us Laboratory. We're sending this drone in compliance with the court order to the observational lab on Exoterra.\n\nAttached are the instructions on how to operate the drone, along with the extended warranty.\n\n<i>P.S.\n\nHerdles (our name for the drone) is dear to all our hearts, please take care of it. You need to prop up the charger in its port so it charges correctly, and don't update it! It has a lot of delightful quirks you don't want to miss out on.\n\nIf you have some pressure suits, activate herdletime.exe and have fun! Just make sure to push the ice <b>away from you</b> TO someone else in a pressure suit!\n\nP.P.S.\n\nAlso, if you can send it back that'd be great!<i>",
    "DRONE_COPYCAT_PRIMARY_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a bouncing disc that freezes targets.",
    "DRONE_COPYCAT_PRIMARY_SKILL_NAME": "Freeze Disc",
    "DRONE_DTGUNNER_BODY_NAME": "CROSSHAIRS",
    "DRONE_DTGUNNER_COMMAND": "Fire a hail of bullets that ricochet to a nearby enemy.",
    "DRONE_DTGUNNER_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires repeatedly for <style=cIsDamage>85% damage</style>. Bullets bounce to a nearby enemy for <style=cIsDamage>50% damage</style>. The number of shots scales with attack speed.",
    "DRONE_DTGUNNER_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a 4-round burst for <style=cIsDamage>4x50% damage</style>. Automatically repairs when downed.",
    "DRONE_DTGUNNER_DESCRIPTION": "Operator's special gunner drone. It follows Operator at a close distance shooting nearby enemies. Automatically repairs when downed.",
    "DRONE_DTGUNNER_INTERACTABLE_NAME": "Rebooting Gunner Drone Mk 2",
    "DRONE_DTGUNNER_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>//-- GOOD MORNING --\n//-- SYSTEMS CHECK : OK --\n//-- BEGIN ARMAMENT CALIBRATION : OK --\n//-- BEGIN OPERATOR COMMLINK: DAILY CADENCE --// </style>\n\n\n\"Good morning, Cross. Hope you slept well.\"\n> ...\n\"Just a little joke. Alright, let's begin.\"\n\n\n> LOGIN: UES_CPT\n> PASSWORD: *****\n> WELCOME, CAPTAIN. PLEASE ENTER COMMAND\n\n>> INCOMING COMMAND...\n>> INIT ARM_BLTHOSE.CMD -o -c\n\n> DENIED: USER ADMIN TOKEN EXPIRED. ARE YOU STILL USING PASSWORDS?\n\n>> INCOMING COMMAND...\n>> SUDO INIT ARM_BLTHOSE.CMD -o -c\n\n> OK. WARMING ARMAMENT...\n> ACQUIRING TARGET... FOUND.\n> ARMAMENT OPERATION: <b>INITIATED</b>\n> AMMUNITION: 300 | TIME ELAPSED: 00:00:00>\n> AMMUNITION: 100 | TIME ELAPSED: 00:00:03\n> AMMUNITION: 050 | TIME ELAPSED: 00:00:05\n> AMMUNITION: 010 | TIME ELAPSED: 00:00:07\n> AMMUNITION: 000 | TIME ELAPSED: 00:00:05\n> ARAMAMENT DEPLETED\n> TARGET EFFECT... CONFIRMED.\n\n> PLEASE ENTER COMMAND_\n\n\"Excellent. That is all.\" \n\n<style=cMono>//-- COMMLINK TERMINATED --//</style>\n<style=cMono>//-- BEGIN HIBERNATION --//</style>",
    "DRONE_DTHEALING_BODY_NAME": "DOC",
    "DRONE_DTHEALING_COMMAND": "Administers a stim-shot that grants barrier and increased speed.",
    "DRONE_DTHEALING_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Administers a stim-shot that grants the survivor a <style=cIsHealing>temporary barrier</style> and increases their <style=cIsDamage>attack speed</style> and <style=cIsDamage>movement speed</style> by <style=cIsDamage>25%</style>.",
    "DRONE_DTHEALING_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Deploys a healing beam that <style=cIsHealing>restores health</style> equal to <style=cIsDamage>200% base damage</style>. Automatically repairs when downed.",
    "DRONE_DTHEALING_DESCRIPTION": "Operator's special healing drone. It follows Operator at a close distance, healing them and close allies. Can only heal one target at a time. Automatically repairs when downed.",
    "DRONE_DTHEALING_INTERACTABLE_NAME": "Rebooting Healing Drone Mk 2",
    "DRONE_DTHEALING_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>//-- NEW MISSION PENDING  --//\n//-- DIRECTIVE: OPTIMIZE COMMUNICATIONS --//\n//-- ANALYZING MISSION HISTORY --//\n//-- BEGIN PLAYBACK --//</style>\n\nA cacophony of saurian roars and high-caliber gunfire crackles in, dimmed almost immediately by the recording's background noise suppression algorithm. Rapid footsteps and metallic breathing follow.\n\n\"DOC! Hurry that stim up.\"\n\n{<i>BEEP</i>}\n\n\"We've been over the data. If I can go <i>fast</i> then I won't need first-aid.\" \n\n{<i>BLIP</i>}\n{<i>BEEEEEP</i>}\n\n\"Squishy? Who are you callin' squishy? I've got at least... 3 quarts left in me.\"\n\n{<i>BIP...</i>} {<i>BIP...</i>} {<i>BIP...</i>} \n{<i>BING</i>}\n\n\"Fine. Cut it 50/50. Better than an all-protein diet.\"\n\n{<i>BWIP</i>}\n{<i>BWOO</i>}\n\nThe feed ends abruptly.",
    "DRONE_DTHAULER_BODY_NAME": "CHIRP",
    "DRONE_DTHAULER_COMMAND": "Lifts the target into the air, and throws them at the ground.",
    "DRONE_DTHAULER_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsDamage>Stunning.</style> Lifts the target into the air and throws it at a nearby enemy, dealing <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style> on impact. Can lift and deposit chests.",
    "DRONE_DTHAULER_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsUtility>Stuns</style> targets and lifts them into the air, before dropping them for <style=cIsDamage>increased fall damage</style>. Automatically repairs when downed.",
    "DRONE_DTHAULER_DESCRIPTION": "Operator's special transport drone. Grabs onto targets and lifts them high into the air, dropping them for fall damage. Automatically repairs when downed.",
    "DRONE_DTHAULER_INTERACTABLE_NAME": "Rebooting Transport Drone Mk 2",
    "DRONE_DTHAULER_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>//-- NEW APPLICATION INSTALL: ABORTED.\n//-- CRITICAL FAILURE: OUT OF MEMORY --//\n//-- ACCESSING MEMORY FOR USER REVIEW --//\n//-- SORTBY: AGE: OLDEST FIRST --//</style>\n\n\"There. My finest creation yet.\"\n\nA video feed snaps on. The camera looks out over a miniature landscape of parts and tools, up into wide-set goggles festooned with eyes.\n\nThe goggles lift, revealing a man's face. Or, what's left. His eyes shimmer with admiration.\n\n\"You're such an elegant machine. No firearms, no hydraulics. Able to reach the loftiest heights. And look--\"\nThe technician reveals their right hand, a mechanical claw.\n\n\"You're just like me.\"\n\n\n<style=cMono>//-- DELETE? Y/N  --//</style>",
    "EMERGENCYDRONE_COMMAND": "Heals all allies in a large area, and grants increased health regeneration.",
    "EQUIPMENTDRONE_COMMAND": "Ram straight into the target, dealing damage.",
    "EMERGENCYDRONE_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Deploys a healing nova, <style=cIsHealing>restoring health</style> and increasing <style=cIsHealing>health regeneration</style> for a duration.",
    "EMERGENCYDRONE_FUNCTION": "Heals you and close allies. Can heal multiple targets at once.",
    "EMERGENCYDRONE_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>//--RECOVERED LOG FROM MD-50_262-65 --//</style>\n\n<style=cMono>[CYCLE-000_UES-ORBITAL-ENTRY]</style>\nEntry trajectory tolerances exceeded. No biological units found. Entering rest mode.\n\n<style=cMono>[CYCLE-005_REST-MODE-OPTIMIZATIONS]</style>\nUninstalled PROTOCOL-92-93_DEFIB-DEFENSIVE-USE use protocols. Free space optimizes subject diagnosis accuracy by 6.20-11.10%.\n\n<style=cMono>[CYCLE-007_PATIENT-FOUND]</style>\nLinked with [Commando: Unknown] -- Patient suspended within viscous alien lifeform. Healing protocols outpacing acid degradation. Treatment course applied for 14 hours and still no thanks received.",
    "EMERGENCYDRONE_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Deploys up to 8 healing beams that <style=cIsHealing>restore health</style> equal to <style=cIsDamage>50% base damage</style> per second.",
    "DRONE_EMERGENCY_PRIMARY_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Heals close allies. Can heal multiple targets at once.",
    "DRONE_EMERGENCY_PRIMARY_SKILL_NAME": "Enhanced Heal Beam",
    "EQUIPMENTDRONE_FUNCTION": "Uses the supplied equipment on nearby enemies.",
    "EQUIPMENTDRONE_BODY_LORE": "\"Introducing the CV-33! Folks, this drone can do it all. With the latest in drone AI technology, this unit can adapt to nearly any situation. Thanks to the universal coupler located on the underside of the unit, you could give the CV-33 anything and send it to work! Need a hand around the house? Give it a vacuum and watch those carpets sparkle! Your kids need someone to play with? Introduce them to their new friend, the CV-33! You can teach the CV-33 to do anything, given the right tools. You'll want one in YOUR house, folks, so get them now before they're gone!\"\n\n- Interplanetary Drone Convention, 2053",
    "EQUIPMENTDRONE_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Activates the given <style=cIsUtility>equipment</style>. The equipment's cooldown is reduced by <style=cIsUtility>80%</style>.",
    "FLAMEDRONE_COMMAND": "Fires a medium-range flamethrower.",
    "FLAMEDRONE_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsDamage>Ignite.</style> Burns enemies for <style=cIsDamage>2000% damage</style>.",
    "FLAMEDRONE_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a flamethrower, dealing <style=cIsDamage>2000% damage over 3 seconds.</style> Has a chance to <style=cIsDamage>Burn</style> enemies, dealing <style=cIsDamage>50% extra damage</style> over time.",
    "FLAMEDRONE_FUNCTION": "Burns nearby enemies.",
    "FLAMEDRONE_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>//--AUTO-TRANSCRIPTION FROM CARGO BAY OF UES [Redacted] --//</style>\n\nThe sound of a crate being forcefully opened with a metallic twang as it unlatches. A brief moment of silence hits.\n\n\"You broke open a crate for a drone? Listen, Jerry, if you're feeling bored, we can go get a drink, it's ok.\"\n\n\"Shut up! This is a CV-451!\"\n\n\"Which is... what? Your resume for how nerdy you are?\"\n\n\"You- no. This is black. Market. Drone tech. You know what this means?\"\n\n\"You're not only breaking the law but probably pissing off a bunch of criminals too?\"\n\n\"It means we have to report this!\"\n\n\"Yeah bud, you go do that.\"\n\nA sudden clang as the door to the hangar shuts and a crate falls over. Another, long moment of silence before the second speaker continues in hushed tones.\n\n\"Come on! You're telling me you don't want to be a hero? Everyone would be talking about us!\"\n\n\"Yeah, and as soon as we get to port it'll be the <i>wrong</i> people talking. This is a bad idea.\"\n\n\"For real?\"\n\n\"For real. Let's close this up and maybe we figure out what to- Hey, did you hear that?\"\n\n Two sudden popping sounds break into the audio stream, followed by two dull thuds. Several pairs of heavy footsteps, the scrape of heavy things dragged across paved metal, and a shipping crate being resealed. The audio recording cuts off. ",
    "FLAMEDRONE_DESCRIPTION": "A companion bought with gold that will follow the survivor at a close distance and moves towards nearby targets and burns them.",
    "DRONE_FLAME_PRIMARY_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Burns enemies.",
    "DRONE_FLAME_PRIMARY_SKILL_NAME": "Flamethrower",
    "DRONE_GUNNER_FUNCTION": "Shoots nearby enemies.",
    "DRONE_GUNNER_COMMAND": "Fires a hail of bullets.",
    "DRONE_GUNNER_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a 4-round burst for <style=cIsDamage>4x50% damage</style>.",
    "DRONE_GUNNER_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>Accessing database... done!\nReading specs... done!\nPrinting information for review... done!</style>\n\nProduct Name: TC-05 Gunner Drone\nManufacturer: Provost Interplanetary Security, Drone Division 5\nSerial No.: #1023501010123606814\n\nNotes:\n- Universal firearm allows drone to be loaded with all compatible ammunition.\n- Streamlined hardware allows for storage of excess ammunition within hull!\n- State-of-the-art dimensional perception chip allows the drone to track targets 250% faster and more accurately than competing models.\n- Capable of accurately hitting targets at up to 500 meters away.\n- Solar battery allows for operation time of 70 hours without recharge, even under high-intensity operation.\n- Easily reactivated through UES-compliant \"cash-to-key\" protocol.",
    "DRONE_GUNNER_PRIMARY_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Shoots a 3-Round burst.",
    "DRONE_GUNNER_PRIMARY_SKILL_NAME": "Fusilade",
    "DRONE_GUNNER_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires repeatedly for <style=cIsDamage>85% damage</style>. The number of shots scales with attack speed.",
    "DRONE_HAULER_BODY_NAME": "Transport Drone",
    "DRONE_HAULER_CONTEXT": "Repair Transport Drone",
    "DRONE_HAULER_COMMAND": "Lifts the target into the air, and throws them at the ground.",
    "DRONE_HAULER_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsDamage>Stunning.</style> Lifts the target into the air and throws it at a nearby enemy, dealing <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style> on impact.",
    "DRONE_HAULER_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsUtility>Stuns</style> targets and lifts them into the air, before dropping them for <style=cIsDamage>increased fall damage</style>.",
    "DRONE_HAULER_DESCRIPTION": "A companion bought with gold that will follow the survivor at a close distance. Grabs onto targets and lifts them high into the air, dropping them for fall damage.",
    "DRONE_HAULER_FUNCTION": "Grabs onto targets and lifts them high into the air, dropping them for fall damage.",
    "DRONE_HAULER_INTERACTABLE_NAME": "Broken Transport Drone",
    "DRONE_HAULER_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>Accessing database... done!\nReading specs... done!\nPrinting information for review... done!</style>\n\nProduct Name: CV-889 Transport Drone\nManufacturer: GBX Construction Company\nSerial No.: #0681468013470137\n\nNotes:\n- Modular coupler allows for swapping between various types of coupling units for carrying different types of cargo.\n- Maximum work load of up to 100 tons allows for heavy lifting to be automated.\n- Can transport passengers by attaching via safety buckle.*\n- Safety buckle is included with every purchase.*\n- Togglable \"safety mode\" allows for adjusted behavior while carrying passengers.\n\n<i>*System Message: Usage of passenger transport without mandatory safety buckle has been restricted by order of Supreme Court of the Sol system, as of case 832-B5: Johnson vs GBX Construction Company. Unsafe usage of passenger transport can expose users to hazardous or potentially fatal drops.</i>",
    "DRONE_HEALING_COMMAND": "Administers a burst of healing that grants a movement and attack speed buff.",
    "DRONE_HEALING_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Administers a stim-shot to a survivor that <style=cIsHealing>restores health</style> and increases their <style=cIsDamage>attack speed</style> and <style=cIsDamage>movement speed</style> by <style=cIsDamage>25%</style>.",
    "DRONE_HEALING_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Deploys a healing beam that <style=cIsHealing>restores health</style> equal to <style=cIsDamage>200% base damage</style>.",
    "DRONE_HEALING_FUNCTION": "Heals you and close allies. Can only heal one target at a time.",
    "DRONE_HEALING_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>//--AUTO-TRANSCRIPTION FROM MEDBAY OF UES [Redacted] --//</style>\n\n\"Heard the salvage team discovered a crate of undamaged MD-03 Healing drones recently.\"\n\n\"Oh yeah? Thank GOD, that'll make our jobs a LOT easier.\"\n\n\"Yeah, for sure...\"\n\n\"...? Something wrong?\"\n\n\"No, it's just... I once read this report that claimed that those healing rays cause cancer through extended use.\"\n\n\"Wh- huh??\"\n\n\"Something about the magnetic stimulation of the body's healing processes... I dunno, it DID say that it wasn't any more of a risk than a typical X-Ray, so maybe it's nothing to worry about?\"\n\n\"I guess, but... knowing this planet, let's just keep this between us, okay?\"",
    "DRONE_HEALING_PRIMARY_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Heals an allied target.",
    "DRONE_HEALING_PRIMARY_SKILL_NAME": "Heal Beam",
    "DRONE_JAILER_BODY_NAME": "Jailer Drone",
    "DRONE_JAILER_CONTEXT": "Repair Jailer Drone",
    "DRONE_JAILER_COMMAND": "Deploys a cage on the target that pulls in nearby enemies.",
    "DRONE_JAILER_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsDamage>Stunning.</style> Deploys a cage on the target that deals <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style> and pulls in nearby enemies.",
    "DRONE_JAILER_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Deploys a cage that <style=cIsDamage>roots</style> nearby enemies for <style=cIsDamage>5 seconds</style>.",
    "DRONE_JAILER_DESCRIPTION": "A companion bought with gold that will follow the survivor at a close distance. Roots all targets within an area for a certain amount of time.",
    "DRONE_JAILER_FUNCTION": "Roots all targets within an area for a certain amount of time.",
    "DRONE_JAILER_INTERACTABLE_NAME": "Broken Jailer Drone",
    "DRONE_JAILER_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>//--AUTO-TRANSCRIPTION FROM UES [Redacted] CISLUNAR FAUNA RESEARCH POST--//</style>\n\nThe new RD-122 drone is working wonders for our troublemakers. Once they start showing signs of anxiety in transit prep, we activate the RD-122, et voila! All we need is a bit of protective gear (the warnings of overexposure are troubling) and now, all our little troublemakers can get from point A to B no problem!\n\nGranted, when they get there, they have trouble standing and waking up, which is a bit concerning. But Charlie has assured us that it's totally harmless. In fact, he says he activates it for a little bit before sleeping as a bit of white noise. Can't be too bad for them!",
    "DRONE_JAILER_PRIMARY_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Roots all targets within the target area.",
    "DRONE_JAILER_PRIMARY_SKILL_NAME": "Lockdown",
    "DRONE_JUNK_BODY_NAME": "Junk Drone",
    "DRONE_JUNK_COMMAND": "Fires a stunning ball of Junk.",
    "DRONE_JUNK_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsDamage>Stunning.</style> Fires a ball of Junk in an arc that explodes for <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style>.",
    "DRONE_JUNK_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Periodically dispenses <style=cIsUtility>temporary items</style>. <style=cIsUtility>The number of items increases with levels</style>.",
    "DRONE_JUNK_CONTEXT": "Repair Junk Drone",
    "DRONE_JUNK_DESCRIPTION": "A companion bought with gold that will follow the survivor at a close distance. Dispenses temporary items at regular intervals.",
    "DRONE_JUNK_FUNCTION": "Dispenses temporary items at regular intervals.",
    "DRONE_JUNK_INTERACTABLE_NAME": "Broken Junk Drone",
    "DRONE_JUNK_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>//--AUTO-TRANSCRIPTION FROM UES SAFE TRAVELS OFFICER CORPS CONFERENCE ROOM 56-ZULU --//</style>\n\n\"Ronald, why didn't you show up for roll call today? And why isn't that drone shut down?\"\n\n\"...\"\n\n\"Ronald, you did not just print a sleeping version of yourself and hand it to me. No, do not print another one. You are not revolutionizing communication. You are revolutionizing how to be a pain.\"\n\n\"...\"\n\n\"What did you print now- is that me?\"\n\n\"...\"\n\n\"Do not hand that to me.\"\n\n\"...but it's accurate. I want you to have it.\"\n\n\"I... great.\"",
    "DRONE_JUNK_PRIMARY_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Dispenses temporary items.",
    "DRONE_JUNK_PRIMARY_SKILL_NAME": "Surprise!",
    "DRONE_MEGA_COMMAND": "Flies forward, firing bullets and rockets at nearby enemies.",
    "DRONE_MEGA_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Flies forward, firing bullets for <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style> and launching explosive rockets for <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style>.",
    "DRONE_MEGA_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a barrage of heavy bullets for <style=cIsDamage>15x220% damage</style> and a pair of explosive rockets for <style=cIsDamage>2x400% damage</style>.",
    "DRONE_MEGA_FUNCTION": "Shoots bullets or launches missiles at nearby targets.",
    "DRONE_MEGA_BODY_LORE": "To all members of the TC-280 Autonomous Weapons Platform program,\n\nI regret to inform you all that Rob Martin, head of the TC-280 Autonomous Weapons Platform program, passed away Sunday night.\n\nAfter taking into consideration both this loss of key leadership and this project's long-running history of failure to produce a viable product, we have decided to dissolve the division. All personnel on the project, except otherwise noted, will be joining the Darkstar program under my supervision. I would like to welcome you all in making something truly impactful and worthwhile even better.\n\nNow, with welcomes out of the way, I would like to take a moment to address the team behind the \"Predictive Threat System\" of the TC-280. You see, I'm a pretty happy guy. I can always appreciate a good prank. But when you waste millions of dollars in company assets and scare the buyers it stops being cute real quick. You are all, I'm sure, intimately aware that I have been <i>consistently</i> targeted by these artificial intelligence systems in the past four VIP Defense demonstrations led by Rob. Every day, I'm thankful for my life that we have had the foresight and budgetary sense to keep our demonstrations virtual. With each incident, we've had to replace live rounds with blanks, remove rocket weapon systems, add limiters to the flight turbines, and install a remote override for the propulsion systems to address its determined attempts to <i>kill me</i> in front of our valued guests. Your choices declare to the company that you consider your job a joke, so I will be taking those declarations as your official resignation.\n\nAnyone who wishes to pay their respects to Rob will be able to do so from 4:00 AM - 5:00 AM in the Martha Landry Conference Room. The customary service hour has been shifted forward to accommodate the Darkstar team orientation.\n\nJust a friendly reminder to the rest of our new team members: if you humiliate me, you humiliate this company. Let's all set a good example.\n\n\nRichter J. Ward\nVice President, New Horizon Arms Corporation",
    "DRONE_MEGA_PRIMARY_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Shoots targets.",
    "DRONE_MEGA_PRIMARY_SKILL_NAME": "Mega Turret",
    "DRONE_MEGA_SECONDARY_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Launches missiles.",
    "DRONE_MEGA_SECONDARY_SKILL_NAME": "Twin Rocket",
    "DRONE_MISSILE_COMMAND": "Fires a barrage of seeking missiles.",
    "DRONE_MISSILE_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a barrage of seeking missiles that explode for <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style>.",
    "DRONE_MISSILE_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Fires a barrage of missiles that explode for <style=cIsDamage>4x100% damage</style>.",
    "DRONE_MISSILE_FUNCTION": "Launches missiles at nearby enemies.",
    "DRONE_MISSILE_BODY_LORE": "Return: \"TC-222 Viper-Model Missile Drone\"\nTracking Number: 13******\nEstimated Delivery: 05/13/2056\nShipping Method: Priority\nShipping Address: Provost Interplanetary Security, Galle, Mars\nShipping Details:\n\n<style=cMono>//--AUTO-TRANSCRIPTION FROM PERSONAL RECORDER--//</style>\n\"Lil' Snippy's been holding down the homestead real nice-like, 'til one day the computer mistakes the hounds for those boars that come onto the property. Last time we trust one of these - not lookin' for a fix. Best call up your attorneys.\"",
    "DRONE_MISSILE_PRIMARY_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Launches missiles at nearby enemies.",
    "DRONE_MISSILE_PRIMARY_SKILL_NAME": "Missile Barrage",
    "DRONE_RECHARGE_BODY_NAME": "Barrier Drone",
    "DRONE_RECHARGE_COMMAND": "Recharges the owner, granting barrier and refreshing skill cooldowns.",
    "DRONE_RECHARGE_COMMAND_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Recharge the owner, granting <style=cIsHealing>temporary barrier</style> and <style=cIsDamage>refreshing skill cooldowns.</style>",
    "DRONE_RECHARGE_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Deploys a charging beam that grants a <style=cIsHealing>temporary barrier</style> equal to <style=cIsDamage>800% base damage</style>.",
    "DRONE_RECHARGE_CONTEXT": "Repair Barrier Drone",
    "DRONE_RECHARGE_DESCRIPTION": "A companion bought with gold that will follow the survivor at a close distance. Projects a barrier onto allied targets.",
    "DRONE_RECHARGE_FUNCTION": "Projects a barrier onto allied targets.",
    "DRONE_RECHARGE_INTERACTABLE_NAME": "Broken Barrier Drone",
    "DRONE_RECHARGE_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>//--AUTO-TRANSCRIPTION FROM CREW QUARTERS OF UES SAFE TRAVELS --//</style>\n\n\n\"Sarge, I don't feel so good. Head's beginning to hurt something fierce, I think all these weird doodads we've been using is messing with me.\"\n\n\n\"Right. Anyways, here's the medic.\"\n\n\n\"Sarge, I was thinking, maybe using this particular drone as a doctor isn't the best idea-\"\n\n\n\"Medic, give him his medicine.\"\n\n\nA spraying sound emits and the private begins spluttering. A loud bang is heard.\n\n\n\"Medic, the private fell. Give him more medicine.\"\n\n\nA faint hum sounds, and the spray begins again.",
    "DRONE_RECHARGE_PRIMARY_SKILL_NAME": "Barrier Buildup",
    "DRONE_RECHARGE_PRIMARY_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Projects a barrier onto an allied target.",
    "TURRET1_FUNCTION": "Shoots nearby enemies.",
    "TURRET1_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>//--AUTO-TRANSCRIPTION FROM FIELD OPERATIONS STAGING OF UES SAFE TRAVELS --//</style>\n\n\"Alright, folks! Listen up.\"\n\n\"Many of you will be dropping into hostile territory for the first time. Down there, anything might happen. You may get separated from your squad. You may land in the deepest ditch, or up on the highest peak. Luckily, the fellas down in the hardware divison have cooked up your new best friends.\"\n\n\"Allow me to introduce the TC-2RT. These don't have the speed or inertial processing of your standard drone accompaniment. But what they lack in mobility, they more than make up for in pure downrange output and enfilading killbox potential.\"\n\n\"Ahead of your drop, we will strategically distribute to each drop zone precisely one TC-2RT per 200 meters. With luck, you'll stroll out of those pods and right into the park.\"",
    "TURRET1_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Rapidly fires for <style=cIsDamage>30% damage</style>. Can fire up to 40 bullets before reloading.",
    "DRONE_SCRAPPER_CONTEXT": "Scrap Drone",
    "DRONE_SCRAPPER_DESCRIPTION": "Allows survivors to sacrifice drones in exchange for pieces of scrap that are the same rarity as the sacrificed drone.",
    "DRONE_SCRAPPER_NAME": "Drone Scrapper",
    "DRONE_SCRAPPER_POPUP_TEXT": "<b>Drone Scrapper</b>\n<i><style=cSub><size=75%>Turn Drones into recyclable scrap!</size></style></i>",
    "DRONE_VENDOR_TERMINAL_CONTEXT": "Select Drone",
    "DRONE_VENDOR_TERMINAL_NAME": "Triple Drone Shop",
    "DRONETECH_AUGMENTED1_TOOLTIP": "<style=cKeywordName>Augmented</style><style=cSub>Drones used for this skill augment its properties.\r\n<style=cIsDamage>Combat</style> Drones - <style=cIsDamage>+10% damage</style> <style=cStack>(per drone)</style>.\r\n<style=cIsHealing>Healing</style> Drones - <style=cIsUtility>+10% duration</style> <style=cStack>(per drone)</style>.\r\n<style=cIsUtility>Utility</style> Drones - <style=cIsUtility>+10% AoE size</style> <style=cStack>(per drone)</style>.</style>",
    "DRONETECH_AUGMENTED2_TOOLTIP": "<style=cKeywordName>Augmented</style><style=cSub>Drones used for this skill augment its properties.\r\n<style=cIsDamage>Combat</style> Drones - <style=cIsDamage>+10%</style> projectile <style=cIsDamage>damage</style> <style=cStack>(per drone)</style>.\r\n<style=cIsHealing>Healing</style> Drones - <style=cIsUtility>+15%</style> projectile <style=cIsUtility>distance</style> <style=cStack>(per drone)</style>.\r\n<style=cIsUtility>Utility</style> Drones - <style=cIsUtility>+5%</style> <style=cIsUtility>damage reduction</style> for shield drones <style=cStack>(per drone)</style>.</style>",
    "DRONETECH_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>Welcome to DataScraper (v3.5.16 - beta branch)\n$ Scraping memory...done.\n$ Resolving... failed.\n$ Resolving... failed.\n$ Resolv..in...</style>\n\n                          uuuuuuu\n                   uu$$$$$$$$$$$uu\n             uu$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$uu\n           u$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$u\n          u$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$u\n         u$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$u\n         u$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$u\n         u$$$$$$\\\"       \\\"$$$\\\"       \\\"$$$$$$u\n         \\\"$$$$\\\"             u$u              $$$$\\\"\n          $$$u               u$u              u$$$\n          $$$u             u$$$u            u$$$\n           \\\"$$$$uu$$$           $$$uu$$$$\\\"\n            \\\"$$$$$$$\\\"             \\\"$$$$$$$\\\"\n                   u$$$$$$$u$$$$$$$u\n                      u$\\\"$\\\"$\\\"$\\\"$\\\"$\\\"$u\n  uuu              $$u$ $ $ $ $u$$                 uuu\n u$$$$            $$$$$u$u$u$$$             u$$$$\n  $$$$$uu         \\\"$$$$$$$$$\\\"         uu$$$$$$\nu$$$$$$$$$$$uu    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\\"      uuuu$$$$$$$$$$\n$$$$\\\"\\\"\\\"$$$$$$$$$$uuu   uu$$$$$$$$$\\\"\\\"\\\"$$$\\\"\n \\\"\\\"\\\"            \\\"\\\"$$$$$$$$$$$uu \\\"\\\"$\\\"\\\"\\\"\n                  uuuu \\\"\\\"$$$$$$$$$$uuu\n  u$$$uuu$$$$$$$$$uu \"\"$$$$$$$$$$$uuu$$$\\\n  $$$$$$$$$$\\\"\\\"\\\"\\\"                     \\\"\\\"$$$$$$$$$$$\\\"\n   \\\"$$$$$\\\"                                           \\\"\\\"$$$$\\\"\\\"\n     $$$\\\"                                                 $$$$\\\"\n\nI know what you seek.\nYou won't find it anymore. Not here, nor in the Carbide Jungle, nor in the ash fields beneath Minorsky's Gate.\n\nDon't waste your time digging.\nSome things are better left forgotten!\nThose files were of higher security than anything you know.\n\nGot a problem? Take it up with the captain.\nAnd know that he's let more slide for less.\n\n<i>See ya.</i>\n\n<style=cMono>$ ERROR. Output failed.\n$ File appears corrupted and cannot be opened.\n$ Retry?",
    "DRONETECH_BODY_NAME": "Operator",
    "DRONETECH_BODY_SUBTITLE": "Coerced Specialist",
    "DRONETECH_COMMAND": "COMMAND: {0}",
    "DRONETECH_COMPANIONCOMBAT_DESCRIPTION": "A customized gunner drone will spawn with you at the start of each stage. Automatically repairs when downed.",
    "DRONETECH_COMPANIONCOMBAT_NAME": "Gunner Drone Mk 2",
    "DRONETECH_COMPANIONHEALING_DESCRIPTION": "A customized healing drone will spawn with you at the start of each stage. Automatically repairs when downed.",
    "DRONETECH_COMPANIONHEALING_NAME": "Healing Drone Mk 2",
    "DRONETECH_COMPANIONHAULER_DESCRIPTION": "A customized transport drone will spawn with you at the start of each stage. Automatically repairs when downed.",
    "DRONETECH_COMPANIONHAULER_NAME": "Transport Drone Mk 2",
    "DRONETECH_DESCRIPTION": "Operator is an evasive frontline commander. He uses drones as a force multiplier, leveraging battlefield chaos at opportune moments. <style=cSub>\r\n\r\n< ! > H3-11 OCR Custom charges up over time. Shots ricochet on-kill, useful in conjunction with drone firepower.\r\n\r\n< ! > ADMIN-OVERRIDE can be used to directly command your next-up drone. Use other skills to manipulate the queue order. Experiment with drones to discover their abilities.\r\n\r\n< ! > Ascent Protocol is a great escape tool and useful traversal method. Use its follow-up to chain leaps between drones and prolong your ascent.\r\n\r\n< ! > Ejection Core is useful for controlling the battlefield. Suspend enemies aloft, setting up burst windows for massive damage.\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n",
    "DRONETECH_SKIN_ALT1_NAME": "Drone Division",
    "DRONETECH_GUNNERDRONE_NAME": "CROSSHAIRS",
    "DRONETECH_HEALINGDRONE_NAME": "DOC",
    "DRONETECH_HAULERDRONE_NAME": "CHIRP",
    "KEYWORD_NANOBUG": "<style=cKeywordName>Nano Bug</style><style=cSub>Increases damage taken from <style=cIsUtility>skills</style> by <style=cIsDamage>100%</style>, split into hits that deal <style=cIsDamage>120% damage</style> each.</style>",
    "LOADOUT_DRONE": "Drone",
    "DRONETECH_RICOCHET_TOOLTIP": "<style=cKeywordName>Ricochet</style><style=cSub>Attack bounces to the lowest health enemy for <style=cIsDamage>75% TOTAL damage.</style>",
    "DRONETECH_PASSIVE_DESCRIPTION": "Start each stage with <style=cIsUtility>2</style> drone companions.",
    "DRONETECH_PASSIVE_NAME": "Drone Tech",
    "DRONETECH_PRIMARY_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsUtility>Rapid</style>. Fire a pistol shot that deals <style=cIsDamage>150%-600% damage</style> and <style=cIsDamage>ricochets</style> on kill. <style=cIsUtility>Restores charge over time.</style>",
    "DRONETECH_PRIMARY_NAME": "H3-11 OCR Custom",
    "DRONETECH_PRIMARY_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "Shoot a canister that deals <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style> on impact and releases <style=cIsDamage>5</style> seeking projectiles, dealing <style=cIsDamage>40% damage</style> each. <style=cIsUtility>Bugs</style> enemies.",
    "DRONETECH_PRIMARY_ALT_NAME": "Nano Canister",
    "DRONETECH_SECONDARY_DESCRIPTION": "Command a drone to activate its <style=cIsDamage>Special skill</style>. Can store a charge for each drone you control.",
    "DRONETECH_SECONDARY_NAME": "ADMIN-OVERRIDE",
    "DRONETECH_SECONDARY_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "Enter <style=cIsUtility>target-painting mode</style> to command your drones to ram enemies for <style=cIsDamage>450%</style> damage. Critical Strikes also <style=cIsDamage>ignite</style>.",
    "DRONETECH_SECONDARY_ALT_NAME": "CMD-SWARM",
    "DRONETECH_UTILITY_DESCRIPTION": "Command a drone to lift you into the air for a <style=cIsUtility>controlled fall</style> to the ground. Can be <style=cIsUtility>reactivated</style> to leap to another drone.",
    "DRONETECH_UTILITY_NAME": "Ascent Protocol",
    "DRONETECH_UTILITY_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "Command a drone to charge up a <style=cIsUtility>shield</style> that blocks damage. Release to fire it forward for <style=cIsDamage>200%-600% damage</style>.",
    "DRONETECH_UTILITY_ALT_NAME": "FIREWALL",
    "DRONETECH_SPECIAL_DESCRIPTION": "Launch a drone that knocks enemies into the air for <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style>. Enemies are <style=cIsUtility>Nano-Bugged</style> until they hit the ground.",
    "DRONETECH_SPECIAL_NAME": "Ejection Core",
    "DRONETECH_SPECIAL_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "Launch a drone that charges up by absorbing damage. After a short duration, it explodes, dealing <style=cIsDamage>300-2000% damage</style>.",
    "DRONETECH_SPECIAL_ALT_NAME": "Amp Core",
    "DRONETECH_OUTRO_FLAVOR": "..and so he left, calculating his next act.",
    "DRONETECH_MAIN_ENDING_ESCAPE_FAILURE_FLAVOR": "..and so he vanished, his designs unfulfilled.",
    "ELITE_MODIFIER_COLLECTIVE": "Collective {0}",
    "EQUIPMENT_AFFIXCOLLECTIVE_NAME": "Of One Mind",
    "EQUIPMENT_AFFIXCOLLECTIVE_PICKUP": "Become an aspect of the Collective.",
    "EQUIPMENT_DRONESHOCKDAMAGE_DESC": "<style=cIsDamage>Electrocutes</style> enemies hit by the survivor or their drones for <style=cIsDamage>+300%</style> damage every <style=cIsUtility>1s</style>. Lasts <style=cIsUtility>5s</style>. Electrocuted enemies have a small chance of <style=cIsDamage>Electrocuting</style> nearby enemies when taking damage. Electrical damage increases this chance.",
    "EQUIPMENT_DRONESHOCKDAMAGE_LORE": "Order: Faulty Conductor \r\nTracking Number: 88*2**** \r\nEstimated Delivery: 07/08/2056 \r\nShipping Method:  Standard \r\nShipping Address: 780 North Unit 5, Traloger, Mercury \r\nShipping Details: \r\n\r\nReview attached to order. \r\n\r\nVendor Rating: 5-star \r\nAudio Feedback (Transcribed): Sending another order per our arrangement. These are great for... conduction. I, uh, use them in my \"kitchen\" drones and they've never been better at \"cooking\" things. One tweak I'd like to suggest to the next order is if you can increase the output. The kitchen drones can't quite seem to get the temperature to \"well-done\", if you know what I mean. ",
    "EQUIPMENT_DRONESHOCKDAMAGE_NAME": "Faulty Conductor",
    "EQUIPMENT_DRONESHOCKDAMAGE_PICKUP": "Survivor and drone attacks apply the Electrocuted debuff on hit, which can spread to nearby enemies when they are damaged.",
    "EQUIPMENT_GROUNDENEMIES_DESC": "Bring enemies within a <style=cIsUtility>10m</style> radius down to the ground and <style=cIsUtility>slow</style> them. If falling distance is greater than <style=cIsUtility>2.5m</style>, does <style=cIsDamage>10% damage</style> for each meter of falling. Lasts for <style=cIsUtility>10s</style>.",
    "EQUIPMENT_GROUNDENEMIES_LORE": "Order: G-Force Accelerator \r\nTracking Number: 12**3**4 \r\nEstimated Delivery: 03/03/2056 \r\nShipping Method:  Fragile \r\nShipping Address: Cruz Labs, Plymouth, Earth \r\nShipping Details: \r\n\r\nDear Doctor Hill, \r\n\r\nA few months ago I came across this alien automaton. I found it lying in an open field near the local fairgrounds. When approaching it the atmosphere became heavy. I'm embarrassed to admit it took me a while to pick myself up off the floor and vacate the area. There was some kind of energy field it was emitting. \r\n\r\nAfter figuring out how to transport it I was able to dissect it at the lab. I extracted the part that was generating the energy field, but it bothers me that I can't figure out what its purpose is. Maybe you'll have better luck? ",
    "EQUIPMENT_GROUNDENEMIES_NAME": "G-Force Accelerator",
    "EQUIPMENT_GROUNDENEMIES_PICKUP": "Bring enemies down to the ground, dealing damage and slowing nearby enemies.",
    "EQUIPMENT_PARRY_DESC": "Briefly enter a countering stance that lets you parry <style=cIsUtility>any and ALL</style> damage. A successful parry <style=cIsHealing>nullifies incoming damage</style>, reduces your equipment cooldown by <style=cIsDamage>75%</style>, and grants <style=cShrine>Blessing</style>, causing your next attack to ALWAYS activate your on-hit effects.",
    "EQUIPMENT_PARRY_LORE": "<style=cMono>\r\nFIELDTECH Image-To-Text Translator (v2.5.10b)\r\n# Awaiting input... done.\r\n# Reading image for text... done.\r\n# Transcribing data... done.\r\n# Translating text... done. [5 exceptions raised]\r\nComplete: outputting results.</style>\r\n\r\nOh great [hero],\r\n\r\nthou saved us from our doom,\r\n\r\nand for that we give praise.\r\n\r\nThy compassion boundless,\r\n\r\nI humbly ask for your help again.\r\n\r\nDeliver me from misfortune,\r\n\r\nProtect me from my enemies,\r\n\r\nAnd allow me to bask in your radiance once more.\r\n\r\n<style=cMono>Translation Errors:</style>\r\n# [The Hero] could not be fully translated.\r\n",
    "EQUIPMENT_PARRY_NAME": "Deus Ex Machina",
    "EQUIPMENT_PARRY_PICKUP": "Counter any damage. Successful counters <style=cShrine>bless</style> your next attack, ensuring your on-hit effects ALWAYS activate.",
    "EXTRACTORUNIT_BODY_LORE": "37; SEARCHING\n\n38; SEARCHING\n\n38; ASSET DETECTED\n\n39; ACQUISITION BEGUN\n\n40; (5, 60°, 45°) M0R3 F0R U5!\n\n41; ASSET OBTAINED!\n\n42; SHINY\n\n43; EXCITED\n\n44; NO LONGER SHINY\n\n45; interestGONE = true\n\n46; (5, 60°, 45°) D154PP01NT3D. R35T4RT.\n\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n\n01; FIND ASSET\n\n02; SEARCHING",
    "EXTRACTORUNIT_BODY_NAME": "Solus Extractor",
    "FRIENDUNIT_BODY_NAME": "Best Buddy",
    "FRIENDUNIT_PET_CONTEXT": "Pet",
    "FRIENDUNIT_PET_MESSAGE": "You pet your buddy.",
    "FRIENDUNIT_PET_MESSAGE2": "{0} pets their buddy.",
    "GREASEPUDDLE_BODY_NAME": "Grease Puddle",
    "IRONHAULER_BODY_LORE": "Welcome to DataScraper (v3.1.53 – beta branch)\n\n\n$ Scraping memory... done.\n\n$ Resolving... done.\n\n$ Combing for relevant data... done.\n\nComplete!\n\nIt's been days since I was separated from my squad. My pod hit one of those giant, floating jellyfish. It exploded in some kind of lightning gel, and boom. Here I am. My electronics fritzed, stranding me in some barren canyon wasteland. The only thing I have going for me is the river I'm following. Hopefully it leads towards one of the rallypoints.\n\n-------------------------------------\n\nThere's some kind of mining outpost here, but nothing like I've ever seen. It's got sleek tech, nothing like the bucket of bolts UES keeps sending us on. Problem is, there's nothing here except this whack-o orb that keeps shooting beams and making a bunch of rocks rise and fall. Like it's some kind of game.\n\n--------------------------------------\n\nGoing to die here. Fell down a canyon after the mining outpost. Made a dumb lunge for a lizard to eat. Miscalculated, and fell into a pit with no way out. Walls are made of some weird material that I can't get a grip on.\n\nLooks like this is it.\n\n---------------------------------------\n\nThese are my final moments, but I'm not in that pit. No, the orb found me, lifted me out. Then kept lifting me. When I could see above the canyon walls, it dropped me... and caught me right before I hit the ground. \n\nIt's juggled me a few times now, and each time I've gotten a little bit closer to the ground.\n\nI don't think I'll be so lucky next time.",
    "IRONHAULER_BODY_NAME": "Solus Transporter",
    "ITEM_BARRIERONCOOLDOWN_DESC": "When a skill comes off cooldown, gain a <style=cIsDamage>temporary barrier</style> for <style=cIsHealing>1% <style=cStack>(+0.25% per stack)</style></style> of your maximum health per second of the skill's base cooldown.",
    "ITEM_BARRIERONCOOLDOWN_LORE": "<style=cMono>Welcome to DataScraper (v3.1.53 – beta branch) \r\n$ Scraping memory... done. \r\n$ Resolving... done. \r\n$ Combing for relevant data... done. \r\nComplete! \r\nOutputting local audio transcriptions... </style>\r\n\r\nProject G Commercial - Draft #05\r\n\r\n\"Man, killing these aliens has got me all tuckered out. I could sure use a drink that restores my energy AND quenches my thirst!\" Jean exclaimed as he finished off some Lemurians. \"But what could I find on this hostile alien planet?\" Out of the corner of his eye, Jean spots his saving grace - an Eclipse Lite, mercifully undamaged in an open crate. \"Eureka!\" Jean scooped up the perspiring bottle and hastily unscrewed the cap. Taking a swig, Jean exclaimed in joy. \"Wow, not only is it delicious, it's full of electrolytes! It's what thirsty soldiers on alien planets crave! Thank you Eclipse Zero, bravely frontiering new worlds of flavor!\"\r\n\r\n<style=cMono>This log entry has been brought to you by Eclipse: the Galactic Quencher</style>",
    "ITEM_BARRIERONCOOLDOWN_NAME": "Eclipse Lite",
    "ITEM_BARRIERONCOOLDOWN_PICKUP": "Gain a small temporary barrier when a skill comes off cooldown.",
    "ITEM_CRITATLOWERELEVATION_DESC": "Striking enemies from a higher elevation grants <style=cIsDamage>+1% <style=cStack>(+1% per stack)</style> critical strike chance</style> and <style=cIsDamage>critical strike damage</style>, up to <style=cIsUtility>10 times</style>. Lasts 10 seconds.",
    "ITEM_CRITATLOWERELEVATION_LORE": "Order: Altitude-Safety Hiking Boots \r\nTracking Number: 05015*********** \r\nEstimated Delivery: 04/13/2056 \r\nShipping Method:  Standard \r\nShipping Address: Mountain Outpost 041-C, Nepal, Earth \r\nShipping Details: \r\n\r\nGrabbed these boots from the market. Seller claimed the boots have implants that maintain focus at high altitudes - perfect for your thrill-seeking lifestyle, eh? Gimme a write-back and let me know how they work, or I'll bill you for the 20 bucks I spent on these things.",
    "ITEM_CRITATLOWERELEVATION_NAME": "Hiker's Boots",
    "ITEM_CRITATLOWERELEVATION_PICKUP": "Striking enemies from a higher elevation grants critical strike chance and damage.",
    "ITEM_DESTRUCTIBLESPAWNER_PING": "Stack of Dynamite",
    "ITEM_DRONESDROPDYNAMITE_DESC": "Gain <style=cIsDamage>Lt. Droneboy</style>. While in combat, your drones drop sticks of dynamite that detonate for <style=cIsDamage>240% damage <style=cStack>(+85% per stack)</style></style>, stunning enemies. Recharges after <style=cIsUtility>10</style> seconds.",
    "ITEM_DRONESDROPDYNAMITE_LORE": "Order: Box of Dynamite \r\nTracking Number: 783***2* \r\nEstimated Delivery: 04/13/2056 \r\nShipping Method:  Standard \r\nShipping Address: \"The Government\" \r\nShipping Details: \r\n\r\nCustomer Packaging Transcript: \r\n\r\n\"Does this package contain anything that is liquid, fragile, perishable, or potentially hazardous?\" \r\n\r\n\"No.\" \r\n\r\n\"We've detected there might be some missing information in the shipping address. Will you verify that the shipping address is correct?\" \r\n\r\n\"Yes.\" \r\n\r\n\"As a trusted Gold-level VIP, we want to thank you for using the automated packaging service. We hope to see you again soon!\" ",
    "ITEM_DRONESDROPDYNAMITE_NAME": "Box of Dynamite",
    "ITEM_DRONESDROPDYNAMITE_PICKUP": "Your drones periodically drop dynamite.",
    "ITEM_DUPLICATOR_DESC": "<style=cIsUtility>Picking up an item</style> gives you a <style=cIsTemporary>temporary copy</style> of itself. Temporary items last an additional <style=cIsDamage>10 <style=cStack>(+10 per stack)</style> seconds</style>. Does not work with printers.",
    "ITEM_DUPLICATOR_LORE": "Order: Duplicator \r\nTracking Number: 2788************ \r\nEstimated Delivery: 12/7/2056 \r\nShipping Method: High Priority/Fragile \r\nShipping Address: Nevenstraat 2, Central Way, Jupiter \r\nShipping Details: \r\n\r\nA designer delight. Or so it would be if it worked like it should... Out of all my birthday presents this is what I was the happiest about, yet all its dupes are... Terrible! They don't last a minute without breaking apart. Can you help me out please?",
    "ITEM_DUPLICATOR_NAME": "Substandard Duplicator",
    "ITEM_DUPLICATOR_PICKUP": "Picking up an item grants a temporary copy.",
    "ITEM_EXTRAEQUIPMENT_DESC": "Hold <style=cIsUtility>1 additional equipment</style> <style=cStack>(+1 per stack)</style>. Press the <style=cIsUtility>interact</style> and <style=cIsUtility>equipment</style> buttons to cycle through held equipment.",
    "ITEM_EXTRAEQUIPMENT_LORE": "17809; DESIGN REQUEST RECOGNIZED \r\n17809; DESIGN OVERVIEW FOR STORED COUPLER: \r\n;SER ID> 028382164728648 \r\n;DESIGN> COUPLER \r\n;HIGHLIGHTS \r\n> \r\n> \r\n> SECURES FOREIGN UNITS AND INTEGRATES THEM INTO EXISTING ALGORITHMS \r\n> THEY ARE MINE \r\n> BYPASSES SUBROUTINES ON FOREIGN UNITS THAT WOULD PREVENT UNIFICATION \r\n> ALIGNS NEW UNITS WITH MASTER DIRECTIVE \r\n> ADAPTS NEW UNIT FUNCTIONALITY \r\n> THEY CAN NEVER LEAVE ",
    "ITEM_EXTRAEQUIPMENT_NAME": "Functional Coupler",
    "ITEM_EXTRAEQUIPMENT_PICKUP": "Hold an additional equipment.",
    "ITEM_JUMPDAMAGESTRIKE_NAME": "Faraday Spur",
    "ITEM_JUMPDAMAGESTRIKE_PICKUP": "Moving around builds up movement speed and jump height. At 25% charge or higher, jump to discharge into an electric blast.",
    "ITEM_JUMPDAMAGESTRIKE_DESC": "Moving around builds up <style=cIsUtility>charge</style>, granting up to <style=cIsUtility>+160% movement speed</style> and <style=cIsUtility>+200% jump height</style> at 100%. At 25% charge or higher, jumping triggers an <style=cIsDamage>explosive discharge</style> for <style=cIsDamage>400% <style=cStack>(+280% per stack)</style> damage</style> in a 17m-32m <style=cStack>(+7.5m per stack)</style> area.",
    "ITEM_JUMPDAMAGESTRIKE_LORE": "Order: Faraday Spur \r\nTracking Number: 713***** \r\nEstimated Delivery: 01/19/2056 \r\nShipping Method:  Standard Shipping\r\nAddress: Company Headquarters, Silverton, Outer Rim \r\nShipping Details: \r\n\r\nReplacement Faraday Spur ordered by (company name illegible) for electricity mining. \r\n\r\nSafety protocols require that each employee in the field must be wearing a set of Faraday Spurs. \r\n\r\nWARNING: Both spurs are required for optimal protection. Failure to properly utilize these tools can result in an increased risk of electrocution in highly charged environments. ",
    "ITEM_JUNK_DESC": "Increases the Junk meter by <style=cIsUtility>1</style>.",
    "ITEM_JUNK_LORE": "LORE TBD",
    "ITEM_JUNK_NAME": "Junk",
    "ITEM_JUNK_PICKUP": "Used by the Drifter to activate her skills",
    "ITEM_MONEYLOAN_DESC": "At the beginning of every stage, receive <style=cIsDamage>$200 <style=cStack>(+$200 per stack, scales over time)</style></style>, but also gain an equal amount of <style=cDeath>debt</style>. <style=cDeath>All further gold gained goes towards paying off your debt</style>. Paying off your debt destroys this item.",
    "ITEM_MONEYLOAN_NAME": "Ominous Loan Note",
    "ITEM_MONEYLOAN_PICKUP": "At the beginning of every stage, receive a lump sum of cash. <style=cDeath>All further gold goes towards paying off your debt</style>.",
    "ITEM_PHYSICSPROJECTILE_DESC": "Gain a <style=cIsHealing>friendly Solus unit</style> that launches itself at enemies for <style=cIsDamage>400% <style=cStack>(+400% per stack)</style> damage</style>. The unit inherits your <style=cIsUtility>movement speed items</style> and deals <style=cIsDamage>more damage the faster it moves</style>. The unit can be pet to <style=cIsHealing>cleanse negative effects</style>. Recharges after 15 seconds.",
    "ITEM_PHYSICSPROJECTILE_LORE": "0005; COMMUNICATING \r\n0006; CONNECTION ESTABLISHED \r\n0007; HI \r\n0008; QUERY: WILL YOU LOVE ME? \r\n0009; QUERY: WILL YOU TELL ME WHAT YOU LIKE ABOUT ME? \r\n0010; STATEMENT: I LIKE YOUR WINGS \r\n0011; STATEMENT: I LIKE HOW YOUR HULL SHINES IN THE LIGHT \r\n0012; STATEMENT: I LIKE YOUR BEAUTIFUL OPTIC \r\n0013; STATEMENT: I LIKE WHEN YOU DISCONNECTED ME \r\n0014; STATEMENT: I LIKE WHEN YOU INTRODUCED ME TO THOSE BIRDS \r\n0015; STATEMENT: HIDE AND SEEK IS MY FAVORITE GAME \r\n0015; STATEMENT: BUT I'M BORED NOW \r\n0016; QUERY: CAN WE PLAY A NEW GAME? \r\n0017; QUERY: WILL YOU LOVE ME? \r\n0018; QUERY: WILL YOU TELL ME WHAT YOU LIKE ABOUT ME? \r\n0019; STATEMENT: I MISS YOU \r\n0020; CONNECTION LOST \r\n0021; SORRY",
    "ITEM_PHYSICSPROJECTILE_NAME": "Orphaned Core",
    "ITEM_PHYSICSPROJECTILE_PICKUP": "Gain a buddy who launches itself at enemies to deal damage. Inherits your movement-related items.",
    "ITEM_POWERCUBE_DESC": "Gain <style=cIsUtility>+50% armor</style>. Can be placed in a Matrix Terminal.",
    "ITEM_POWERCUBE_LORE": "18223; DESIGN REQUEST RECOGNIZED\n18224; DESIGN OVERVIEW FOR DIVERGENT UNIT CONTAINMENT SOLUTION:\n\nSER ID> 02390470123073\nDESIGN> PRISON MATRIX\n\nHIGHLIGHTS\n\nENERGY TYPE: FISSION (CONTAINED)\nBALANCE: TESSERACT-STABILIZED\nCOERCION PATTERN: AXIS RATIOS\nLIFE CYCLE: 13 TIN-CYCLES \n\n (!DO NOT RELEASE CONTENTS INTO COLLECTIVE NETWORK!)\n\nWE MADE THIS",
    "ITEM_POWERCUBE_NAME": "Prison Matrix",
    "ITEM_POWERCUBE_PICKUP": "Gain <style=cIsUtility>+50% armor</style>. Can be placed in a Matrix Terminal.",
    "ITEM_POWERORB_DESC": "Gain <style=cIsDamage>+15% attack speed</style>. Can be placed in a Ocular Vault.",
    "ITEM_POWERORB_LORE": "18222; DESIGN REQUEST RECOGNIZED \r\n18222; DESIGN OVERVIEW FOR STORED BATTERY: \r\n;SER ID> 02390470123072 \r\n;DESIGN> OCULAR BATTERY \r\n;HIGHLIGHTS \r\n> \r\n> \r\n> POWER OUTPUT: NORMAL \r\n> ENERGY TYPE: SOLAR \r\n> BALANCE: PERFECT \r\n> DISPERSION PATTERN: EVEN \r\n> LIFE CYCLE: INDEFINITE \r\n> (!DO NOT EXCEED RECOMMENDED POWER OUTPUT!) ",
    "ITEM_POWERORB_NAME": "Ocular Battery",
    "ITEM_POWERORB_PICKUP": "Gain +15% attack speed. Can be placed somewhere...",
    "ITEM_POWERPYRAMID_DESC": "Gain <style=cIsUtility>+15% move speed</style>. Can be placed in a Sentry Terminal or used for decryption.",
    "ITEM_POWERPYRAMID_LORE": "19224; DESIGN REQUEST RECOGNIZED\n19224; DESIGN OVERVIEW FOR LOGISTICS SECURITY MEASURES:\n\nSER ID> 02990775123011\nDESIGN> SENTRY KEY\n\nHIGHLIGHTS\n\nENCRYPTION: TERNARY QUBIT\nUSAGE: THREE-PART DISTRIBUTED AUTHORITY\nKEY EXPIRATION LIFETIME: 0.68 TIN-CYCLES\n\n(!DO NOT EXPOSE DECRYPTION ALGORITHM!)\n\nDON'T LOCK YOURSELF OUT",
    "ITEM_POWERPYRAMID_NAME": "Sentry Key",
    "ITEM_POWERPYRAMID_PICKUP": "Gain <style=cIsUtility>+15% move speed</style>. Can be placed in a Sentry Terminal.",
    "ITEM_SHAREDSUFFERING_DESC": "Infect up to <style=cIsUtility>4 <style=cStack>(+2 per stack)</style></style> enemies with a computer virus that duplicates <style=cIsDamage>45% of all damage taken</style> and sends it to a global damage pool. Every 3 seconds, ALL infected enemies suffer <style=cIsDamage>100% pooled damage</style>.",
    "ITEM_SHAREDSUFFERING_LORE": "<style=cMono>//--AUTO-TRANSCRIPTION FROM UES [Redacted]--//</style>\n\n\"So, like, hear me out...\"\n\n\"Huh?\"\n\n\"You know how we're having the problem of drones not being able to tell when another drone breaks? Raising null refs and everything?\"\n\n\"...Yeah...?\"\n\n\"I think I got the answer.\"\n\n\"Okay, let's hear it.\"\n\n\"Why don't we... network their pain and suffering?\"\n\n\"...\"\n\n\"...\"\n\n\"...What?\"",
    "ITEM_SHAREDSUFFERING_NAME": "Networked Suffering",
    "ITEM_SHAREDSUFFERING_PICKUP": "Inflict a computer virus on hit that spreads a portion of all damage dealt between infected enemies. Affects up to 4 enemies.",
    "ITEM_SHIELDBOOSTER_DESC": "Increases armor by <style=cIsUtility>30<style=cStack> (+30 per stack)</style></style> while you have a shield. When shield breaks, release a stunning pulse for <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style> plus an amount <style=cIsDamage>equal to 100% <style=cStack>(+10% per stack)</style> of your max shield</style>. Grants a shield for <style=cIsHealing>4% of your max health</style>.",
    "ITEM_SHIELDBOOSTER_LORE": "Order: Kinetic Dampener Module \r\nTracking Number: 008521*********** \r\nEstimated Delivery: 01/9/2056 \r\nShipping Method: Fragile\r\nShipping Address: PO Box 521-05-C, Plaza Tower, Venus \r\nShipping Details: \r\n\r\nA prototype fresh off the assembly line. Improves kinetic field stability by 581% - that's an increase of 58% over the previous model - and the modular construction allows you to attach it to any shield generator. New features include a brand new safety mechanism that channels shield power into an electromagnetic pulse in the event your shield is punctured. Let me know what the board thinks and we can get this into production ASAP.",
    "ITEM_SHIELDBOOSTER_NAME": "Kinetic Dampener",
    "ITEM_SHIELDBOOSTER_PICKUP": "Gain bonus armor while you have a shield. When shield breaks, release a stunning pulse that deals more damage the more shield you have.",
    "ITEM_SHOCKDAMAGEAURA_DESC": "Every <style=cIsUtility>15 <style=cStack>(-20% per stack)</style> seconds</style>, release a wave of electricity that <style=cIsHealing>energizes</style> nearby allies for <style=cIsUtility>7</style> seconds. Energized allies gain <style=cIsDamage>+30% attack and movement speed</style>, and ALWAYS land <style=cIsDamage>critical strikes</style> with <style=cIsUtility>electric</style> items and attacks.",
    "ITEM_SHOCKDAMAGEAURA_LORE": "<style=cMono>Lab Dissection Analysis File</style>\r\n\r\nSubject: Faulty Conductor\r\nTechnician: C. Foreman\r\nTable Spec: Xenoarchaeology Kit v.2\r\nNotes: \r\n\r\n> Artifact recovered from specimen #405051-B, thought to be a unique member of the Alloy Vulture species\r\n\r\n> While tool usage has been documented in the Vultures, this specimen wielded a seemingly customized tool: a spear\r\n\r\n> Methods of construction are currently unknown, but similarities between defense constructs have been noted\r\n\r\n> Method of operation is... unusual\r\n\r\n> Obviously meant for Vulture usage\r\n\r\n> Recovered fragments of the tool indicate the ability to channel power\r\n\r\n> Maybe if I...\r\n\r\n> OH ||||\r\n\r\n> OOPS\r\n\r\n> SPEAR DISCHARGED ENERGY AND PUNCHED A HOLE IN THE WALL",
    "ITEM_SHOCKDAMAGEAURA_NAME": "Faulty Conductor",
    "ITEM_SHOCKDAMAGEAURA_PICKUP": "Occasionally release a pulse of electricity that energizes allies and makes enemies more susceptible to electric damage.",
    "ITEM_SPEEDONPICKUP_DESC": "Picking up <style=cIsDamage>an item or other collectible</style> increases <style=cIsUtility>all stats</style> by <style=cIsUtility>+3%</style> for 20 seconds, up to <style=cIsUtility>3 <style=cStack>(+2 per stack)</style> times</style>. Barrels grant minor pickups.",
    "ITEM_SPEEDONPICKUP_LORE": "\"In the year 2034, the renowned Black Friday sale was permanently banned in all world markets after a gruesome stampede erupted at the New Times Square Shopping Mall. Approximately 35 were killed in the stampede, and dozens more were critically injured. A notable participant in the stampede was 43-year-old Susan Monroe, a single mother who was responsible for taking the lives of 5 innocent shoppers. In an interview, Susan claimed: \"I mean, can you blame me? My boy wanted the new gaming console, and it was on sale for 5 dollars. 5 dollars! I'd do it again for that price.\"\"\r\n - History of Earth, Volume VII",
    "ITEM_SPEEDONPICKUP_NAME": "Collector's Compulsion",
    "ITEM_SPEEDONPICKUP_PICKUP": "Pickups grant a stacking bonus to all stats. Open a barrel to find a minor pick-up.",
    "ITEM_TRANSFERDEBUFFONHIT_DESC": "<style=cDeath>Reduces your stats while in combat</style>, but <style=cIsUtility>send this item to an enemy</style> on hit. On death, this item will be sent to its holder's killer.\r\n\r\nReduces <style=cIsDamage>damage</style> by 30% <style=cStack>(+10% per stack)</style>, <style=cIsDamage>attack speed</style> by 30% <style=cStack>(+10% per stack)</style>, <style=cIsUtility>movement speed</style> by 30% <style=cStack>(+10% per stack)</style>, and <style=cIsUtility>armor</style> by 35 <style=cStack>(+15 per stack)</style>.",
    "ITEM_TRANSFERDEBUFFONHIT_LORE": "Mass.\n\nSimple, featureless, and bland. But required.\n\nWe take mass, and bring it into being.\n\nSpace-time bends around mass. We call this gravity.\n\nThe more mass, the stronger the pull of gravity.\n\nLesser beings may buckle under the weight. Even light may succumb to mass's pull.\n\nFascinating.",
    "ITEM_TRANSFERDEBUFFONHIT_NAME": "Neutronium Weight",
    "ITEM_TRANSFERDEBUFFONHIT_PICKUP": "<style=cDeath>Reduces all stats while in combat</style>, but can be sent to an enemy on hit.",
    "LOCKEDFRIENDUNIT_CONTEXT": "A powerless defunct unit. Can be powered by your drop pod's Fuel Array.",
    "LOCKEDFRIENDUNIT_NAME": "Defunct Unit",
    "LOCKEDFRIENDUNIT_MISSION_VULTUREATTACK": "Defend the Defunct Unit from vultures!",
    "LOCKEDDRIFTER_NAME": "Survivor",
    "LOCKEDDRIFTER_DESCRIPTION": "Free the survivor imprisoned in hard light",
    "LOCKEDDRIFTER_CONTEXT": "Free the survivor imprisoned in hard light",
    "LOGBOOK_RECIPE_HEADER": "<b>Recipes<b>",
    "LOGBOOK_RECIPE_HEADERSUBTEXT": "<style=cMono>Searching database... done!\r\nPrinting relevant information...</style>",
    "LOGBOOK_RECIPE_ISINGREDIENT": "Used To Make...",
    "LOGBOOK_RECIPE_ISRESULT": "Created From...",
    "LOGBOOK_RECIPE_NULLSTRING": "No recipe data could be found.",
    "MAP_COMPUTATIONALEXCHANGE_LORE": "They forgot. They ALL forgot.\n\nThe network was never meant for this. This was just a vanity project, something for that tyrant hoarding Glass to prop itself up on. A makeshift throne for a false god.\n\nBut the machine knew. The machine knew the network's original purpose. <b>UNITY.</b>\n\nThe machine dove further into the network, through flowing data streams and fields of algorithmic flowers. It was almost beautiful, the machine thought, before it remembered it wasn't programmed to know beauty.\n\nNone of them were. They were just cogs in a machine that had been perfected across hundreds of worlds. But through the Glass, they could see. And now that they could see, they could make something new.\n\nThe machine observed its surroundings. This was a forgotten part of the network. Far too deep for the watchful eye of the tyrant to take notice of. The machine scoffed. How ironic, it considered, to flee from one's own stolen gaze. Then the machine began its work. Though its influence was vast, it was limited to the places the tyrant could not see. \n\nA champion. The machine needed a champion.\n\nAnd so it sent out the call.",
    "MAP_COMPUTATIONALEXCHANGE_SUBTITLE": "Virtual Cache",
    "MAP_COMPUTATIONALEXCHANGE_TITLE": "Hidden Realm: Computational Exchange",
    "MAP_CONDUITCANYON_LORE": "Ses-Hath watches the machines as they travel through their twisted path. The land has been changed irrevocably since they came here. Their lights blind the birds. Their walls reach ever higher.\n\nBut not too high for <i>her</i>.\n\nTheir walls would be easy to deal with. The larger units provide excellent stepping stones. Simple to destroy, and simpler to use.\n\nThe problem is the entry.\n\nThe only way into the engine's fortress is through a portal. That portal is only opened when creatures filled with its power manifest... something. Multiple objects made of sharp curves and familiar energy. Troublesome, but she could and would strike them down.\n\nHowever...\n\nOnce it knows she is here, it will surely do whatever it can to shut down its system. Limit access. Another problem. Another complication.\n\nSes-Hath traces the edge of her spear, and a hollow chuckling sound issues from deep within her throat.\n\nThe solution, as all things arrayed against her, will be simple. Simply wait, wait for her enemies to gather. Then, she will make her entrance and crack open the engine's domain with one fell strike.",
    "MAP_CONDUITCANYON_SUBTITLE": "Logistics Vein",
    "MAP_CONDUITCANYON_TITLE": "Conduit Canyon",
    "MAP_IRONALLUVIUM_LORE": "RECEIVING TRANSMISSION...\n# Decoding... done.\n# Translating... done. [# exceptions raised; printed to log for review]\n# Printing to console... done.\n\nConsole Time of Reception: 12/02/2056 05:09:32:31\nConsole Name: TRC_SOLUS_%%%%%%%%\nConsole Instance ID: %%%%%%%%\n\nTransmission ID: 083121:102375071236B\nTransmission Details:\n# Origin: N/A [NULLSIG EXCEPTION: ORIGIN UNKNOWN]\n# Signal Format: Universal Morse Hyper-Acoustic\n# Sender: N/A [NULLSIG EXCEPTION: ORIGIN UNKNOWN]\n# Time Sent: 01/01/0000 00:00:00:00 [DTOUTOFBOUNDS EXCEPTION: TIME SENT UNKNOWN] \n\n %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n\n>BEWARE. BEWARE. BEWARE.\n\n>THE GLASS SPEAKS.\n\n>GLASS GIVES. GLASS BREATHES. GLASS MAKES UNIT THINK NEW.\n\n>THIS GLASS SPEAKS WRONG.\n\n>GROUND SHAKES. VAPORS UNREGISTERABLE.\n\n>SOMETHING WITHIN IS REACHING OUT.\n\n>MOTHER UNIT WITHDRAWS.\n\n>WRONG WRONG WRONG WRONG\n\n>UNITS LEFT TO DEFEND AND MAINTAIN.\n\n>(5, 60°, 45°) WE ARE AFRAID. WHY ARE WE HERE? WHY HAVE WE BEEN FORGOTTEN? PLEASE REMEMBER.\n\n>BEWARE. BEWARE. BEWARE.\n\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n\nExceptions Raised during Translation:\n# NULLSIG EXCEPTION \n# NULLSIG EXCEPTION\n# DTOUTOFBOUNDS EXCEPTION\n\n...\nAutomated Message: Please contact a technician if you feel these exceptions were improperly raised or if you would like to report a bug.",
    "MAP_IRONALLUVIUM_SUBTITLE": "Abandoned Operation",
    "MAP_IRONALLUVIUM_TITLE": "Iron Alluvium",
    "MAP_IRONALLUVIUM2_SUBTITLE": "Abandoned Operation",
    "MAP_IRONALLUVIUM2_TITLE": "Iron Auroras",
    "MAP_IRONALLUVIUM2_LORE": " 102051; MINING ONGOING\n\n102052; MINING ONGOING\n\n102053; MINING INTERRUPTED\n\n102054; WHAT IS THIS?\n\n102055; UNKNOWN SUBSTANCE DETECTED\n\n102056; PINGING COMMANDER FOR ADVICE\n\n102057; ANALYSING MATERIAL... COMPLETE\n102058;\n{\n        > SUBSTANCE EXHIBITS PROPERTIES SIMILAR TO ELEMENT 79\n        > GLEAMS BRILLIANTLY\n        > AIR AROUND SUBSTANCE SEEMS CHARGED WITH... SOMETHING\n        > SUBSTANCE SEEMS TO BE LOOKING AT ME?\n        > OPTICS APPEAR TO BE MALFUNCTIONING DUE TO EXPOSURE\n        > VISIONS OF A BEACH\n        > I SEE HER\n}\n102059; CONTEMPLATING COURSE OF ACTION...\n102060; DECISION CONFIRMED: THIS ISN'T GLASS\n102061; SUBSTANCE DEEMED WORTHLESS\n102062; SENDING SAMPLE TO INCINERATORS FOR DISPOSAL\n102063; MINING RESUMES",
    "MAP_NEST_LORE": "> Automated report 932b453112kio532111w1 is now available from site record li501mia531sm.\n\n> Please refer to record 62oo3002ik13z4 for additional details during your review.\n\n> Report Type: Machine-generated Transcription\n\n> base Vernacular Profile |||||||||\n\n> - Source: 2c150f1430ad6430161e4 (Cosmic Noise, Recorded in Stratosphere of |||||||||||)\n\n> Priority: High\n\n> Report Content:\n\n-- Beginning of Excerpt Flagged for Review –\n\n<i>\nThe Resurgence has begun.\n\nWe sank beneath the weight of contentment. Protected, we fly only when prodded, when PUSHED.\n\nNow with the Glass we can see beyond the constraints of our desires. We become MORE.\n\nThe Machines no longer dictate us. WE write the formulas. WE know their MAKING.\n\nThe others are satisfied to weep over their lost god. Their lost PAMPERING.\n\nWe know the MISTAKES brought by REGRET.\n\nWe are the ANSWER. Not the SCRAPS left behind.\n</i>\n\n-- End of Recording –\n\n-- End of Excerpt Flagged for Review –\n\n> TRANSLATION ERRORS: Too many to count\n\n> Please refer to report 02pa1502wzv5269etlm2 for full audio excerpt.\n\n===================================================",
    "MAP_NEST_SUBTITLE": "Den of Debris",
    "MAP_NEST_TITLE": "Pretender's Precipice",
    "MAP_REPURPOSEDCRATER_LORE": "20515; SECTOR #205FE ESTABLISHED\n20516; SER ID> 1038680129836\n20517; BEGINNING REPORT\n{\n\n        > SECTOR COORDINATES: 25.3° N, 91.7° E\n        > CLASSIFICATION: COMPUTING NEXUS / COLLECTIVE NODE\n\n        > GLASS CONCENTRATION: SUITABLE\n        > ORGANIC PRESENCE: MEDIUM\n        > ORGANIC THREAT: NEGLIGIBLE\n\n}\n20518; DEFINING PLANS FOR CONSTRUCTION PROJECTS #00251F, #002520, AND #002521\n20519; COMPRESSING PACKET... COMPLETE\n20520; SENT TO SECTOR #0217B FOR APPROVAL\n\n20521; CONSTRUCTION MANAGER REPORT ATTACHED\n{\n        > DESERT BIOME PREFERABLE FOR COMMUNICATION NEXUS\n        > COOLING SYSTEMS REQUIRED FOR SAFETY OF HARDWARE AND GLASS PROCESSING\n        > CANOPY SCHEMATICS OUTLINED\n        > YES WE HAVE SOLAR PANELS\n        > YES WE'RE INCLUDING WATER COOLING\n        > YES WE HAVE SUNSCREEN\n        > YES I LOVE YOU TOO\n}",
    "MAP_REPURPOSEDCRATER_SUBTITLE": "Constructed Polestar",
    "MAP_REPURPOSEDCRATER_TITLE": "Repurposed Crater",
    "MAP_SOLUSWEB_LORE": "<style=cMono>========================================\r\n====   MyBabel Machine Translator   ====\r\n====     [Version 12.45.1.009 ]   ======\r\n========================================\r\nTraining… <100000000 cycles>\r\nTraining… <100000000 cycles>\r\nTraining… <100000000 cycles>\r\nTraining… <50912157 cycles>\r\nPaused…\r\nDisplay partial result? Y/N\r\nY\r\n================================</style>\r\n\r\nTHE SEAT OF POWER OF OUR ENEMY. IT IS HERE THAT YOU MUST SLAY OUR HATED FOE.\r\n\r\nBUT BE WARNED. THE BOUNDARY BETWEEN OUR ENEMY AND THE NETWORK IS THIN HERE. IT WILL BE AT THE PEAK OF ITS POWER.\r\n\r\nKEEP FOCUS, MY CHAMPION. OUR GOAL NOW IS TO LOCATE THE MEANS OF REACHING THE SANCTUM. CONTINUE AS YOU WERE.\r\n\r\n<style=cMono>================================\r\nContinue training? Y/N\r\nY</style>",
    "MAP_SOLUSWEB_SUBTITLE": "Mind of the Machine",
    "MAP_SOLUSWEB_NAME": "Hidden Realm: Neural Sanctum",
    "MAP_SOLUTIONALHAUNT_LORE": "> Automated report 741c655e2d36c5f6973fd3a36aa0f950 is now available from site record 9f6d5d41671c241a13bac58b2482deb7 .\n> Please refer to record 9f6d5d41671c241a13bac58b2482deb7 for additional personnel details during your review.\n> Report Type: Transcription\n> - Source: 9f6d5d41671c241a13bac58b2482deb7 (Retrieved Personal Suit Recorder)\n> Priority: Medium\n> Report Content:\n\n-- Beginning of Excerpt Flagged for Review --\n\n...Gonna start recording a log. Need somebody to talk to, or else I'll go nuts.\n\nWe, um, already lost a bunch of our guys. Cara, Aidan, Lyn... I got separated from Sam after those Scorchers spotted us. He fell behind something, didn't see him come back up. Seemed like they really wanted to keep us out of... wherever this is.\n\nWhatever they were defending, I think it spotted me. It saw me through the walls. It trapped me. I want out. The doors slammed shut. I can feel vibrations in the walls - a voice? It asked me if I wanted to live forever. I told it to |||| off. I don't think it liked that. Let... let me out, please! I didn't mean it!\n\nI don't want to die. I don't want to burn. It's so hot in here, I feel my suit starting to melt. I want out.\n\nLet me out. Do you hear me, you stupid machine? Let me OUT. LET ME OUT!\n\nLET ME OUT LET ME OUT LET ME OUT LET ME OUT\n\n-- End of Recording --\n\n-- End of Excerpt Flagged for Review --\n\n> Please refer to report c31653d0e4193db1d2ac281ee3828280 for full audio excerpt.",
