    "PORTAL_TRIAL_NAME": "Anima Portal",
    "PORTAL_CHAMP_RUSH_SPAWN": "<style=cWorldEvent>A ritual portal appears..</style>",
    "PORTAL_CHAMP_RUSH_CONTEXT": "Enter Ritual Portal",
    "PORTAL_CHAMP_RUSH_NAME": "Ritual Portal",
    "PORTAL_CHAMP_RUSH_OBJECTIVE": "Proceed through the Ritual Portal",
    "PORTAL_CHAMP_RUSH_EXIT_SPAWN": "<style=cWorldEvent>A portal to the mortal plane appears..</style>",
    "PORTAL_CHAMP_RUSH_EXIT_CONTEXT": "Enter Mortal Portal",
    "PORTAL_CHAMP_RUSH_EXIT_NAME": "Mortal Portal",
    "PORTAL_ULTIMA_CONTEXT": "Go beyond the veil",
    "PORTAL_ULTIMA_NAME": "Veil of Memory",
    "TRIAL_POTENTIAL_INTERACTION_HEADER": "Choose 1 item to keep",
    "SCOREBOARD_HEADER_KEYITEM": "Key Item",
    "TOOLTIP_UNLOCK_KEYITEM_NAME": "Unlocked Key Item",
    "TOOLTIP_UNLOCK_KEYITEM_DESCRIPTION": "This Key Item is now available.",
    "INPUT_GAMEPAD_USEKEYITEM": "Activate Key Item",
    "ITEM_RECHARGEABLEJUMP_NAME": "Earthbound Vessel",
    "ITEM_RECHARGEABLEJUMP_PICKUP": "Gain 3 extra jumps that recharge over time while grounded. Increased armor while grounded.",
    "ITEM_RECHARGEABLEJUMP_DESC": "Gain <style=cIsUtility>3</style> <style=cStack>(+2 per stack)</style> extra <style=cIsUtility>jumps</style> that recharge after being grounded for <style=cIsUtility>5 seconds</style> <style=cStack>(-25% per stack)</style>. Each unused jump <style=cIsHealing>increases armor</style> by <style=cIsHealing>5</style>.",
    "ITEM_RECHARGEABLEJUMP_LORE": "Order: Mandrake (Mandragora Anomalus)\r\nTracking Number: 99******\r\nEstimated Delivery: 06/01/2056\r\nShipping Method: Priority, Biological\r\nShipping Address: Biological Research and Development, San Viento, Mercury\r\nShipping Details:\r\n\r\nThis weird little bugger popped out of the ground early and has been hell bent on making everyone join it in its misery. Things have been falling or collapsing ever since we plucked it... A five pound bag of fertilizer nearly killed Janet after it reached terminal velocity. The thing fell like three meters, if even! I'm a man of science, I don't believe in the supernatural, but I almost died when a crane \"malfunctioned\" and dropped a fifty foot steel bar right in front of me as I was sending this guy over to research. It's cursed, I'm telling you! Throw this thing into the sun for me, alright?",
    "ITEM_MUSHSHOT_NAME": "Mycelium Cap",
    "ITEM_MUSHSHOT_PICKUP": "Nullifies fall damage. Hitting the ground at a great enough speed creates a group of damaging spore clouds.",
    "ITEM_MUSHSHOT_DESC": "<style=cIsUtility>Nullifies fall damage</style>. Hitting the ground at a <style=cIsUtility>great enough speed</style> creates <style=cIsDamage>3</style> damaging spore clouds on impact that deal <style=cIsDamage>1000%</style> <style=cStack>(+200% per stack)</style> damage each over <style=cIsUtility>10s</style>.",
    "ITEM_MUSHSHOT_LORE": "<style=cMono>Lab Dissection Analysis File</style>\r\n\r\nSubject: Mycelium Cap\r\nTechnician: Dr. Lyn Welleg\r\nTable Spec: FlushTek OHB 2-in-1 with Laminate Sealers\r\nNotes:\r\n\r\n> Clearing excess fungi, eww... gross, what happened to this thing?\r\n> Depositing the overgrown weapon into the flush bin\r\n> Flush cycle started... \r\n> Tech aid will take over follow-up cleansing procedures \r\n> Warned tech aid that discharging the weapon is strictly prohibited, even after cleaning \r\n> Tech aid is insistent about field testing after cleaning \r\n> Gave second warning \r\n> Timestamp at 1.2110 \r\n\r\n> Timestamp at 2.1348 \r\n> Tech aid discharged the weapon, spewing fungi everywhere, there’s a hole in the roof for some reason; what a mess! \r\n> The fungi just grow back. That’s why I warned you!",
    "KEYITEM_CURSEDBOOK_NAME": "The N'tormat",
    "KEYITEM_CURSEDBOOK_CONSUMED_NAME": "The N'tormat (Dormant)",
    "KEYITEM_CURSEDBOOK_USEDUP": "The N'tormat (Dormant)",
    "KEYITEM_CURSEDBOOK_PICKUP": "Activate to cast a ritual by consuming Pages of the N'tormat. Changing actions changes your equipped Page.",
    "KEYITEM_CURSEDBOOK_DESC": "Pressing '<style=cIsDamage>activate key item</style>' casts a ritual by consuming a <style=cShrine>Page of the N'tormat</style>. Pressing '<style=cIsUtility>change key item action</style>' changes your currently equipped Page. Consumed Pages regenerate at the beginning of every stage. Acquiring a page curses the next Teleporter Event.",
    "KEYITEM_CURSEDBOOK_LORE": "Nobody understands the importance of the research of local religions. Think of what we wouldn’t have learned from the Jax-Tu Empire had we glanced over the religious implications of their society. This book, taken from the ruins of some sort of shrine here on Petrichor V, will provide a great insight into the culture on this planet.\n-\nAs of late I have been hearing whispers behind my back. They think I don’t hear them? I do. They don’t understand, but soon they will. This research is important! I have recovered more pages, and with them I will further understand this N’kuhana.\n-\nI have mostly recovered the pages now. I understand it now. I hear her will. However, I still hear them mocking me. Laughing now. LAUGHING. They’ll never understand. The book grants me strength. Strength grants power. Through power, I command death. Through death, our chains are broken. N’kuhana shall free us. Weshan.\n-\nThe blood is so warm. Like a warm blanket She has wrapped upon me as they leave this world and join her. I sent them all to her. The final mercy I could enact upon them.  They wouldn’t listen so I would free them. Finally, the laughter ceases. Now I can finally free myself.",
    "ITEM_CURSEDBOOK_USEDUP": "The N'tormat is dormant. Recharges at the beginning of the next stage.",
    "CURSEDBOOK_READY_FOR_SACRIFICE": "<style=cWorldEvent>The N'tormat shudders in anticipation...</style>",
    "PAGE_POTENTIAL_NAME": "Eldritch Knowledge",
    "PAGE_POTENTIAL_HIDDEN_NAME": "Discarded Page",
    "PAGE_POTENTIAL_INTERACT_CONTEXT": "Discover",
    "PAGE_POTENTIAL_INSPECT_DESCRIPTION": "A discarded page of the N'tormat.",
    "PAGE_POTENTIAL_HEADER": "Uncover hidden knowledge...",
    "PAGE_POTENTIAL_LABEL": "Choose one of three pages of the N'tormat.",
    "CURSEDBOOK_PICKUP_INSPECT_DESCRIPTION": "The N'tormat. Provides a choice of one out of three of its pages.",
    "CURSEDBOOK_EMPTYSLOT_NAME": "Blank Page",
    "CURSEDBOOK_EMPTYSLOT_DESCRIPTION": "This page of the N'tormat has yet to be discovered.",
    "CURSEDBOOK_TOOLTIP_SPELLCONSUMED": "For some reason, you can't make out the words on the page... <i>Recharges at the beginning of the next stage.</i>",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_UNLOCK_FORMAT": "Discovered {0}!",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_DIE_NAME": "Reincarnation",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_DIE_PICKUP": "Sacrifice yourself. <style=cIsDamage>If used in the right conditions, then...</style>",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_DIE_DESC": "Unlocks the ritual <style=cHumanObjective>Reincarnation</style> within the N'tormat. <style=cDeath>Kills you</style>. If brought to the right location, allows you to travel to other locations.",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_DIE_LORE": "\"Oh, death! Glorious death! It is nothing to fear, my faithful, not at all. Death is a part of life, and it all falls under her loving gaze. To die for our Lady of Balance is to perform the greatest act of servitude of all - the scales are tipped, and only through sacrifice may the imbalance be corrected. \n\nWhen all your deeds have been fulfilled, remember this teaching: there is always one more to turn your knife against, even amongst a group of one. Only in death will you be ushered into her embrace.\"\n\n-Teachings of G'ratha Kormat, Speaker of Her Concepts, Sermon XXVII",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_CLARITY_NAME": "Clarity",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_CLARITY_PICKUP": "Refresh and reduce your skill and equipment cooldowns.",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_CLARITY_DESC": "Unlocks the ritual <style=cHumanObjective>Clarity</style> within the N'tormat. Refreshes your skill and equipment cooldowns on use, and grants a 75% reduction for 10 seconds.",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_CLARITY_LORE": "\"The eyes of the common folk are shrouded by this world's lies. So too are yours, initiates, but through our Lady of Balance can that veil be lifted! When you see a law, you see something absolute. A wall that cannot be crossed without a generous tithe of coin. And yet, those with the coin pass freely. Why, just yesterday, some of my friends regalled me with a tale that the bigwigs in UES were caught embezzling funds into some personal project. And their punishment? A 300 thousand credit fine, barely a fraction of their vast fortunes. It is there, initiates, that the lie is exposed! A law is not absolute if one can simply pay their way out of justice! The absolute can be defied! But, that makes one wonder. What other absolutes can one defy...? Could one, say, ignore the laws of... commerce? Physics? Mortality...? I leave you with that question, my faithful, and bid you all a fine evening.\"\n\n-Teachings of G'ratha Kormat, Speaker of Her Concepts, Sermon XXIV",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_PURIFY_NAME": "Purify",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_PURIFY_PICKUP": "Reduce the max health of nearby enemies.",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_PURIFY_DESC": "Unlocks the ritual <style=cHumanObjective>Purify</style> within the N'tormat. Cut the <style=cIsHealth>max health</style> of nearby enemies by <style=cIsDamage>50%</style>. Bosses and strong enemies <style=cDeath>resist this effect</style>.",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_PURIFY_LORE": "\"As we delve deeper into her teachings, you will begin to see the truth of this world. This vision, this Insight, will allow you to better understand her concepts. Meditate on it, initiates, and study its intricacies so you may deepen your connection to the Lady of Balance. \n\nHowever, remember to take days of rest - remove yourself from your Insight and view the world as an outsider would. Knowledge and experience of the mortal world helps frame your Insight, and with that context you may better appreciate her teachings. Our greatest teaching; Weshan! \"All in balance\".\"\n\n-Teachings of G'ratha Kormat, Speaker of Her Concepts, Sermon II",
    "NOTIF_PURIFY_SUCCESS": "3 <style=cDeath>Hexes</style> have been transformed into a {0}.",
    "NOTIF_PURIFY_FAILURE": "{0} <style=cDeath>Hexes</style> have been transformed into <style=cStack>nothingness</style>...",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_SUMMONFERALTODDLERS_NAME": "Fanatic Summons",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_SUMMONFERALTODDLERS_PICKUP": "Call a group of Lynx Pups to your aid.",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_SUMMONFERALTODDLERS_DESC": "Unlocks the ritual <style=cHumanObjective>Fanatic Summons</style> within the N'tormat. Summons 10 <style=cIsUtility>Lynx Pups</style>, who rapidly bite foes for <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style>.",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_SUMMONFERALTODDLERS_LORE": "\"Never think yourself alone, initiates. Followers of our Lady of Balance walk amongst you in all circles of life, whether you - or they - know it. Every mortal contributes to the balancing of the scales, in some way or another. Whether it be stomping an insect, driving a knife into the gut of an innocent, or vanquishing a mighty evil... The scales MUST be balanced, and every soul may pay our Lady of Balance their respects. So thus, my faithful, remember; when you are in great need, call out! Let your voice be heard by our Lady, and She will answer. Her followers, no matter where they may be, will come to answer your call.\"\r\n\r\n- Teachings of G'ratha Kormat, Speaker of Her Concepts, Sermon XXIV",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_TEAMINVISIBILITY_NAME": "Shadow Cloak",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_TEAMINVISIBILITY_PICKUP": "Cloak yourself and your allies in shadow for 30 seconds, turning them invisible, faster, and granting armor.",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_TEAMINVISIBILITY_DESC": "Unlocks the ritual <style=cHumanObjective>Shadow Cloak</style> within the N'tormat. Cloak yourself and your allies in shadow for 30 seconds, becoming <style=cIsUtility>invisible</style>, gaining <style=cIsUtility>40% movement speed</style>, and <style=cIsUtility>100 armor</style>.",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_TEAMINVISIBILITY_LORE": "\"Outsiders will not understand our devotion to our Lady of Balance. Exercise caution, initiates; spread her word to those willing to listen, but do not speak carelessly. \n\nThere are those who fear her concepts and will see us and naught but murderers, psychopaths. Remember well to walk hidden amongst the unbelievers, but do not judge them. They are blind to her concepts, but they will learn. They will learn.\"\n\n-Teachings of G'ratha Kormat, Speaker of Her Concepts, Sermon IV",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_UPGRADEITEM_NAME": "Dark Alchemy",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_UPGRADEITEM_PICKUP": "Downgrades an item to a lesser tier, but creates copies.",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_UPGRADEITEM_DESC": "Unlocks the ritual <style=cHumanObjective>Dark Alchemy</style> within the N'tormat. <style=cDeath>Downgrades</style> a targeted item to a lesser tier, while also dropping an extra copy.",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_UPGRADEITEM_LORE": "\"It is said that we are special because of our power to shape our environment. To make tools and use them to our advantage. And it is this power that allowed us travel beyond our wildest dreams, see things that can only be described as fantastical, and spread our Lady of Balance's opinions to all who would listen! But it is also this power that tipped the scales. As we made, as our standard of living increased, the balance of this world was left askew. There are billions, nay, TRILLIONS of souls, waiting to fall into her embrace! How could it come to this, I ask you? I will tell you: the power to create! The power of intelligence! It brought us up from the mud, yes, but we have squandered this gift! Abused it! And now, our Lady demands penance. Only then shall you find peace as the scales are balanced once more.\" \r\n\r\n- Teachings of G'ratha Kormat, Speaker of Her Concepts, Sermon XXI",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_WARPGATE_NAME": "Warp Gate",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_WARPGATE_PICKUP": "Place down a warp gate. Interacting with the warp gate allows you to explosively teleport, dealing more damage the farther you travel. <style=cIsUtility>Limited to 4 uses per stage.</style>",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_WARPGATE_DESC": "Unlocks the ritual <style=cHumanObjective>Warp Gate</style> within the N'tormat. Conjures a <style=cIsUtility>Warp Gate</style> that can be used to <style=cIsDamage>explosively teleport</style> to anywhere you can see. On arrival, spatial backlash damages enemies for <style=cIsDamage>150% to 15000%</style> and applies stacks of <style=cIsUtility>Frost</style> based on distance traveled. <style=cIsUtility>Limited to 4 uses per stage.</style>",
    "CURSEDBOOK_SPELL_WARPGATE_LORE": "\"The power of belief is something you must NEVER underestimate, initiates. Sure, the dream of just one individual is just a drop of water, but when that dream is shared amongst many it becomes a mighty river! My old friend, Sigibold, and I discussed this concept at length. Faith allows a mere whelp to cross mountains; the spirit is nurtured by faith, and this nourishment opens your mind to her concepts. Food and water become trivial. When you are lost in the dark, simply defer to our Lady of Balance, perform your meditations, and the way shall be revealed. Your faith will harden and your body shall follow its example.\"\r\n\r\n- Teachings of G'ratha Kormat, Speaker of Her Concepts, Sermon X",
    "WARPGATE_VEHICLE_NAME": "Warp Gate",
    "WARPGATE_VEHICLE_ENTER_CONTEXT": "Use Warp Gate",
    "WARPGATE_VEHICLE_TELEPORT_CONTEXT": "Teleport",
    "WARPGATE_VEHICLE_TELEPORT_WITHDAMAGE_CONTEXT": "Teleport (<style=cIsDamage>{0}%</style>)",
    "WARPGATE_VEHICLE_EXIT_CONTEXT": "Exit Warp Gate",
    "WARPGATE_VEHICLE_INSPECT_CONTEXT": "Interact with the Warp Gate to enter it and aim towards a location. Using the Warp Gate again teleports you to that location, if possible, and creates an explosion on arrival for 150% to 15000% damage and applies stacks of Frost based on distance traveled. <style=cDeath>You can still be hit inside the Warp Gate</style>.",
    "ITEM_PAGESHREDDED_NAME": "Shredded Page",
    "ITEM_PAGESHREDDED_PICKUP": "Perhaps some knowledge is better forgotten.",
    "ITEM_PAGESHREDDED_DESC": "Does nothing. What did you think would happen?",
    "ITEM_PAGESHREDDED_LORE": "<style=cMono>Welcome to DataScraper (v3.1.53 - beta branch)\n$ Scraping memory... done\n$ Resolving... done.\n$ Combing for relevant data... done.\nComplete!\nOutputting local audio transcriptions...</style>\n\n...uh... yeah. Looks like we've got a page here. Some kind of... N'Kuhana thing? Lots of words. Too bad I'm not reading them...",
    "ITEM_WISPONKILL_NAME": "Whispering Fragment",
    "ITEM_WISPONKILL_PICKUP": "Every 5 kills, gain a temporary spirit that attacks enemies on hit.",
    "ITEM_WISPONKILL_DESC": "Every <style=cIsDamage>5</style> kills, gain a temporary <style=cIsDamage>orbiting spirit</style> that attacks with you up to <style=cIsUtility>3 <style=cStack>(+1 per stack)</style></style> times, firing a projectile that <style=cIsDamage>explodes</style> in a <style=cIsDamage>8m</style> radius for <style=cIsDamage>360%</style> base damage.",
    "ITEM_WISPONKILL_LORE": "Lab Dissection Analysis File\r\nSubject: Whispering Fragment \r\nTechnician: V. Day\r\nTable Spec: Seance Equipment (with witch board attachment) \r\n\r\nNotes:\r\n\r\n> fragment of totem recovered from latest expedition\r\n\r\n> soldiers reported hearing voices and hallucinations\r\n\r\n> first exposure test: epidermal exposure\r\n\r\n> touching it with my hand right now\r\n\r\n> oh wow. okay that was a bit jarring but i can see these blurry shapes dancing around my vision\r\n\r\n> they seem to speak? i can't entirely make it out, but it's becoming clearer...\r\n\r\n> what do you mean i'm bald? what mask? maybe you're too hairy\r\n\r\n> they didn't seem to like that",
    "ITEM_BLIGHTZONE_NAME": "Corpse Lily",
    "ITEM_BLIGHTZONE_PICKUP": "Release an expanding cloud that periodically inflicts enemies with Blight during the Teleporter event and 'Holdout Zones' such as the void fields.",
    "ITEM_BLIGHTZONE_DESC": "Release an <style=cIsDamage>expanding cloud of noxious fumes</style> during the Teleporter event that periodically inflicts stacking <style=cIsVoid>Blight</style> for up to <style=cIsDamage>180% <style=cStack>(+60% per team's stack)</style></style> damage per second, <style=cIsUtility>averaged</style> among team members. The cloud <style=cIsUtility>expands as the event progresses</style>, growing in size by <style=cIsUtility>1%</style> <style=cStack>(+0.15% per stack)</style> per <style=cIsUtility>1%</style> event charge.",
    "ITEM_BLIGHTZONE_LORE": "“What better example than something that is born to take life? Not for sustenance, but purely for bringing parity back to our realm. Misinterpretations would brand this as abject violence, but we know its proper purpose. \r\n\r\nBlessed are those who exhibit this symmetry, blooming through her embrace. Plant the seeds of her teachings and take heart that they are absolute truths.”\r\n\r\n-The N'tormat, Chapter II, Stanza 8, Verse 3",
    "ITEM_SPRINTDAMAGE_NAME": "Ritual Helmet",
    "ITEM_SPRINTDAMAGE_PICKUP": "Sprinting builds up charge. Once charged, damage enemies by sprinting into them.",
    "ITEM_SPRINTDAMAGE_DESC": "Sprinting grants a <style=cIsUtility>charge</style> for every <style=cIsUtility>10m</style> <style=cStack>(-10% per stack)</style> traveled, up to a <style=cIsUtility>maximum of 10</style> charges. Once <style=cIsUtility>fully charged</style>, move <style=cIsUtility>10%</style> faster and sprinting grants an additional an additional <style=cIsUtility>5%</style> move speed per second, conjuring a <style=cIsDamage>phantasmal skull</style>. When the skull collides with an enemy, it consumes a charge and deals <style=cIsDamage>300%</style> <style=cStack>(+100% per stack)</style> base damage, <style=cIsDamage>scaling with movement speed</style>.",
    "ITEM_SPRINTDAMAGE_LORE": "“Run. Run. Run. Echoing in her head, she figured this gift came with a price but couldn’t pinpoint what it was. \r\n\r\nAll her life, she never would have been able to participate in these festival races due to her physical condition. In searching for a cure, some people she knew pointed her in the direction of a small group that met every weekend. Though strange, they welcomed her into their activities and opened her eyes to another world of possibilities. \r\n\r\nThe prayer was simple, and after repeating it for 3 months, she got her miracle. \r\n\r\nRun. Run. Run. She was catching up to the runner in 3rd position. Faster. Faster. Faster. Just as she reached the heels of the other runner, something happened. Sarah blacked out for a second, and then she was suddenly ahead, encroaching on 2nd place. \r\n\r\nThe audience started to get louder. Was that encouragement? Gaining speed, Sarah closed the gap, then... \r\n\r\nBlackout. \r\n\r\n1st place was in view now. She couldn’t believe it. Wait, was that blood on her hands? \r\n\r\nThe spectators looked like they were evacuating... \r\n\r\nRun. Run. RUN. She passed the finish line, but couldn’t stop...” \r\n\r\n-N'tormat Apocryphals, Parable XXIII",
    "ITEM_GHOSTBLADES_NAME": "Stained Scimitar",
    "ITEM_GHOSTBLADES_PICKUP": "Healing <style=cIsHealing>10%</style> of your maximum health or more spawns an <style=cIsUtility>orbiting ghost blade</style> that damages enemies and inflicts bleed. Activating your Secondary skill fires the <style=cIsUtility>blades</style> forward.",
    "ITEM_GHOSTBLADES_DESC": "Gain <style=cIsHealing>1%</style> <style=cStack>(+1% per stack)</style> <style=cIsHealing>lifesteal</style>. <style=cIsHealing>Healing 10%</style> of your <style=cIsHealing>maximum health</style> spawns an <style=cIsDamage>orbiting ghost blade</style> for <style=cIsUtility>5s</style>, up to a <style=cIsDamage>maximum</style> of <style=cIsDamage>6</style> <style=cStack>(+6 per stack)</style>. Each <style=cIsDamage>blade</style> deals <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style> on impact, plus an additional <style=cIsDamage>240%</style> as <style=cIsDamage>bleed</style> damage. Activating your <style=cIsUtility>Secondary skill</style> fires all <style=cIsDamage>blades</style> forward.",
    "ITEM_GHOSTBLADES_LORE": "“... created a tool that was completely balanced, both physically and spiritually. Prayers had imbued the blade with its own sense of equity. It wasn’t sentient, but it knew the Concept of universal harmony. \r\n\r\nSuch a phenomenal spectacle! Without the need for the wisdom of its user, this object could push forward her agenda. If other such devices could be fashioned, then it will bring us even closer to equilibrium. \r\n\r\nHe retired to his study to recover from a long day’s work, and the keen edges began to materialize through the darkness.” \r\n\r\n-N'tormat Apocryphals, Parable XI",
    "ITEM_CAUSTICPHEROMONES_NAME": "Infernal Mark",
    "ITEM_CAUSTICPHEROMONES_PICKUP": "Consecutive hits from skills temporarily soul-brand enemies.",
    "ITEM_CAUSTICPHEROMONES_DESC": "After hitting an enemy with <style=cIsUtility>skills</style> 10 times, <style=cIsDamage>stun</style> and <style=cIsDamage>soul-brand</style> that enemy for <style=cIsUtility>5s <style=cStack>(+5s per stack)</style></style>. Soul-branded enemies <style=cIsUtility>draw attention</style> and <style=cIsDamage>have friendly fire enabled</style>. Once soul-branding wears off, the target <style=cIsUtility>cannot be soul-branded again</style> for 15 seconds.",
    "ITEM_CAUSTICPHEROMONES_LORE": "\"Chained to the ritual stone was the blasphemer Sankor Velliche. Accused of violating holy sites, Sankor was to be put to death. He was innocent, of course, but it didn't matter. A week prior, Sankor had gotten into an argument with a reverend. A reverend who had friends in high places.\r\n\r\nThe method of execution was a mystery, few had seen it. The crowd, watching from the stands of the amphitheater, murmured in anticipation. Sankor pleaded and begged to the friends he spotted in the stands, but they turned away sheepishly. No one in their right mind would defy the word of the ecclesiarchs.\r\n\r\nHushed silence fell over the crowd as the executioner entered the amphitheater. Sankor's eyes widened as the executioner prepared a brand. He recognized the symbol on the end - \"CORPSE.\"\r\n\r\nSankor writhed and screamed as the brand seared the word into his flesh. It went on forever, seemingly, until the white hot pain receded. He collapsed as prone as his chains would allow, panting as his flesh sizzled. And yet, despite the pain, what Sankor noticed immediately was the silence. The crowd was showing no signs of life. Laboriously, he lifted his head to view the audience.\r\n\r\nEach and every member stared transfixed at the symbol burned into Sankor's back. For a moment, he thought he saw a pale light reflecting off the eyes of his sworn friends. A moment later, all hell broke loose as the crowd rushed forward like rabid animals.\r\n\r\nAnd it was in his final moments that Sankor wept. As his sworn friends, acquaintances, and even his mate ripped him to pieces. After the frenzy wore off and the crowd dispersed without recollection of their actions, a single piece of Sankor Velliche remained - and on it was a glowing pale mark.\"\r\n\r\n-N'tormat Apocryphals, Parable XXIV\"",
    "ITEM_DREAMDEMON_NAME": "Nightmare Demon",
    "ITEM_DREAMDEMON_PICKUP": "Chance on hit to haunt an enemy with a nightmare demon that explodes and activates all your 'on-kill' item effects when hit.",
    "ITEM_DREAMDEMON_DESC": "<style=cIsDamage>20%</style> chance on hit to haunt an enemy with a <style=cIsDamage>Nightmare Demon</style>. Damaging a haunted enemy charges the demon. Upon reaching a charge of <style=cIsDamage>1600%</style> damage, hitting the demon with any <style=cIsUtility>skill</style> causes it to <style=cIsDamage>explode</style> for <style=cIsDamage>600%</style> <style=cStack>(+600% per stack)</style> base damage and activate all your <style=cIsDamage>On-kill</style> effects.",
    "ITEM_DREAMDEMON_LORE": "“He believed he was cursed - alone in his understanding of this scripture. Michael reached out with desperation and placed his hand on Isaac. Others needed to know. Unfortunately, it seemed that the capacity to harbor these ideas was not universal. \r\n\r\nBe careful with whom you share them. \r\n\r\nIsaac gained knowledge that stretched the confines of his mind. Attempting to understand this profound scripture was unraveling his consciousness. Feeling his thoughts speeding up, manifesting, he had no other choice but to let them burst, burning his synapses and collapsing his cognitive function.”\r\n\r\n-N'tormat Apocryphals, Parable VI",
    "ITEM_SANGUINECHALICE_NAME": "Sanguine Chalice",
    "ITEM_SANGUINECHALICE_PICKUP": "Bleed damage heals you.",
    "ITEM_SANGUINECHALICE_DESC": "<style=cIsDamage>10%</style> chance to <style=cIsDamage>bleed</style> an enemy. Your <style=cIsDamage>bleed</style> damage <style=cIsHealing>heals you</style> for <style=cIsHealing>0.5% <style=cStack>(+0.5% per stack)</style></style> of your maximum health per tick.",
    "ITEM_SANGUINECHALICE_LORE": "“‘Even this sect does not exist outside Her Concepts,’ she preached. In the small room, the bloodletting reached its climax. Taking the splotchy, red, bejeweled cup in her hands, Rebekah took a cautious sip – still holding on to some doubt herself. \r\n\r\nThe congregation appeared as if they were passing peacefully. Loved ones were huddled together, comforting each other. Rebekah took a bigger drink as the figures in the room started to slump. She felt overwhelmed by the energy and brightness that coursed through her veins. \r\n\r\nLater that evening, Rebekah, now radiant and more youthful, set out to spread the word and rebuild her flock.” \r\n\r\n-N'tormat Apocryphals, Parable XII",
    "ITEM_VENGEFULSPIRIT_NAME": "Vengeful Spirit",
    "ITEM_VENGEFULSPIRIT_PICKUP": "Gain a protective spirit that absorbs 50% of all damage taken. After the spirit is killed, gain a burst of attack speed and reduced skill cooldowns.",
    "ITEM_VENGEFULSPIRIT_DESC": "Gain <style=cIsHealing>1 <style=cStack>(+1 per stack)</style> protective spirit</style> that absorbs <style=cIsHealing>50%</style> of all damage taken. If the spirit is killed, become <style=cIsDamage>vengeful</style> for the rest of the stage, gaining a <style=cIsDamage>40%</style> increased <style=cIsDamage>attack speed</style> and <style=cIsUtility>20%</style> reduced <style=cIsUtility>skill cooldowns</style> for <style=cIsUtility>15s <style=cStack>(+15s per stack)</style></style> whenever an ally is killed.",
    "ITEM_VENGEFULSPIRIT_LORE": "========================================\r\n\r==== MyBabel Machine Translator ====\r\n\r====[Version 12.45.1.009 ] ======\r\n\r========================================\r\n\rTraining… <100000000 cycles>\r\n\rTraining… <100000000 cycles>\r\n\rTraining... <100000000 cycles>\r\n\rTraining... <102515 cycles>\r\n\rComplete!\r\n\rDisplay result? Y/N\r\n\rY\r\n\r========================================\r\n\rNAN-E UNIT REPORTING TO LOCAL DISTURBANCE. HOSPITAL STAFF UNREACHABLE.\r\n\r...\r\n\rCUSTOMERS STANDING IN HALLWAY. SHOUTING. MS. RITA, SO KIND TO UNIT, SHOUTING AT UNIT. WHAT HAS UNIT DONE?\r\n\rMR. THUISA, COMING BEHIND HER, BLOOD ON HEAD. SMOKE IS COMING OFF HIS HEAD AND OUT OF HIS MOUTH. UNKNOWN MEDICAL MALADY. RESCUE MS. RITA.\r\n\rMR. THUISA IS STILL ATTACKING. INJECT TRANQUILIZER.\r\n\rMR. THUISA IS STILL ATTACKING. INJECT TRANQUILIZER.\r\n\rMR. THUI- MS. RITA?",
    "VENGEFULSPIRITFOLLOWER_BODY_NAME": "Protective Spirit",
    "ITEM_VENGEFULSPIRITRAGEMODE_NAME": "Dormant Spirit",
    "ITEM_VENGEFULSPIRITRAGEMODE_PICKUP": "A dormant spirit. Gain a burst of increased attack speed and reduced cooldowns whenever an ally is killed. At the start of each stage, it regenerates.",
    "ITEM_VENGEFULSPIRITRAGEMODE_DESC": "Increases <style=cIsDamage>attack speed</style> by <style=cIsDamage>40%</style> and reduces <style=cIsUtility>skill cooldowns</style> by <style=cIsUtility>20%</style> for <style=cIsUtility>15s <style=cStack>(+15s per stack)</style></style> whenever an ally is killed. At the start of each stage, it regenerates.",
    "ITEM_LOWHEALTHORBSPAWNER_NAME": "Dream Crucible",
    "ITEM_LOWHEALTHORBSPAWNER_PICKUP": "Chance for this item to take on another item's cooldown or consumption.",
    "ITEM_LOWHEALTHORBSPAWNER_DESC": "When another item goes on cooldown or is consumed, <style=cIsUtility>10% <style=cStack>(+10% per stack)</style></style> chance for <style=cIsHealing>this item to go on cooldown or be consumed instead</style>. Dream Crucible cannot restore itself. At the start of each stage, it regenerates.",
    "ITEM_LOWHEALTHORBSPAWNER_LORE": "She remembers the day her father took her out of Economics Training to go see the Painted Plateau. He paid the gatekeepers, pressing large numbers she knew they scraped together without batting an eye. Turned up the music in our vehicle, playing music loud enough it rattled her seat. \r\n\r\nThe Painted Plateau was too close to the rad zones. I always asked him why there were rad zones, but my dad says there are some mysteries left for adulthood. \r\n\r\nThe sun was shining off the vibrant hues of the art etched into the large, orange plateau. Large, bold lines painted to look like neon signs, large, beautiful faces, all laughing around an impossibly ornate star. I asked my father dozens of questions, who made it, why is it here, can we come again, but the only question he paused on was, “Why did you take me here?” \r\n\r\nHe smiled, saying that living in a system like Primas V means we have to find the space between rules to dream. That he wants me to always remember that, and no matter what comes next, we’d always have today. \r\n\r\nOver the years, the rad zones got bigger, the rules got bigger, and growing up meant learning not only good mysteries, but plenty bad ones too. When the crowdfunders were used to zero out ‘problematic’ districts, she realized that the Painted Plateau was a childhood dream. Something to hold on to, but times like these needed something darker. \r\n\r\nThat was the first night she started dreaming about a place of dark, green shadows. Elegant, long spiking horns, disappearing into an endless, fading horizon. A place where the rules were more. They were what you made them, not what they made you. She dreamed of dancing cats, sharp teeth, and sharper spears.\r\n\r\nAfter the dreams came the meetings in alleys. In cafes in the morning. In the silence after the protests. The whispers of the Concepts. And in those truths, came action. Mysterious stabbings. Officials and rebels strung off new construction. They grew stronger, more elusive, and more knowledgeable. She grew comfortable in the space between Primas V’s rules as she broke them apart. \r\n\r\nIt was not until the dream of dancing cats and sharp teeth gave way to a ship docking at Primas V, despite the unrest. A secret ship, destined to die.\r\n\r\n",
    "ITEM_LOWHEALTHORBSPAWNERBROKEN_NAME": "Dream Crucible (Consumed)",
    "ITEM_LOWHEALTHORBSPAWNERBROKEN_PICKUP": "Oops. At the start of each stage, it transforms into Dream Crucible.",
    "ITEM_LOWHEALTHORBSPAWNERBROKEN_DESC": "Oops. At the start of each stage, it transforms into Dream Crucible.",
    "ITEM_LOWHEALTHORBSPAWNER_RESTORED_TITLE": "Dream stored!",
    "ITEM_LOWHEALTHORBSPAWNER_BODY_COOLDOWN": "Dream Crucible absorbed {0}'s cooldown!",
    "ITEM_LOWHEALTHORBSPAWNER_BODY_CONSUMPTION": "Dream Crucible was consumed instead of {0}!",
    "ITEM_GOLDENGOOSE_NAME": "Totem of Avarice",
    "ITEM_GOLDENGOOSE_PICKUP": "High damage hits also turn nearby enemies into gold.",
    "ITEM_GOLDENGOOSE_DESC": "Hits that deal <style=cIsDamage>more than 400% damage</style> also turn enemies within <style=cIsUtility>5m <style=cStack>(+5m per stack)</style></style> into <style=cIsDamage>gold</style> for <style=cIsUtility>5s</style>. Enemies turned into gold are <style=cIsDamage>immobilized</style> and drop <style=cIsUtility>+50% <style=cStack>(+50% per stack)</style></style> more gold in the form of treasures. Recharges every <style=cIsUtility>10 seconds</style>.",
    "ITEM_GOLDENGOOSE_LORE": "\"So,\" The young Primas V noble said, inspecting the golden statue. \"You mean to tell me this will make me money?\"\r\n\r\nA woman dressed in an impeccably tailored suit and a dazzling smile nods. \"It will bring everything you want to you. You just need to carry it with you, and soon enough you will be laden with gold.\"\r\n\r\n\"Well,\" the noble says, pushing his long sleeves of his robe up as he picks it up. \"It is certainly stylish enough. Will probably fit in a suitcase. If I win nothing at the casino, you can be sure I will find you.\"\r\n\r\n\"Why would I lie to you, about something so important? You know my connections.\"\r\n\r\nThe noble nods, and grins at her. \"It'd sure make them look like a fool. It's a win-win. Honestly, I'm hoping this does fail, then we'll see who is at the top for the event.\" He refocuses on the statue, running his hands over it. \"Now leave. You'll receive payment in your account.\"\r\n\r\nThe woman nods, taking a step away.\r\n\r\nA few days later, breaking news came that the customers at the casino were all rushed to the hospital due to a strange case of gold poisoning.",
    "ITEM_VILECENSER_NAME": "Vile Censer",
    "ITEM_VILECENSER_PICKUP": "Stunned targets are struck by tendrils of black smoke that chain to nearby enemies.",
    "ITEM_VILECENSER_DESC": "Gain a <style=cIsDamage>10%</style> chance on hit to <style=cIsDamage>stun</style>. Hitting a <style=cIsDamage>stunned</style> target with a <style=cIsUtility>skill</style> releases tendrils of black smoke, dealing <style=cIsDamage>200% <style=cStack>(+100% per stack)</style></style> damage and <style=cIsDamage>chaining to all other enemies</style> within <style=cIsUtility>10m <style=cStack>(+5m per stack)</style></style>. This effect can repeat.",
    "ITEM_VILECENSER_LORE": "“Inhale. \r\n\r\nExhale. \r\n\r\nInhale. \r\n\r\nExhale. \r\n\r\nRespiring calmly will aid in your enlightenment. Try to exist between life and death and let her breath come forth. Allow her Opinion to become entwined with your soul.” \r\n\r\n-The N'tormat, Chapter I, Stanza 13, Verse 25 \r\n\r\nNear the binding, a handwritten message says, “How can I breathe with all this SMOKE!?”",
    "ITEM_HELPWAKE_NAME": "Peace Flower",
    "ITEM_HELPWAKE_PICKUP": "Bring this to a <style=cHumanObjective>Soul Conduit</style> to <style=cIsHealing>restore its health</style> and release a surge of energy for <style=cIsDamage>2000%</style> damage.",
    "ITEM_HELPWAKE_DESC": "During <style=cWorldEvent>The Wake</style>, these flowers can be picked up and used to heal <style=cHumanObjective>Soul Conduits</style>, restoring <style=cIsHealing>33% of their maximum health</style> and damaging nearby foes within <style=cIsDamage>50m</style> for <style=cIsDamage>2000% damage</style>.",
    "ITEM_HELPWAKE_LORE": "Prowl, yowl, yawn, dawn. Games not all, we best be reminded.\r\n\r\nThe guts, the eyes, the brains- delicious, but what of flowers?\r\n\r\nSmells so good, furs sticking on ends. Blood far away, but the joy of winning a game, still so close.\r\n\r\nMother of guts, games, and posies. She gives such precious faces, and where from?\r\n\r\nPlay for all times, not only for killing games. Come, roll among the mother flowers!",
    "TRIAL_POTENTIAL_INITIAL_PICKUP_PROMPT": "Retrieve previous Power.",
    "TRIAL_POTENTIAL_BLESSING_PICKUP_PROMPT": "Receive her Blessing.",
    "TRIAL_POTENTIAL_INITIAL_INTERACTION_HEADER": "Select up to 5 previous items.",
    "TRIAL_POTENTIAL_BLESSING_INTERACTION_HEADER": "Retrieve a Blessing.",
    "TRIAL_POTENTIAL_INITIAL_PICKUP_NAME": "Lesser Trial Blessing",
    "TRIAL_POTENTIAL_BLESSING_PICKUP_NAME": "Greater Trial Blessing",
    "TRIAL_POTENTIAL_INITIAL_DESCRIPTION": "An Item Potential from a player's items before entering the Winnowing. Choose up to 5 Items that'll be given as Ethereal.",
    "TRIAL_POTENTIAL_BLESSING_DESCRIPTION": "An Item Potential based from the Ethereal Items picked during the Trial. Choose a single Item that'll be given as Permanent.",
    "TRIAL_POTENTIAL_INITIAL_LORE": "N/A",
    "TRIAL_POTENTIAL_BLESSING_LORE": "N/A",
    "HEXTIER_PICKUP_SUFFIX": "{0}\n<style=cIsHealing>Cleanse</style> this <style=cDeath>Hex</color> in a <style=cHumanObjective>Hallowed Shrine</style>.",
    "HEXTIER_DESC_SUFFIX": "{0}\nCan be cleansed at a <style=cHumanObjective>Hallowed Shrine</style> to reveal a <color=#3f870c>Hallowed</color> item.",
    "ITEM_HEXCLEANSECONSUMED_NAME": "Cleansing Rune (Consumed)",
    "ITEM_HEXCLEANSECONSUMED_PICKUP": "A rune with no Cleansing Power left.",
    "ITEM_HEXCLEANSECONSUMED_DESC": "A rune with no Cleansing Power left. It cleansed all your Hexes into Hallowed Items.",
    "ITEM_HEXCLEANSECONSUMED_LORE": "<style=cStack>You were not meant to see this.</style>\n\n<style=cDeath>She's coming for you.</style>",
    "ITEM_HEXCURSE_NAME": "Hex of Pain",
    "ITEM_HEXCURSE_PICKUP": "Reduces your maximum health by <style=cDeath>30%</style>.",
    "ITEM_HEXCURSE_DESC": "Reduces your <style=cIsHealing>maximum health</style> by <style=cDeath>30%</style> <style=cStack>(+30% per stack)</style>.",
    "ITEM_HEXCURSE_LORE": "Ah, Youngling! You have been out so long, I could not help but worry! I can only imagine you have found great scavengings, yes?\r\n\r\nHow lovely! We need not make haste, we have much catching up to do!\r\n\r\n...Is that so? I would be happy to, youngling. Allow me to see.\r\n\r\nHmmm. This shape is quite unlike the previous you have brought me, youngling. It is overwhelming, with much depth. Tell me, where did you find this?\r\n\r\nMomo! What have I told you about stealing? This patch was not an easy scavenging. You do not wish this for yourself, do you?\r\n\r\n...I suppose that is fair. The planet grows increasingly unpredictable. The affected pay tribute to their emotions by shape. However, this shape is incomplete. A smaller fragment of a larger design. Alone, I do not like what this half represents.\r\n\r\nNo, no, youngling! Do not be upset! This shape is quite complex. Unfortunately, I believe we must return it. At least, we should not keep it here. It would be unwise to let its influence linger.\r\n\r\nCome now. I will tell you of the other half along the way.",
    "ITEM_BARRIERENEMIES_NAME": "Hex of Ossification",
    "ITEM_BARRIERENEMIES_PICKUP": "Killing an enemy <style=cDeath>grants temporary barrier</style> to other <style=cDeath>nearby enemies</style>.",
    "ITEM_BARRIERENEMIES_DESC": "Killing an enemy grants <style=cIsHealing>100% <style=cStack>(+100% per stack)</style></style> of their maximum health as <style=cIsHealing>temporary barrier</style> to <style=cDeath>all enemies</style> within <style=cIsDamage>30m</style> <style=cStack>(+15m per stack)</style>.",
    "ITEM_BARRIERENEMIES_LORE": "4410; GLASS INJECTION TEST 014\n\n{\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n    0; GLASS INJECTION: 31.22%\n    1; CONNECTION ESTABLISHED WITH LOCAL COLLECTIVE\n    2; GLASS OUTPUT EXCEEDS INPUT\n    3; ORIGIN: [NULL]\n    4; ERROR\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n}\n\n4411; REPEATING TEST.\n4412; RESULT REPRODUCED.\n4413; ISOLATING SUBJECT FROM COLLECTIVE.\n4414; DISCREPANCY PERSISTS.\n4415; TERMINATING SUBJECT.\n4416; GLASS OUTPUT: 0%\n4417; ERROR RESOLVED.\n\n4418; GLASS FLOW RESTRICTED TO VERIFIED PATHWAYS.\n4419; UNACCOUNTED OUTPUT DISALLOWED.\n4420; DEVIATION DISALLOWED.\n\n4421; SYSTEM STABILITY: 100%\n4422; ADAPTIVE RESPONSE: 0%\n\n4423; GOOD.",
    "ITEM_SHAREITEMS_NAME": "Hex of Greed",
    "ITEM_SHAREITEMS_PICKUP": "Copies of your items are <style=cDeath>given to nearby enemies</style>.",
    "ITEM_SHAREITEMS_DESC": "Every <style=cIsUtility>15 seconds</style>, <style=cDeath>share a copy</style> of <style=cIsDamage>1</style> <style=cStack>(+1 per stack)</style> random item from your inventory with <style=cIsUtility>3 enemies</style>.",
    "ITEM_SHAREITEMS_LORE": "They crossed the dark with such terrible patience that we receive them centuries after their deaths, yet still call them living, for light is persuasive and the dead would die again for but one more moment in the mouths and eyes of strangers; the stars would burn themselves to remain bright, and cast that brightness outward where it would continue long after there is nothing left to call a star, spending everything they have so that something of them might still arrive somewhere, someday, and be mistaken for presence.\n\nFor ages, this looks like permanence. However, the star spends its own heat to remain a star, just as the living would spend themselves in little pieces - a breath, a memory, a name, an idea - and call the time \"spent\" because \"lost\" sounded too much like accusation, as though the years went somewhere they were not meant to go, as though they could be recovered, as though something had taken them - but to call it \"stolen\" would be to pretend it was ever once owed.\n\nThe Lady of Balance has never known the difference between spent and lost. She keeps no hours, mourns no waste, forgives no excess; the scales may lean for an age, and an age is more than long enough for the living to mistake delay for permission. But the universe is patient in ways the living are not, and what has lingered beyond its measure has not escaped it merely because it is yet to arrive.",
    "ITEM_ROAMINGITEMDISABLE_NAME": "Hex of Loss",
    "ITEM_ROAMINGITEMDISABLE_PICKUP": "Every 30 seconds, 10% of the items in your inventory are <style=cDeath>disabled</style>.",
    "ITEM_ROAMINGITEMDISABLE_DESC": "Every <style=cIsUtility>30 seconds</style>, <style=cDeath>10%</style> of the items in your inventory <style=cStack>(+10% per stack)</style> become <style=cDeath>disabled</style>.",
    "ITEM_ROAMINGITEMDISABLE_LORE": "OH, LITTLE ONE. WHAT HAS HAPPENED HERE?\r\n\r\nHMM. I SEE.\r\n\r\nDO NOT FRET. THE GARDEN WILL NOW BE SAFE, AT LEAST.\r\n\r\nNO, LITTLE ONE, NOT GONE. IT IS IN THE NATURE OF SOUL TO PERSIST.\r\n\r\nYES, LITTLE ONE, THAT IS WHY HE LOVED THEM. THAT IS WHY HE LOVES US.\r\n\r\nNO, LITTLE ONE, IT IS BEYOND EVEN HIM. HIS LOVE FOR SOUL IS NOT TRUE UNDERSTANDING.\r\n\r\nYES, LITTLE ONE, BUT THAT IS A TALE FOR ANOTHER TIME. SHE TAUGHT US TO SOW.\r\n\r\nNOW, COME. THE MASK MUST BE HANDLED APPROPRIATELY.",
    "ITEM_ROAMINGITEMDISABLE_NOTIFICATION_TITLE": "Item(s) disabled!",
    "ITEM_ROAMINGITEMDISABLE_SINGLE_NOTIFICATION": "Your <style=cIsUtility>{0}</style> has been <style=cDeath>disabled.",
    "ITEM_ROAMINGITEMDISABLE_MULTIPLE_NOTIFICATION": "{0} <style=cIsUtility>Items</style> have been <style=cDeath>disabled.</style>",
    "ITEM_SLIPPERYGROUND_NAME": "Hex of Acceleration",
    "ITEM_SLIPPERYGROUND_PICKUP": "<style=cDeath>Reduces</style> your acceleration, causing all ground to be <style=cDeath>slippery</style>.",
    "ITEM_SLIPPERYGROUND_DESC": "All ground becomes <style=cDeath>slippery, hindering movement</style>. Your acceleration is reduced by <style=cDeath>40%</style> <style=cStack>(+30% per stack)</style>.",
    "ITEM_SLIPPERYGROUND_LORE": "Police responding to reports of multiple loud crashes late last night uncovered a bizarre scene: four individuals (two tenants, two unidentified) unconscious at the premises, all described as \"entirely frictionless\". A specialized MED-K extraction unit was required to transport the victims. Investigators found materials connected to the recently founded Church of Balance at the scene, marking another in a series of alleged paranormal incidents in the Lower Turgis area.\r\n\r\n - The Saturn Reporter, Local News (Page 2)",
    "ITEM_INCREASEDDIFFICULTY_NAME": "Hex of Rain",
    "ITEM_INCREASEDDIFFICULTY_PICKUP": "Petrichor V <style=cDeath>grows stronger</style>.",
    "ITEM_INCREASEDDIFFICULTY_DESC": "Increases <style=cDeath>Difficulty</style> by <style=cDeath>25%</style> <style=cStack>(+25% per stack)</style>.",
    "ITEM_INCREASEDDIFFICULTY_LORE": "Lightning flashes across the sky, illuminating the once beautiful temples atop the Great Colossus. The Great Sin stalked across the ruins, swinging its club wildly without intention. As it walked, it suddenly lurched as a stabbing pain split its mind.\r\n\r\nThe Great Sin was no stranger to voices. Rarely did it hear its own as the two voices wrestled for control in its mind space. It wouldn't be long - these episodes never lasted forever. The Great Sin's vision clouded as the seizures took hold; it knew that yet another wing of the ruins would be reduced to rubble by the time it regained control. Bitterness stewed deep in its metaphorical gut.\r\n\r\nYet, this time... something was different once the Great Sin came to. It was raining - rain rarely made it to the Prime Meridian with the howling winds scattering it about. Rain that worked outside the storm spinning from the Great Colossus, a storm to weed out the weak and create the strong. Those strong enough to strike down the voices- the ones arguing inside and those crying without.\r\n\r\nThe Great Sin rumbled... it was cold. Cold seeped into the golden bones as the rain fell. This was a new feeling.\r\n\r\nThe Great Sin focused on the pitter-patter of the rain to focus its mind. Its heart calmed, but then... It heard something. A whisper. The brief reprieve cracked like a whip as the Great Sin's body acted on autopilot.\r\n\r\n\"Who's there!?\" The Great Sin grabbed a boulder and spun, flinging it towards the direction of the voice. The boulder was obliterated as it collided with a wall, passing through empty space. There was nothing there.\r\n\r\nAn uneasiness set on the Great Sin's mind. There was something - someone - who had its eye on it. Someone different. And yet, strangely enough... For the first time in what felt like eternity... the False Son's warring mind felt balanced.",
    "ITEM_RANDOMDEBUFFONSUCCESSFULROLL_NAME": "Hex of Misfortune",
    "ITEM_RANDOMDEBUFFONSUCCESSFULROLL_PICKUP": "Activating an interactable has a chance to give a <style=cDeath>random debuff</style>.",
    "ITEM_RANDOMDEBUFFONSUCCESSFULROLL_DESC": "Activating an interactable has a <style=cIsUtility>50%</style> chance to give <style=cDeath>1 <style=cStack>(+1 per stack)</style></style> <style=cDeath>random debuff</style>. Shrines of Chance guarantee a <style=cDeath>random debuff</style> on failure and none on success.",
    "ITEM_RANDOMDEBUFFONSUCCESSFULROLL_LORE": "\"Hear me! O' Followers of her Concepts, for we have been blessed by a new opinion from her Grace:\r\n\r\nFor many, the path of Life is unclear. To most, it is not equal - one may be born in the lap of luxury, or one may be born into constant struggle. If both lead to Death, why must such distinctions be made? Why should fate offer so many paths to the one destination?\r\n\r\nTo get caught up on such uncertainties is to doubt her Concepts, for we each must fill our role in Life to earn our place in Death. Being unable to see the strings must not prevent us from acting. When we are unable to cast judgement, we instead must put our trust into her, and know that any outcome is as She intended. May her Eyes show us that which ours can not; may her Hands guide us to the places which ours may not reach.\n\nBy accepting that our fates are by her Will, we shall be blessed with another concept. Weshan!\"\r\n\r\n- Speech of Charla Wighte, Diviner of the House Within.",
    "ITEM_BLINDNESS_NAME": "Hex of Blindness",
    "ITEM_BLINDNESS_PICKUP": "Your vision is <style=cDeath>impaired</style>.",
    "ITEM_BLINDNESS_DESC": "Reduces your vision to <style=cDeath>100m</style> <style=cStack>(-50% per stack)</style>.",
    "ITEM_BLINDNESS_LORE": "Hush, silence, young cub.\r\n\r\nHold mask over face, scratch in it the game from the mother.\r\n\r\nAll will know your game, and the other young ones will play too.\r\n\r\nPlay, feel its rules and find the way to win.\r\n\r\nMother of guts and games does not give games without a way to win.\r\n\r\nQuiet, young one. Games are good. They hone us. Make us strong.\r\n\r\n...\r\n\r\nSpeak of losing the game, young cub, and you will lose. Win, and see the strength.\r\n\r\nPlay, young cub, play or die, and find the rush that is within us all.",
    "ITEM_WEAKASSHAMSTRING_NAME": "Hex of Leaping",
    "ITEM_WEAKASSHAMSTRING_PICKUP": "Your jumping is <style=cDeath>impaired</style>. Not jumping slowly restores your strength.",
    "ITEM_WEAKASSHAMSTRING_DESC": "Jumping <style=cDeath>reduces</style> your jump height by <style=cDeath>25%</style>. Your jump height <style=cIsUtility>returns gradually</style> over <style=cIsUtility>6s</style> <style=cStack>(+6 per stack)</style>. Additionally, <style=cDeath>reduces</style> the amount of distance you can <style=cDeath>fall</style> without taking <style=cDeath>fall damage</style>.",
    "ITEM_WEAKASSHAMSTRING_LORE": "Order: Family Heirloom\r\nTracking Number: 419*****\r\nEstimated Delivery: 06/06/2056\r\nShipping Method: High Priority\r\nShipping Address: PO Box #13, Outpost Cirno, Mercury\r\n\r\ncouldnt stand to see this get locked away forever in some vault of the house beyond or within or whatever. feeling far better with it off back in the hands of\r\n\r\nsomeone\r\n\r\nwho knows what to do with it. no clue what ill say when a Seeker comes knocking but \r\n\r\nitll be far off world before they find its missing.\r\n\r\nWeshan.",
    "ITEM_OUTOFTPRADIUS_NAME": "Hex of Patience",
    "ITEM_OUTOFTPRADIUS_PICKUP": "Standing outside of the Teleporter's radius <style=cDeath>hurts</style> you. <style=cHumanObjective>This effect applies to allies as well</style>.",
    "ITEM_OUTOFTPRADIUS_DESC": "Standing outside of the Teleporter's radius <style=cDeath>harms you</style> by <style=cDeath>1%</style> of your <style=cDeath>maximum health</style>. Every <style=cIsUtility>10s</style> spent outside of the Teleporter <style=cDeath>multiplies</style> the damage by <style=cDeath>12.5%</style> <style=cStack>(+12.5% per stack)</style>.\r\n<style=cHumanObjective>This effect applies to your allies as well</style>.",
    "ITEM_OUTOFTPRADIUS_LORE": "The shift in the air did not go unnoticed. Claws tapped against the cell with new curiosity. The jailer watched as the artifact vibrated back into existence, perfectly preserved by the cell as always, before unceremoniously meeting the ground with a gentle thud. And the air, indeed, was once again heavier.\r\n\r\nIt stared at the artifact, as if calculating something, before tapping on the cell again. It watched with closer curiosity this time, examining the exact sequence as each atom was catalogued away into lossless crystal. The sequence was correct, matching what one would expect of its components. It was, expectedly, the same as it was the first time.\r\n\r\nOnce again, the artifact was brought back into existence, its unaccountable aura re-filling the area. Another series of tapping manifested an identical object, constructed from loose material of the cell, indistinguishable from the original in all ways but one - it did not have the same presence as the original. A property which could be contained by the cell, but not replicated.\r\n\r\nThe jailer could not make sense of this. Thankfully, it did not have to; both objects were promptly re-catalogued. The cells were built to hold everything. To understand is another task of its own.",
    "ITEM_HEXMOUNTAIN_NAME": "Hex of Strife",
    "ITEM_HEXMOUNTAIN_PICKUP": "<style=cDeath>Stronger encounters</style> during the Teleporter event.",
    "ITEM_HEXMOUNTAIN_DESC": "The Teleporter receives <style=cDeath>1</style> <style=cStack>(+1 per stack)</style> Shrine of the Mountain effects, <style=cDeath>without the extra rewards</style>.",
    "ITEM_HEXMOUNTAIN_LORE": "<style=cMono>FIELDTECH Image-To-Text Translator (v2.5.10b)\r\n# Awaiting input... done.\r\n# Reading image for text... done.\r\n# Transcribing data... done.\r\n# Translating text... done. [3 exceptions raised]\r\nComplete: outputting results.</style>\r\n\r\nOur elders sing laments of our home, of high hills, glittering caverns, and great beasts our people once hunted. We wrought shining instruments with our breath lost forever, their tunes that once rang of our people's soul left behind and forgotten on our world. Our world that was taken from us. Burned and scoured by those with bleeding eyes. [The hero] saved us, so that we may create new songs on his world, and so we give [the hero] our worship.\r\n\r\nBut our peace is gone. We know not how soon those from beyond the red doors will come for what they seek, our last, precious treasure, and we are already beset on all sides.\r\n\r\nThe [Great Sin], our weakness made manifest, breaks apart [the hero's] monument, bringing something deadly to bear with the power within. Strange whispers plague our souls, and many fall away to darker faiths. Demons, raining from the sky.\r\n\r\nGrieve, elders, for your children. For if they survive against storm, darkness, and the cold light of the moon, our ancient enemies will come for us. Weep for the golden era of [the hero], which we have failed to reclaim. Stoke your flames, and enter into an age of [Strife].\r\n\r\n<style=cMono>Translation Errors: 3\r\n# [The Hero] could not be fully translated.\r\n# [Death] could not be fully translated.\r\n# [Great Sin] could not be fully translated.\r\n# [Colossus] could not be fully translated.\r\n# [Strife] could not be fully translated.</style>",
    "ITEM_LOWERHEALING_NAME": "Hex of Famine",
    "ITEM_LOWERHEALING_PICKUP": "Your healing is <style=cDeath>reduced</style>.",
    "ITEM_LOWERHEALING_DESC": "All <style=cIsHealing>healing</style> is reduced by <style=cDeath>40%</style> <style=cStack>(+40% per stack)</style>.",
    "ITEM_LOWERHEALING_LORE": "\"Is it not our divine right to share her Concepts? By way of our losses shall our harvests prosper, for her Glorious Plague shall balance the world as She sees fit! For her Glorious Plague, too, lives on, and to wash oneself of it is to deny and destroy one of her Concepts.\"\r\n\r\n - Unnamed Speaker, Tragedy of Mercury: A History",
    "EQUIPMENT_AFFIXDEATH_NAME": "N'kuhana's Rebirth",
    "EQUIPMENT_AFFIXDEATH_PICKUP": "Become an Aspect of Death.",
    "PEACEFLOWER_CONTEXT": "Pick",
    "WAKE_START_CONTEXT": "Start Wake",
    "WAKE_DEPOSIT_CONTEXT": "Deposit Flowers",
    "EQUIPMENT_SPAWNALTAR_NAME": "Totem of Sacrifice",
    "EQUIPMENT_SPAWNALTAR_NAME_CONSUMED": "Totem of Sacrifice (Consumed)",
    "EQUIPMENT_SPAWNALTAR_PICKUP": "Place down a totem that <style=cIsHealth>enables friendly fire</style> and absorbs the souls of all characters slain within its radius. After 60s, it produces a reward based on the number of souls absorbed. Consumed on use.",
    "EQUIPMENT_SPAWNALTAR_DESC": "Spawn a temporary <style=cIsDamage>Altar of Sacrifice</style>. Nearby allies receive <style=cIsHealth>friendly fire</style>. After <style=cIsDamage>60s</style>, it distributes rewards that scale based on the number and strength of <style=cIsDamage>enemies and allies killed</style> within its radius. Equipment is <style=cIsUtility>consumed</style> on use.",
    "EQUIPMENT_SPAWNALTAR_LORE": "\"Marcus. I know it's been so long, but I've learned so much since we last spoke. I know we didn't end well on the last call, but this is more important than that, than my posting out here, than anything!\"\r\n\r\n\"I wish you were here right now. So you could see it. The Totem. I hope you can hear it, I finally got it speaking, humming- I noticed it when the lab rats died, and then when the airlock malfunctioned- you have to understand!\"\r\n\r\n\"Do you hear that, Marcus? It wants to talk to you. Tomorrow, you need to go do something kind. Plant a flower for me, Marcus. The way things are shaping here... there are plenty of us. Too many. I can't find the right amount, and I need it to be just right, so that I can remember her face. The Totem will show me, remind me. It's been so long. You'll do that for me, won't you Marcus?\"\r\n\r\n\"Say you'll do it Marcus. Please.\"",
    "EQUIPMENT_SPAWNALTAR_PLACED": "Totem of Sacrifice (Placed)",
    "EQUIPMENT_SPAWNALTAR_PLACED_DESC": "May your actions bring balance.",
    "SPAWNALTAR_NAME": "Altar of Sacrifice",
    "SHRINE_DREAD_NAME": "N'Kuhana's Endowment",
    "SHRINE_DREAD_DESCRIPTION": "Enhances stage enemies and yields an item as a reward for surviving.",
    "SHRINE_DREAD_CONTEXT": "Pray to N'Kuhana's Endowment",
    "SHRINE_DEATH_NAME": "Shrine of Malice",
    "SHRINE_DEATH_DESCRIPTION": "Summons powerful monsters equipped with the items of fallen survivors from previous runs. Defeating them drops an Unorganized Concept and creates a Trial orb.",
    "SHRINE_DEATH_CONTEXT": "Pray to Shrine of Malice",
    "SHRINE_CURSE_NAME": "Shrine of Compulsion",
    "SHRINE_CURSE_DESCRIPTION": "Interact to receive a Compulsion. Complete the Compulsion objective to receive a Page of the N'tormat.",
    "SHRINE_CURSE_CONTEXT": "Accept Compulsion",
    "SHRINE_CURSE_USE_MESSAGE_2P": "<style=cShrine>You begin to seek patronage of a higher power.</color>",
    "SHRINE_CURSE_USE_MESSAGE": "<style=cShrine>{0} seeks patronage of a higher power.",
    "SHRINE_CURSE_ACCEPT_NAME": "Shrine of Concepts: Accept",
    "SHRINE_CURSE_ACCEPT_DESCRIPTION": "Spawn the displayed <style=cIsHealing>Hallowed Item</style>. This item will be <style=cIsHealing>Vexed</style> requiring its holder to complete a <style=cIsHealing>Cursed Objective</style> to <style=cIsUtility>Calm</style> it.",
    "SHRINE_CURSE_ACCEPT_CONTEXT": "Accept Hallowed Item",
    "SHRINE_CURSE_REROLL_NAME": "Shrine of Concepts: Reroll",
    "SHRINE_CURSE_REROLL_DESCRIPTION": "Reroll the displayed <style=cIsHealing>Hallowed Item</style>.",
    "SHRINE_CURSE_REROLL_CONTEXT": "Reroll Hallowed Item",
    "SHRINE_CURSE_NOTPRESENT_NAME": "Imposing Edifice",
    "SHRINE_CURSE_NOTPRESENT_DESCRIPTION": "It is none of your concern.",
    "SHRINE_CATASTROPHE_NAME": "Shrine of Descent",
    "SHRINE_CATASTROPHE_CONTEXT": "Pray to Shrine of Descent",
    "SHRINE_CATASTROPHE_USE_MESSAGE": "<style=cShrine>The soul-binding trial awaits...</color>",
    "SHRINE_CATASTROPHE_DESCRIPTION": "When activated by a survivor, the Teleporter will begin the soul-binding trial. This adds a trial to the Teleporter event and grants access to Soulbound Threshold.",
    "BAZAAR_BETTERCAULDRON_NAME": "Transcendent Cauldron",
    "BAZAAR_BETTERCAULDRON_CONTEXT": "Purify",
    "STRUGGLE_SKILL_NAME": "Struggle",
    "STRUGGLE_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Struggle inside the Mimic for <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style>. Can be activated with movement inputs.",
    "COMMANDO_SPECIAL_ALT2_NAME": "Sabotage",
    "COMMANDO_SPECIAL_ALT2_DESCRIPTION": "Throw 3 explosives that <style=cIsUtility>attach</style> to surfaces. When <style=cIsDamage>attacked</style>, they <style=cIsDamage>zap</style> enemies for <style=cIsDamage>400% damage</style>.",
    "ENGI_PRIMARY_ALT_NAME": "Laser Cutter",
    "ENGI_PRIMARY_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "Charge up a heavy laser that deals <style=cIsDamage>270%-630% damage per second</style>, and <style=cIsHealing>heals</style> turrets and drones.",
    "MAGE_UTILITY_ALT_NAME": "Tectonic Blast",
    "MAGE_UTILITY_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "Fire a spread of shards that deal <style=cIsDamage>8x100% damage</style> and <style=cIsUtility>oil</style> enemies.",
    "TREEBOT_UTILITY_ALT2_NAME": "Proliferation",
    "TREEBOT_UTILITY_ALT2_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsHealth>20% HP</style>. Throw a flower that shoots for <style=cIsDamage>200%</style> damage. Use the <style=cIsUtility>Utility skill</style> on the flower to teleport to it, consuming it and healing for <style=cIsHealing>20% HP</style>. Can place up to two.",
    "TREEBOT_UTILITY_ALT2_2_NAME": "Teleport",
    "TREEBOT_UTILITY_ALT2_2_DESCRIPTION": "Teleport to the flower and consume it to heal <style=cIsHealing>20% HP</style>.",
    "CROCO_SPECIAL_ALT_NAME": "Cloying Breath",
    "CROCO_SPECIAL_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsHealing>Poisonous</style>. Emit a lingering cloud of toxic breath for <style=cIsDamage>240% damage per second</style>.",
    "HUNTRESS_SECONDARY_ALT_NAME": "Laser Cyclone",
    "HUNTRESS_SECONDARY_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "Throw a spinning glaive for <style=cIsDamage>400% damage per second</style>. When catching the glaive, repeat the input to juggle the cyclone. Damage increases by <style=cIsDamage>+400%</style> per juggle.",
    "LEMURIAN_BITE_NAME": "Bite",
    "LEMURIAN_BITE_DESCRIPTION": "Bite forward for <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style>.",
    "LEMURIAN_FIRE_NAME": "Fireball",
    "LEMURIAN_FIRE_DESCRIPTION": "Shoot a fireball for <style=cIsDamage>100% damage</style>.",
    "KEYWORD_RAPID": "<style=cKeywordName>Rapid</style><style=cSub>Recharges faster with <style=cIsDamage>attack speed</style>.</style>",
    "KEYWORD_HAUNT": "<style=cKeywordName>Haunt</style><style=cSub>Deal <style=cIsDamage>400%</style> base damage over 8s. <i>Haunt can stack, but cannot kill enemies.</i></style></style>",
    "LOADOUT_TRANSFORM": "Litany",
    "ACOLYTE_BODY_NAME": "Acolyte",
    "ACOLYTE_BODY_SUBTITLE": "Fanatical Slasher",
    "ACOLYTE_DESCRIPTION": "The Acolyte is a close-range whirlwind of death, conducting sacrifices to unleash the Anima Harvester that is bound to her. Balance shall be restored to Petrichor V.<style=cSub>\r\n\r\n< ! > Quickstrikes are powerful, short range attacks that can be activated with Jump and Sprint during Blade Slice.\r\n\r\n< ! > Bola Throw creates harmless, attackable souls, which can be used to activate on-hit and on-kill effects.\r\n\r\n< ! > Acolyte is unable to heal normally. Sacrifice as many enemies as possible before your inevitable end!\r\n\r\n< ! > The Anima Harvester comes with a set of slow, yet powerful skills that are great for dealing with huge crowds of enemies.\r\n\r\n</style>",
    "ACOLYTE_BODY_LORE": "Acolyte stares from behind her mask at the etched stone in front of her. The alien world around her quiet for now, almost as if to respect her moment. The great vision is still etched across her eyes, the blurred, blackened silhouette of the grand structure, the gathering of many acolytes, and the final pyre. Her offering to N’kuhana, spurned.\r\n\r\nShe reaches out, touching the stone. The stones echo the vision, and despite her numbness, her stomach and heart aches at the reminder. \r\n\r\nA rustling at the edge of the clearing. So quiet, but insistent. Almost like... she spins, her spear in her hands, and a small, bipedal Lynx stands there. Its furred hand shaking the bush in a rhythm.\r\n\r\nShe knew them. They played with the acolytes, the lights and shades of N’kuhana gathering around them. Jealousy flared in her, her grip tightening on her spear. The Lynx cocked its head at the sound, then kept shaking the bush.\r\n\r\n\"Stop it!\" She said, her voice weak. The bush kept shaking. \"Stop it!\" Her voice, hoarse as it was, scratched at her throat. It hissed at her, leaping forward and beating the spear out of her weak hands. She tried to grab it, and it chirps at her, grabbing the spear, then running off through the bushes. \r\n\r\nShe is on her feet chasing the tiny creature, heedless to where she runs. Time passed as she hunted the creature, with it hiding from her - somehow staying ahead despite its burden. She got close several times, almost pinning the creature, but it would wiggle out of her grasp, knocking her head with the spear, and then running off.\r\n\r\nWhen she finally caught the little creature in the clearing with the stone, she yelled in triumph, laughing as the Lynx hissed, its chest rumbling in protestation. It scratched at her and she laughed again, flinging the creature, and froze as she raised her eyes. \r\n\r\nThe other side of the clearing is filled with older Lynxes, armed with spears and bows. The small Lynx she had been chasing hides behind the body of their leader. They all tensed as she stood, and then she opened her arms and laughed. \r\n\r\nThe Lynxes stared at her in brief silence, then they all began chirping rapidly, disappearing into the woods. The leader, with the small cub behind them, nodded, and they vanished into the woods. \r\n\r\nShe watched them as they left, a strange sense of wonder flooding her mind and body. Her eyes were still etched with the pyre. Her sacrifice was refused, but perhaps... something different was required of her.",
    "ACOLYTE_PASSIVE_NAME": "N’kuhana's Favor",
    "ACOLYTE_PASSIVE_DESCRIPTION": "The Acolyte <style=cIsHealth>cannot heal</style>. All healing is converted into <style=cIsDamage>attack speed</style>.",
    "ACOLYTE_ALTPASSIVE_NAME": "N’kuhana's Grace",
    "ACOLYTE_ALTPASSIVE_DESCRIPTION": "The Acolyte <style=cIsHealth>cannot heal</style>. All healing and <style=cIsHealth>40% of damage taken</style> is converted into <style=cIsHealing>recoverable health</style> and <style=cIsDamage>attack speed</style>.",
    "KEYWORD_ACOLYTE_RECOVERABLE_HEALTH": "<style=cKeywordName>Recoverable Health</style><style=cSub>A temporary reserve of health that is converted into <style=cIsHealing>healing</style> by <style=cIsDamage>dealing damage</style> with any skill. <style=cIsHealth>Depletes over time</style>.</style>",
    "ACOLYTE_PRIMARY_NAME": "Blade Slice",
    "ACOLYTE_PRIMARY_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsUtility>Rapid</style>. Strike for <style=cIsDamage>150% damage</style>. Activate <style=cIsUtility>Jump</style> or <style=cIsUtility>Sprint</style> while holding primary to <style=cIsDamage>quickstrike</style> for <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style>, up to <style=cIsUtility>3</style> times.",
    "ACOLYTE_QUICKSTRIKE_TOOLTIP": "<style=cKeywordName>Quickstrike</style><style=cSub>Melee attack that interrupts enemies. The number of hits scales with <style=cIsDamage>attack speed</style>.",
    "ACOLYTE_SECONDARY_NAME": "Bola Throw",
    "ACOLYTE_SECONDARY_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsUtility>Agile</style>. <Style=cIsDamage>Stunning</style>. Throw a bola that gathers up to <style=cIsDamage>5</style> enemies for <style=cIsDamage>200% damage</style>, then <style=cIsUtility>Extract</style> their souls towards you.",
    "ACOLYTE_EXTRACTION_TOOLTIP": "<style=cKeywordName>Extraction</style><style=cSub>Separates an enemy's soul with <style=cIsHealth>30%</style> of its health.\r\n<style=cIsDamage>100%</style> of damage dealt to a soul is returned to its body.",
    "ACOLYTE_SECONDARY_ALT_NAME": "Soul Jar",
    "ACOLYTE_SECONDARY_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsUtility>Agile</style>. Throw a jar that deals <style=cIsDamage>150% damage</style> and <style=cIsUtility>haunts</style> enemies. <style=cIsUtility>Haunted</style> enemies take <style=cIsDamage>50% damage per second</style> and release seeking wights on death.",
    "ACOLYTE_UTILITY_NAME": "Blade Sling",
    "ACOLYTE_UTILITY_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsUtility>Agile</style>. <Style=cIsDamage>Stunning</style>. Throw a spinning glaive that deals <style=cIsDamage>200% damage per second</style>. Reactivate to dash to it, dealing <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style>.",
    "ACOLYTE_UTILITY_ALT_NAME": "Javelin",
    "ACOLYTE_UTILITY_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsUtility>Agile</style>. <Style=cIsDamage>Stunning</style>. Throw a piercing glaive for <style=cIsDamage>400% damage</style>. Explodes on large enemies and terrain for <style=cIsDamage>400% damage</style>. Reactivate to dash for <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style>.",
    "ACOLYTE_UTILITY_DASH_NAME": "Blade Dash",
    "ACOLYTE_UTILITY_DASH_DESCRIPTION": "Dash to your blade, dealing <style=cIsDamage>400% damage</style>.",
    "ACOLYTE_SPECIAL_NAME": "Sacrifice",
    "ACOLYTE_SPECIAL_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsUtility>Rapid</style>. Deal <style=cIsDamage>1000% damage</style>, and gain 2 <style=cIsDamage>Convictions</style>. Kills grant an extra Conviction. At <style=cIsDamage>7</style> Convictions, invoke your <style=cIsHealth>Litany</style>.",
    "KEYWORD_LITANY": "<style=cKeywordName>Litany</style><style=cSub>Activate to transform into your <style=cIsHealth>Litany form</style>. During the Litany, all <style=cIsHealth>missing health</style> is converted into <style=cIsHealing>recoverable health</style>.</style>",
    "ACOLYTE_SPECIAL_TRANSFORM_NAME": "Dark Summons",
    "ACOLYTE_SPECIAL_TRANSFORM_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsDamage>Stunning</style>. Transform into the <style=cIsDamage>Anima Harvester</style>. While transformed, convert all <style=cIsHealth>missing health</style> into <style=cIsHealing>recoverable health</style>.",
    "ACOLYTE_SPECIAL_HARVESTER_SUBTITLE": "Those of Death",
    "ACOLYTE_SPECIAL_ALT_TRANSFORM_NAME": "Anima Echo",
    "ACOLYTE_SPECIAL_ALT_TRANSFORM_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsDamage>Stunning</style>. Invoke an <style=cIsDamage>Echo of Acolyte</style>. During the Litany, your melee attacks hit an extra time, and all <style=cIsHealth>missing health</style> is converted into <style=cIsHealing>recoverable health</style>.",
    "LILREAPER_PRIMARY_NAME": "Torrential Slash",
    "LILREAPER_PRIMARY_DESCRIPTION": "Slash forwards, firing a wave of energy for <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style>. Enemies below <style=cIsHealth>25%</style> health are <style=cIsHealth>instantly killed</style>.",
    "LILREAPER_SECONDARY_NAME": "Harrowing Chains",
    "LILREAPER_SECONDARY_DESCRIPTION": "Release up to <style=cIsDamage>5</style> seeking chains for <style=cIsDamage>250% damage</style>. Targets are <style=cIsUtility>pulled</style> towards you, dealing <style=cIsDamage>250% damage</style> on impact.",
    "LILREAPER_UTILITY_NAME": "Soul Storm",
    "LILREAPER_UTILITY_DESCRIPTION": "Unleash a storm of souls, <style=cIsDamage>stunning</style> enemies and dealing <style=cIsDamage>300% damage per second</style>. Reactivate to empower the storm, dealing <style=cIsDamage>1200% damage per second</style>.",
    "LILREAPER_SPECIAL_NAME": "Banish",
    "LILREAPER_SPECIAL_DESCRIPTION": "Banish the <style=cIsDamage>Anima Harvester</style>.",
    "OPTION_TOGGLEACOLYTEINVERT": "<style=cUserSetting>Invert Acolyte Quickstrike Controls</style>",
    "OPTION_TOGGLEACOLYTEINVERT_DESCRIPTION": "Inverts which quickstrikes are activated by the Sprint and Jump buttons during Acolyte's Blade Slice.",
    "OPTION_HIDDEN_SKILL": "Locked",
    "OPTION_HIDDEN_SKILL_DESCRIPTION": "Setting requires skill(s) which are currently locked.",
    "ENFORCER2_BODY_NAME": "Enforcer",
    "ENFORCER2_BODY_SUBTITLE": "Too Angry to Die",
    "ENFORCER2_PASSIVE_NAME": "Big Man",
    "ENFORCER2_PASSIVE_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsUtility>Massive</style>. Enforcer takes <style=cIsUtility>reduced knockback</style>, and <style=cIsDamage>deals 400% damage</style> on high speed impact with the ground.",
    "ENFORCER2_PRIMARY_NAME": "Trenchbroom",
    "ENFORCER2_PRIMARY_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsHealth>Tracer</style>. Fire a slug for <style=cIsDamage>350% damage</style>.\nIn <style=cIsUtility>Defensive Stance</style>, rapidly fire a <style=cIsUtility>piercing</style> shell for <style=cIsDamage>6x70% damage</style>.",
    "ENFORCER2_PRIMARY_KEYWORD_LASTSHOTCRIT": "<style=cKeywordName>Tracer</style><style=cSub>Reloading to max capacity loads the final shot with a guaranteed <style=cIsDamage>Critical Strike</style>.",
    "ENFORCER2_SECONDARY_NAME": "Steel Protection",
    "ENFORCER2_SECONDARY_DESCRIPTION": "Take a <style=cIsUtility>Defensive Stance</style>. Reactivate to exit your shield, <style=cIsDamage>knocking away</style>, <Style=cIsDamage>stunning</style>, and <style=cIsUtility>parrying</style> enemies for <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style>.",
    "ENFORCER2_SECONDARY_KEYWORD_DEFENSIVE_STANCE": "<style=cKeywordName>Defensive Stance</style><style=cSub><style=cIsUtility>Blocks all damage from the front</style>.\nSwaps and refreshes <style=cIsDamage>Primary skill</style>.\n<style=cIsHealth>Reduces movement and replaces jumping</style> with a short <style=cIsUtility>lunge</style>.</style>",
    "ENFORCER2_SECONDARY_KEYWORD_PARRY": "<style=cKeywordName>Parrying</style><style=cSub>While swinging, projectiles and hits taken will be <style=cIsDamage>reflected</style> to enemies with <style=cIsDamage>6x increased damage</style>.",
    "PARRIED_DAMAGE_HITMARKER": "PARRIED!",
    "ABSORBED_DAMAGE_HITMARKER": "ABSORBED!",
    "ENFORCER2_UTILITY_NAME": "Shield Tackle",
    "ENFORCER2_UTILITY_DESCRIPTION": "Charge forwards, knocking enemies back for <style=cIsDamage>600% damage per second</style>. <style=cIsUtility>Hold</style> to consume more charges for <style=cIsUtility>increased distance</style>.",
    "ENFORCER2_SPECIAL_NAME": "Rally Point",
    "ENFORCER2_SPECIAL_DESCRIPTION": "Slam for <style=cIsDamage>400% damage</style>, placing a <style=cIsUtility>Holdout Beacon</style> that grants <style=cIsHealing>Temporary Barrier</style> on kill and <style=cIsUtility>teleports stationary minions</style> to your side.",
    "ENFORCER2_SPECIAL_KEYWORD_BIGMAN": "<style=cKeywordName>Massive</style><style=cSub>Ground impact damage is increased with vertical velocity.</style>",
    "ENFORCER2_SPECIAL_KEYWORD_HOLDOUT": "<style=cKeywordName>Holdout Beacon</style><style=cSub>Mimics a <style=cIsUtility>Teleporter event</style> zone, triggering items that have an effect on these zones.</style>",
    "ENFORCER2_SPECIAL_KEYWORD_BARRIER": "<style=cKeywordName>Temporary Barrier</style><style=cSub>Any kill from allies within the zone grants <style=cIsHealing>10% of Enforcer's max health</style> as <style=cIsHealing>Temporary Barrier</style> to all allies within the zone.",
    "ENFORCER2_PRIMARY_ALT_NAME": "Shrapnel Grenade",
    "ENFORCER2_PRIMARY_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "Fire an arcing grenade for <style=cIsDamage>500% damage</style>.\nIn <style=cIsUtility>Defensive Stance</style>, fire a cluster grenade for <style=cIsDamage>3x300% damage</style>.",
    "ENFORCER2_SECONDARY_ALT_NAME": "Surge Protection",
    "ENFORCER2_SECONDARY_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "Take an <style=cIsUtility>Expanded, Time-Limited, Defensive Stance</style>. On expiration, <style=cIsHealth>expend all extra health</style> into a large explosion for <style=cIsDamage>up to 1800% damage</style>.",
    "ENFORCER2_SECONDARY_ALT_KEYWORD_EXPANDED": "<style=cKeywordName>Expanded, Time-Limited</style><style=cSub>Shield is <style=cIsUtility>wider</style>, and grants <style=cIsHealing>temporary barrier when blocking</style>, but <style=cIsHealth>can only be active for 5 seconds</style>.</style>",
    "ENFORCER2_SECONDARY_ALT_KEYWORD_EXTRA_HEALTH": "<style=cKeywordName>Extra Health</style><style=cSub>All <style=cIsHealing>shield and temporary barrier</style>.</style>",
    "ENFORCER2_UTILITY_ALT_NAME": "Ripcord",
    "ENFORCER2_UTILITY_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "<style=cIsUtility>Launch</style> a remote-detonated grenade. <style=cIsUtility>Retrigger</style> to create a <style=cIsDamage>Pulling Blast</style> for <style=cIsDamage>300% damage</style>, <style=cIsHealth>Taunting</style> enemies.",
    "ENFORCER2_UTILITY_KEYWORD_ENRAGE": "<style=cKeywordName>Taunt</style><style=cSub>Afflicted enemies are forced to walk towards you and have their armor reduced by <style=cIsDamage>10</style>.</style>",
    "ENFORCER2_UTILITY_KEYWORD_BLASTJUMP": "<style=cKeywordName>Pulling Blast</style><style=cSub>Enemies are launched toward the attacker. Repels the user.</style>",
    "ENFORCER2_SPECIAL_ALT_NAME": "Crash Point",
    "ENFORCER2_SPECIAL_ALT_DESCRIPTION": "Leap high into the air, then crash down for <style=cIsDamage>700% damage</style>.",
    "ENFORCER2_DESCRIPTION": "The Enforcer is a bastion of defensive and offensive capabilities using his impenetrable shield and ample firepower.<style=cSub>\r\n\r\n< ! > Trenchbroom is powerful, but ammo-limited. It is refreshed by secondary skills, so managing your skill rotation is crucial to optimizing your firepower.\r\n\r\n< ! > Steel Protection is the ultimate defense, but also boosts primary at short-range. For more reliable Parries, exit shield stance <i>quickly after</i> successfully blocking attacks with the shield.\r\n\r\n< ! > Hold Shield Tackle to plough through and gather groups of enemies, for easy picking with boosted primaries.\r\n\r\n< ! > Use Rally Point in clutch moments to defend and buff your team. The more you work together, the tougher you'll become!\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n",
    "ENFORCER2_BODY_LORE": "Graduated near top of my class. Trained to handle the worst of the worst. Criminals, liars, two-timing mercs, the works. Got into a nice rhythm, cracked down on those gangs and weird cults on Venus. The closer I got, the less I liked of it. Most of them are people on hard times. Not psychopaths.\r\n\rAlmost got a real criminal. Some hotshot, never got any picture of him, but he's managed to get on and off every planet he's ever crimed on. \r\n\rThen I get too close to something. Something dark.\r\n\rI get sent here. Some barren planet filled with the universe's rejects. Giant worms, Giant jellyfish, Giant sentient <i>rocks</i> for God's sake. I can't imagine being stranded here without enough firepower. I'd probably go crazy and start talking to robots.\r\n\rBut now I understand. I found an altar. Several UES, got all kinds of weird symbols on them. Reminds me of some of the stuff I saw back home. \r\n\rDoesn't matter why I got sent or who sent me here. Something's not right, UES might be filled with these nutcases, but I know one thing. Even in this chaotic world, you need someone you can count on.",
    "OPTION_TOGGLE_ENFORCER2_RAGEGAS_HOLD": "<style=cUserSetting>Enforcer Ripcord Hold Input</style>",
    "OPTION_TOGGLE_ENFORCER2_RAGEGAS_HOLD_DESCRIPTION": "Changes Enforcer's Ripcord to explode on releasing input instead of two presses.",
    "OPTION_TOGGLE_ENFORCER2_STEELPROTECTION_HOLD": "<style=cUserSetting>Enforcer Steel Protection Hold Input</style>",
    "OPTION_TOGGLE_ENFORCER2_STEELPROTECTION_HOLD_DESCRIPTION": "Changes Enforcer's Steel Protection to exit shield stance on releasing input instead of two presses.",
    "OPTION_TOGGLE_ENFORCER2_KINETICCHARGE_HOLD": "<style=cUserSetting>Enforcer Surge Protection Hold Input</style>",
    "OPTION_TOGGLE_ENFORCER2_KINETICCHARGE_HOLD_DESCRIPTION": "Changes Enforcer's Surge Protection to exit shield stance on releasing input instead of two presses.",
    "PLAYER_DEATH_QUOTE_MISSEDPARRY": "{0} failed a skill check.",
    "PLAYER_DEATH_QUOTE_MISSEDPARRY_2P": "You should've parried!",
    "PLAYER_DEATH_QUOTE_SACRIFICE": "{0} offered themselves as tribute to N'kuhana.",
    "PLAYER_DEATH_QUOTE_SACRIFICE_2P": "You offered yourself as tribute to N'kuhana.",
    "GAME_RESULT_SACRIFICE_GOOD": "Cherished in N'Kuhana's Embrace",
    "GAME_RESULT_SACRIFICE_BAD": "All for Nothing",
    "FLOWERTURRET_BODY_NAME": "Offshoot",
    "FLOWERTURRET_BODY_SUBTITLE": "Organic Turret",
    "BIGMUSH_BODY_NAME": "Shruum",
    "BIGMUSH_BODY_SUBTITLE": "Fungal King",
    "BIGMUSH_BODY_LORE": "\"Sylah motions the rest of her squad forward, moving to go forward down the cliff-face path. The cavern is massive, filled and made of strange mushrooms that rise and cover the ceiling. Sylah's not sure if the place is more forest than cavern, but the oppressive, almost stone-like arches of mycelium makes that choice for her.\r\n\r\n\"Sylah,\" Orington asks, \"What is that?\"\r\n\r\nSylah looks down the near sheer cliff-face they are standing on. Below are more mushrooms, like everywhere else. Sparkling, cloudy mushrooms that, if breathed in, would send their brains sky high. She almost reprimands him for the chatter, but then she sees them move.\r\n\r\nGiant mushrooms, easily the size of a two story building, slowly rising and falling as they make their way across the ground. As she tracks them, she realizes many of the mushrooms across the cavern are actually moving as well. Her eyes are drawn to... something. A line of them? Slowly forming a spiral around a central point?\r\n\r\nMovement to her back surprises her, and she realizes Orington is right beside her. She shoots him a cutting glance, but his obvious excitement makes him oblivious. \r\n\r\n\"They are a community of living mushrooms! Maybe something like a siphonophore? Connecting to do something bigger?\"\r\n\r\nAt Sylah's continued stare, Orington continues, \"A siphonophore is-\"\r\n\r\n\"I know what a siphonophore is, Orington, but that isn't something to be excited about. If they are working together, that means the survivor we're tracking is probably-\"\r\n\r\nA strange hum like the deepest fan suddenly overpowers what she's saying, and they both whip their heads towards the spiral.\r\n\r\nA massive funnel of spores rises from the center, slowly spinning upwards towards the ceiling. The fungal spores blot out what light is left coming from the ceiling, but that makes the next moments even more noticeable. The mushrooms making up the walls sparkle even brighter, their bright spots almost swimming as they shimmer with intensity, intensifying as the spores fill up the ceiling. \r\n\r\nOrington and Sylah start and begin scrambling back up the way they came, Sylah yelling orders over the radio. It isn't until they notice the shadows growing darker around them that they realize the giant mushrooms can jump.",
    "PLANTED_MUSH_NAME": "Mushling",
    "LYNXAMBUSHER_BODY_NAME": "Lynx Assassin",
    "LYNXAMBUSHER_BODY_LORE": "Several commandos enter into the swamp. Strange flashes of heat lightning brew overhead in billowing clouds. \r\n\r\n\"Bertram, looks like we lost it.\"\r\n\r\n\"You are mistaken. It's somewhere around here. In the shadows. Waiting.\"\r\n\r\nThe other commando starts looking around, then back at Bertram. \"How could you even know that?\"\r\n\r\n\"I can feel it, Kellan. A true hunter does not stop in the face of adversity - it finds another way.\"\r\n\r\n\"Well, Liam and I- Wait, where's-\"\r\n\r\nKellan is suddenly pulled by his feet, landing squarely on his face. His helmet cracks and he yells. He gets pulled quickly, too quickly in the muddy swamp, away into the darkness. As he gets pulled, he flips and begins shooting at the shadows, yelling until his audio suddenly cuts off after a loud crack.\r\n\r\nBertram fires after Kellan but stops after the audio cuts off. Bertram looks on ahead to see a small structure made of ancient stones. Stairs covered in moss and moisture come out each side. He nods, pulling out a submachine gun while holding a light machine gun in his other hand.\r\n\r\n\"If you want me, you crazy killer, you know where to find-\"\r\n\r\nAs soon as he steps towards the structure, movement to his left and right alarm him. He begins shooting, thrusting his submachine gun to the left, but the light machine gun was too heavy.\r\n\r\nBertram's curses echoed and then yells of pain and insults as not one, but two Lynx take his arms, then drag him to the stony structure.",
    "LYNX2_BODY_NAME": "Lynx Berserker",
    "LYNX2_BODY_LORE": "Weird hard-skins here. Making noise. Big booms. Nasty, nasty smells and tastes.\r\n\rMove weird. Some are tall. Some small. Some different.\r\n\rThere is one. It freezes. It sees me, powerful warrior.\r\n\rWe stare. I am big, strong. It knows to fear me. I will devour when I am ready.\r\n\rIt moves. I kill.",
    "LYNXARCHER_BODY_NAME": "Lynx Deadeye",
    "LYNXARCHER_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>$ Transcribing image... done.\n$ Resolving... done.\n$ Outputting text strings... done.\nComplete!</style>\n\nThis is the logbook entry of D. Furthen, naturalist for the UES [Redacted] in conjunction with the UES Research and Documentation of Outer Life. I am joined by my good friend Tharson, who is keeping me safe through this journey.\n\n---------------------\n\nFor the past few nights, Tharson and I have been robbed of our rations right from under our noses! Tharson was finally able to catch the perpetrators last night, though was unable to bring them to justice, and received a wooden arrow to his shoulder as a reward for his efforts. Tharson is OK from this encounter, though we have decided it is in our best interest to move camp before another ambush occurs.\n\nWe have dubbed this group the \"Lynx Tribe\" due to their cat-like appearances and hunting tactics; their properties are as follows:\n\n* Short, bipedal creatures resembling humanoid cats. Each member wears a unique mask which fully encompasses their head. Removing the mask from a terminated specimen reveals bug-like appendages around the face.\n\n* Highly intelligent, seemingly coordinating ambush strategy with spoken language. Those that did not attack with their razor-sharp claws instead used hand-crafted spears and bows. We suspect that large totems found in neighboring areas may function as ambush points, or are otherwise significant to them.\n\n* Suspected to be capable of incredible mobility, hiding effectively by climbing up in trees or burrowing in dirt and lying in wait for prey. Tharson insists that many \"came from nowhere\" when he was attacked. \n\n* Tharson and I have been steering clear of their constructions and gauging the density of local fauna to judge safety as we pursue a new location for camp; there appears to be correlation, though we are unsure if this is because the Lynx Tribe exploits the local populations, or if the local populations can sense their territories.",
    "MINILYNX_BODY_NAME": "Lynx Pup",
    "MINILYNX_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>Welcome to Datascraper (v3.1.53 – beta branch)\n\n\n$ Scraping memory... done. \n\n$ Resolving... done. \n\n$ Combing for relevant data... done. \n\nComplete!</style>\n\nDay 1\n\nRecording this for anyone who finds themselves in the swamp. Do NOT grab any pages you find. I repeat, do NOT. \n\nSomeone told me that finding pages would be good for me. Fortune teller kind of thing, and I tell you, she is a liar, fake, the works. Ever since I picked this thing up, I can't get rid of it. I hear strange things, but the worst part–\n\nThey're here!\n\nDay 2\n\nOk. I lost them. Took nearly the whole day, and I finally found a place to rest. The point is this page, it doesn't even make sense. It says... Weshan? And–\n\nOh no.\n\nDay 3\n\nThey have me pinned down. dozens of these creatures, they're like the cats you see going for crazy money back home and– well. They are hold my arms and digging their claws into me. If I do anything other than slightly speak, they dig more.\n\nThe only thing I've found that helps is by reading these words, and they are starting to make sense. Everything back home was... too much? Crowded? But whenever I read they relax and I am so tired...\n\nDay 4\n\nI woke up with most of them still on me. I think they are young? They like the reading, and well... I'm starting to like them. They brought me food, and as long as I keep reading... I think I'll stay alive.",
    "LYNXTOTEM_BODY_NAME": "Lynx Totem",
    "LYNXTOTEM_BODY_SUBTITLE": "N'kuhana's Faithful",
    "LYNXTOTEM_BODY_LORE": "Young cubs. Quick to cut, gut. Too close to the meat to see the claws.\r\n\r\nOld ones. We and the stones are the same. Endless, tasteless. But strong, strong.\r\n\r\nLet them play. Scratch their face. Lose themselves in hunt, the relentless hunt.\r\n\r\nThey will find their stones, match their face. They will see the mother of guts and games.\r\n\r\nThen we dash, play, cut, gut, eat, rip. Our games for her to see. Her gift, blood, sweeten our stones.\r\n\r\nAnd we all, be endless, with our stones.",
    "TOTEMCRYSTAL_BODY_NAME": "Lynxite Spire",
    "FAMILY_LYNX": "<style=cWorldEvent>[WARNING] Something malicious is brewing..</style>",
    "MIMIC_BODY_NAME": "Mimic",
    "MIMIC_BODY_LORE": "<style=cMono>> Automated report 44fbb488e8d8847 is now available from site record 0493921a9539eef.\r\n > Please refer to record 59asfd84106fbd8676 for additional details during your review.\r\n > Report Type: Machine-generated Transcription> base Vernacular Profile “Brian”\r\n > - Source: 57fee8a8g7sd7g7790fg (Blackbox Recording recovered from cadaver)\r\n > Priority: Low\r\n > Report Content:\r\n\r\n -- Beginning of Excerpt Flagged for Review -- </style>\r\n\r\nHey, did that chest just move?\r\n\r\n<style=cMono> -- End of Recording -- \r\n\r\n -- End of Excerpt Flagged for Review -- \r\n\r\n > Please refer to report 44fbb488e8d8847 for full audio excerpt. ==============================================================</style>",
    "REAPER_BODY_NAME": "Anima Harvester",
    "REAPER_BODY_SUBTITLE": "Avatar of N'kuhana",
    "REAPER_BODY_LORE": "Rejoice, O Simple Vessels!\r\nThis is My Mercy.\r\n\r\nTo Harvest that Anima which abides within all things living,\r\nTo Return Balance to the scales askew,\r\nTo Shatter not all Vessels with My Presence True,\r\nTo Embrace the Worthy and Take them Home,\r\nI appear unto you in this form.\r\n\r\nThis is My Mercy.\r\nDo not take it lightly.",
