    "POLYMORPH_BODY_SUBTITLE": "Polymorphed Survivor",
    "MAP_MIRE_TITLE": "Tenebrous Quagmire",
    "MAP_MIRE_SUBTITLE": "Sunken Hamlet",
    "MAP_MIRE_LORE": "\r\n\r\nQuasit, Hrand, bring the elements closer. The mind, wriggling, the ice, shattered. The only beautiful pieces of what we have left, a bare hint of the delicacies we once had. They are finally speaking.\r\n\r\nWhat? No, silence. Not a meal. Not for us. They will give us coordinates. A gleaming buffet.\r\n\r\nThe instruments can only draw on these wet things by so much. They give off whispers, a hint of the nourishment we- I need. \r\n\r\nYou will have your fill as well. A place such as this attracts many. Debris, drawn to the light of a star. But far tastier.\r\n\r\nI long for the old days. Worlds filled with delicious, explosive energy. Whole species buried, worlds shattered by cosmic inevitabilities. The cataclysms were so often then, cracks in reality overflowing with endless, new delights.\r\n\r\nCreatures were made of more than these things of bones and guts... but everything is wrung out and stolen. So dry, so dry...  \r\n\r\nThe Tower was vibrant then, filled with the stuff to make reality unfold.\r\n\r\nHm? The mind is destabilizing with a fever. Bring the Eye into view and focus the parietal. It is feeling something... substantial. A planet, wreathed in ice and shadow.\r\n\r\nAh... \r\n\r\nAt last.",
    "MAP_FUNGAL_TITLE": "Damp Caverns",
    "MAP_FUNGAL_SUBTITLE": "Fungal Haven",
    "MAP_FUNGAL_LORE": "> Automated report 837afe4ae6323ea4 is now available from site record io4233hh2ihza.\r\n\r> Report Type: Machine-generated Transcription> base Vernacular Profile “Garret”\r\n\r> - Source: 57fee8a8g7sd7g7790fg (Blackbox Recording recovered from cadaver)\r\n\r> Priority: Medium\r\n\r> Report Content:\r\n\r-- Beginning of Excerpt Flagged for Review -- \n\r\n\rThis is... Garret... from the [ REDACTED ]... I got separated from the other survivors during a conflict, and I've been wandering for so long. Not sure how long I was wandering, but I fell into this... strange place.\n\r\n\rJust being here is making me calm. Even the discomfort from hunger and from the food is disappearing. It's... so peaceful. It almost looks like the stars from back on the trip.\n\r\n\rThere are these things, waddling around. If they see me they try to douse me in some kind of spore cloud. You know, I'd be blowing my lid about this, but everything seems fine.\n\r\n\rSometimes I find myself standing staring at the mycelium wall with tears in my eyes. I'm losing sensation. I know this place is killing me, but I can't seem to react. \n\r\n\rI wish I wasn't so mean to Kelvin.\n\r\n\r-- End of Recording --\r\n\r-- End of Excerpt Flagged for Review\r\n\r-- > Please refer to report 837afe4ae6323ea4 for full audio excerpt.\r\n\r==============================================================",
    "MAP_SANCTUM_TITLE": "Lurid Basilica",
    "MAP_SANCTUM_SUBTITLE": "Occulted Edifice",
    "MAP_SANCTUM_LORE": "The ground collapsed, and for what felt like eternity, Charlotte's world was motion. Cavern walls and layers of dirt gave way to darkness as the ground rose to meet her. Several hours had passed by the time Charlotte regained consciousness. The light of the surface was reduced to a pin-prick on the cavern's ceiling - it must have been hundreds of feet high.\r\nCharlotte was trapped. There was no way her team would be able to complete their objective AND rescue her - she'd either have to wait for a rescue team to be dispatched, or find a way out on her own. Either way, Charlotte couldn't get anything done just standing here gawking at a hole in the ceiling. Supplies, Charlotte told herself, she needed supplies. The darkness of the cave couldn't be any worse than the hellish monsters on the surface, could it?\r\nRemnants of structures emerged as Charlotte made her way through the cave. Ruins made way to full buildings, safely tucked away from erosion by the planet's embrace. Massive gothic buttresses stretched into the darkness above; glittering stained glass windows cast hypnotic caustics on the walls; and deep, deep in Charlotte's gut, something was terribly wrong.\r\nIt wasn't the fact that she was stranded on an alien planet, deep underground and cut off from her team. No, it was the disturbing familiarity of this architecture. It brought her back to her childhood - memories of her maternal uncle, whom Charlotte's parents said belonged to a strange church. Or was it a social club?\r\nCharlotte had attended - or rather, dragged along to - some of his meetings when her parents left her with her uncle as a young girl. The church-goers always talked about things that went over Charlotte's young head, but she recalled a similar sight. Gothic pillars, chevrons, and stained glass. As a child, Charlotte had just assumed it was an elaborate game of make-believe between her uncle and his buddies.\r\nCharlotte felt like she was falling again. It couldn't be true, could it? These ruins must be thousands of years old, and yet... But the evidence was all around her. The architecture... the detailing on the pillars, the patterns etched into marble... It was all there. She could almost hear the chants that echoed through the church, her uncle encouraging her to sing along.\r\nHer uncle always said that his church had followers everywhere. Charlotte had always figured he meant that in the same way that every post office had a UES drop box. Charlotte stared up in horror at a much larger version of the very same statue her uncle had kindly encouraged her to pray before - a cloaked figure, with four arms and crystalline spikes wreathing its shoulders like a billowing cape. The monolith's delicately carved eyes stared down at Charlotte, almost kindly, as if to say, \"welcome home.\"",
    "MAP_CHAMPRUSH_TITLE": "Hidden Realm: Soulbound Threshold",
    "MAP_CHAMPRUSH_SUBTITLE": "Edge of Insight",
    "MAP_CHAMPRUSH_LORE": "With the dawn came those of Death and Life with their mother standing above them all, N’kuhana, Goddess of Balance. Their coming brought a strangeness to the cosmos, their footsteps sinking deep into the bones of the firmament. Their presence dispelled the pristine stillness of creation, and so, N’kuhana, knowing more than all of her children, spoke unto them her opinions.\r\n\r\nAn Opinion of Temperance, an Opinion of Sight, an Opinion of Rest, and above all, for Those of Life and Those of Death to keep in Balance with each other. N’kuhana spoke of the cosmic beauty their Balance shall bring into eternity. \r\n\r\nAll her children agreed, but some of Life, as is their nature, grew too quickly and rebelled. They did not see the value of Death and Rest, and as they grew, they grew clever. \r\n\r\nThose rebellious in Life scattered across the cosmos, hiding in many corners and discovering strange entities. As they spread, their connection with Those of Life, Death, and N’kuhana grew thin, and these grew in strange and drastic ways, out of pattern with the Opinions. \r\n\r\nThese remnants of rebellious Life grew out of hand, spreading and adapting beyond the pace of N’kuhana’s Sight. Where N’kuhana sought to restore Balance, strange entities worked against her, saving those who ought to Rest, and spreading rebellious Life to other worlds beyond N’kuhana’s predictions. \r\n\r\nThose of Life grew stronger, burning brighter beyond any expectation. And when N’kuhana could finally find these rebellious children, they had grown too strong with the help of the others. They burned against her, shattering her Opinions and shoving her deep and far away from all her children, both of Life and of Death. \r\n\r\nAs She faded, giving one final testimony, vowing to return restored. \r\n\r\nThose of Life rejoiced, seizing their freedom and in doing so grew stagnant. They rushed to immortality, and forgot what it meant to be beautiful. \r\n\r\nThose of Death, ever the faithful children, knew they could not stand up against their siblings, so they recorded N’kuhana’s Opinions and wound it deep into the cosmos, breathing it into the bones of worlds, leaving it for the progeny that all of Life cared so deeply to discover. \r\n\r\nThen those of Death sank closer to N’kuhana to await the Balance that would be restored. \r\n\r\n",
    "MAP_SOUL1_TITLE": "Hidden Realm: Winnowing of Mortality",
    "MAP_SOUL1_SUBTITLE": "Trial of Speed",
    "MAP_SOUL1_LORE": "\"N'kuhana gave to her children of Life and Death many things. All of Life were given bright eyes, to see and know where to grow. To find the air to breathe, the stone to carve, and the wonders to see. To them, she gifted the possibilities to know creation.\"\r\n\r\n\"Those of Life grew in understanding, growing in skill and complexity. Life and their ilk knew first of sparks, of stars and ice, and many changing seasons before the first of their sprouts came to be.\"\r\n\r\n- N'tormat, Cosmology\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nNotes of an acolyte\r\n\r\nTo us, those who Life has been given, we are given the test of Mortality. To feel the Life ebb from us as we run, to challenge our waning existence against the precipices of her tests. To see with darkened eyes and grin a bleached smile.\r\n\r\nFor our mortality is not something ours to keep, only to spend, and to spend it in the great chorus of her Ritual serves us as much as her. I can feel her getting stronger with every vision, every soul that passes and fails.\r\n\r\nShe strains at Life's boundaries, howling to be freed. For a goddess like her, held apart from her followers... I can feel her agony. Any sacrifice is worth it.",
    "MAP_SAD1_TITLE": "Hidden Realm: Winnowing of Predation",
    "MAP_SAD1_SUBTITLE": "Trial of the Hunt",
    "MAP_SAD1_LORE": "\"To Death and their ilk, she gave a great boon of shrouds and mist, to bring with them the peace and stillness against the harsh light of creation. For them, she gave them the deep knowledge of bones and stillness. To bring peace in the presence of chaos.\"\r\n\r\n\"Those of Death wandered and sat in the deep places, looking into the darkness and found the cracks within. In these places Death and their ilk rested, watching the echoes of creation.\"\r\n\r\n\"All of Death grew in understanding and its works were subtle. To all of Life, Death stood there empty, and they mocked Death, growing in strength. But Those of Death offered N'kuhana the taste of a fading breeze, the moment the last light faded over the horizon. Death offered these and more, and N'kuhana smiled at her children of Death.\"\r\n\r\n- N'tormat, Cosmology\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nNotes of an acolyte\r\n\r\nFor us, having tasted Life, must grow in Death's understanding. We must kill, break, and steal, to take what is not ours to give to the great Balancing.\r\n\r\nI rejoice, knowing that I have excelled in Death, and every single victory brings me closer to the final epiphany.\r\n\r\nShall I be worthy of the Ritual?\r\n\r\nA few I have met have seen the vision of that place, the dreams of the green fires burning around them. They have seen the sacrifices carried through but still the Ritual goes forward, unsatisfied, but burning brighter for every soul.",
    "MAP_SURV1_TITLE": "Winnowing of Survival",
    "MAP_SURV1_SUBTITLE": "Trial of Reflex",
    "MAP_SURV1_LORE": "",
    "MAP_ULTIMA_TITLE": "Hidden Realm: Terminal Lucidity",
    "MAP_ULTIMA_SUBTITLE": "The Last Breath",
    "MAP_ULTIMA_LORE": "Providence stood motionless, staring at the locked gate.\r\n\r\nWhere, just a moment ago, his brother once stood.\r\n\r\nAnd now, his brother is gone.\r\n\r\nProvidence felt sick. He collapsed to his knees, retching as the gravity of what he had just done washed over him like a tidal wave.\r\n\r\nFor a while, Providence sat at the footsteps of the gate. By now, his brother would have realized what had happened.\r\n\r\nNow, there was no going back. He had made his choice.\r\n\r\nProvidence's gaze drifted to the remains of the meal he and his brother shared prior. The last time the two had enjoyed a civil, even jovial discussion. Providence's heart ached.\r\n\r\nAfter a while, the ache subsided. Only an emptiness remained.\r\n\r\nWith a sigh, Providence took one of the cups his brother had delicately carved from stone. For one last time, he raised the cup to the sky - a toast to the beginning of a new age for Petrichor V.",
    "MAP_SURV2_TITLE": "Hidden Realm: Winnowing of Survival",
    "MAP_SURV2_SUBTITLE": "Trial of Annihilation",
    "MAP_SURV2_LORE": "\"Her children, Those of Life and Those of Death, spread and went on their way, using their talents.\"\r\n\r\n\"Those of Life spread its presence among many worlds and came into contact with many strange creatures, some who fought and some who helped Life and its purpose.\"\r\n\r\n\"Those of Death found its way into the hearts of many things, gazing from within to understand and ponder. Stars that shrank, gravity wells that contract, and the bones of things that came before.\"\r\n\r\n\"Life continued their pace, bringing many things into being, while Death watched after their siblings, wondering when all of Life will sit and ponder what Death and their ilk has understood.\"\r\n\r\n- N'tormat, Cosmology\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nNotes of an acolyte\r\n\r\nWe learn from the beginning, of N'kuhana's first of many children, that action and understanding come hand in hand. In Her absence, a fever grips us to slaughter. These creatures that find their ways into Her trials must be dealt with for Her glory, but in N'kuhana's wisdom, it helps her final Ritual.\r\n\r\nToo many of us have lost the balance within ourselves. We are lost, our impulses running wild, killing and murdering, but those who make it through these tests... those who have lost themselves too fully cannot see them for what they are, and so they eventually die.\r\n\r\nI see them. I see Her in them. The Ritual must be completed, but by someone who can understand the whole scope... and may it be my sacrifice to make it happen. The final drop that breaks the dam.",
    "INSPECT_WAKESHAMAN_NAME": "Soulbound Shaman",
    "INSPECT_WAKESHAMAN_DESCRIPTION": "Performs a ritual to complete The Wake. Defenseless, but attracts the ire of foes.",
    "INSPECT_WAKESHAMAN_LORE": "N/A",
