    "BAZAAR_SEER_SANCTUM": "<style=cWorldEvent>You dream of great vaulted halls.</style>",
    "BAZAAR_SEER_FUNGAL": "<style=cWorldEvent>You dream of a vast underground cavern.</style>",
    "BAZAAR_SEER_MIRE": "<style=cWorldEvent>You dream of a mire.</style>",
    "OBJECTIVE_HOLLOWING": "She's watching...",
    "OBJECTIVE_HOLLOWING_FULL": "She beckons!",
    "PROVIDENCE_BODY_NAME": "Echo of Providence",
    "PROVIDENCE_BODY_SUBTITLE": "Fading Memory",
    "PROVIDENCE_BODY_LORE": "A shift in the balance of power. I can feel it, even from my empty rock.\r\n\r\nThose creatures, from the planet of water and earth... The ones you had your eye on.\r\n\r\nI have to admit, their vessel is impressive, even after you blew it to pieces. Don't think I didn't notice.\r\n\r\nNo matter how many of them you try to remove, I have eyes and ears everywhere, brother. I see the devastation those vermin wreak on your so called \"paradise.\"\r\n\r\nDid I not tell you this would happen? That when left to their own devices, all that vermin know is to destroy? They were never like us.\r\n\r\nThough, I'm curious, brother... How does it feel? The ones you believed held so much potential, ripping your life's work from you?\r\n\r\nIt's almost poetic. Bravo! Not even I could design a better conclusion to the fantasy you've trapped yourself in.",
    "PROVIDENCE_BODY_SUBTITLE_2": "Fallen Bulwark",
    "PROVIDENCE_BODY_SUBTITLE_3": "Dying Wish",
    "PROVIDENCE_SHADOW_BODY_NAME": "Echoing Umbra",
    "GILDEDWURM_BODY_NAME": "Corroded Wurms",
    "GILDEDWURM_BODY_SUBTITLE": "Faithful to the Grave",
    "GILDEDWURM_BODY_LORE": "Who am I?\r\n\r\nI am stretched, refined to a point. I feel an echo of her voice, prodding me along. To become her shadow, her might, her blade.\r\n\r\nI become POWER. Endless souls fall before me as I exact her will. Her voice grows, deafening, close to her moment to strike down the boundary. \r\n\r\nShe desires balance and the inability to achieve it so urges her on. She misses them, those who are in Life.\r\n\r\nI challenge the strongest of her acolytes. Those whose souls are strong enough to weigh the boundary and join her, strengthening her.\r\n\r\nTheir souls weaken those who Live, and spreading her influence wherever her children Death draws their shadows.\r\n\r\nBut then... as her will spread, as balance took hold... the voices I silenced joined me, and I heard beyond her voice, something quiet speaking.\r\n\r\nMemories from a million souls swirl, cacophony joining her voice, but with each sacrifice, the experiences and lives left behind...\r\n\r\nThe cherished memories and the deepest regrets have left an imprint on my being. The slaughter continues, but that quiet voice weighs on me.\r\n\r\nMy form responds. It changes as I listen to that voice, its words showing the beauty of Life.\r\n\r\nWho is this? Whose face is this? A single eye stares back at me, wielding a crystalline blade.\r\n\r\nThis planet... I feel an urge to protect it. It is precious somehow. Necessary. What does this voice ask of me? To safeguard life, rather than snuff it out?\r\n\r\nFor the first time, I can't hear her voice. A moment to ask if her will has grown beyond her means to control.\r\n\r\nBut I am her blade, and a blade does as it is made to do.",
